\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  expected to lay off dozens of staffers in coming week \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 408 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 January 2025\par 14:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Cuts will be deep\u8217\'20\'19, media reporter writes, after paper faced scrutiny for halting endorsement of Harris in October\par \par \uc2 Dozens of employees are expected to be laid off at the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  in the coming week in what is another of several tumultuous episodes in recent months for the storied title, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.status.news/p/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by the media reporter Oliver Darcy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe layoffs are slated to hit the \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  -owned \u8230\'20\'26 newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s business division, I\u8217\'20\'19m told. One person familiar with the matter said that the cuts will be deep, impacting many dozens of employees,\u8221\'20\'1D Darcy, the former CNN reporter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.status.news/p/washington-post-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in his newsletter Status.\par \par \uc2 Darcy also reported that the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reporter Josh Dawsey is leaving the publication and is expected to join the Wall Street Journal. The Post, whose publisher is the UK-born \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  , did not immediately comment to Darcy on the expected layoffs.\par \par \uc2 The cuts come as the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has faced scrutiny from within its own ranks following the publication\u8217\'20\'19s decision in October to halt a planned endorsement of the Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  , which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2024/10/28/post-editorial-board-resignations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended}}}\uc2  by the billionaire owner, \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 More than 250,000 subscriptions to the Post were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/29/washington-post-subscriber-cancellations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cancelled}}}\uc2  in protest of the decision. Two opinion writers and an editor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/10/28/2024/more-editorial-board-members-resign-at-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  in response to the intervention, which came shortly before the Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  defeated Harris, won a second presidency and is set to be sworn back in to the White House on 20 January.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Pulitzer prize-winning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2025/jan/04/washington-post-cartoonist-resigns-jeff-bezos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 editorial cartoonist Ann Telnaes resigned}}}\uc2  in response to the newspaper refusing to publish a satirical cartoon depicting Bezos.\par \par \uc2 In December, two political correspondents at the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  , Ashley Parker and Michael Scherer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/press-releases/archive/2024/12/ashley-parker-and-michael-scherer-join-atlantic/681190/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left}}}\uc2  for the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 And in September 2024, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2024/09/23/washington-post-layoffs-arc-xp-tech-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off}}}\uc2  54 employees in its tech software division, a year after the publication {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/10/10/1204939842/the-washington-post-will-cut-240-jobs-through-voluntary-buyouts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut}}}\uc2  240 jobs through voluntary buyouts.\par \par \uc2 Darcy\u8217\'20\'19s scoop on the upcoming newspaper layoffs at the Post came as the Bezos-founded \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s streaming service Prime announced an upcoming documentary on the former and incoming first lady Melania Trump. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in December also announced plans to donate $1m to help fund the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s second inauguration \u8211\'20\'13 and said that it would also stream the event on its Prime Video service, a separate in-kind donation worth another $1m.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250106el160020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
