\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Forget talk of defending workers, the US visa feud is about the market\u8217\'20\'19s needs\b0\par\par\uc2 Kenan Malik \par \uc2 1,151 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2025\par 18:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2025.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Whether in America or Britain, working-class people only matter when immigration is an issue\par \par \uc2 On the one side stand Silicon Valley moguls and leaders of corporate America; on the other, longstanding \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loyalists and supporters of the Maga (\u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D) movement. One side claims to be building America\u8217\'20\'19s bright new future by recruiting the best talent from across the globe, the other to be defending US workers from the depredations of global capitalism. One side portrays itself as challenging racism and bigotry, the other is outraged by bigoted views of American culture.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscis.gov/working-in-the-united-states/h-1b-specialty-occupations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 H-1B visa}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which allows US companies to hire foreign workers with \u8220\'20\'1Chighly specialised knowledge\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 might seem an unlikely spark for a mini civil war among Trump supporters. Yet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/27/trump-elon-musk-sriram-krishnan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the bitter feud}}}\uc2  that has gripped the Trumpsphere over the past week has exposed many of the fissures of US conservatism. There is little to admire on either side and much to deplore. Both sides are right in certain respects, but usually for desperately wrong reasons.\par \par \uc2 The fallout began when Laura Loomer, a far-right activist with the ear of the incoming president, described as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LauraLoomer/status/1871262423950520454"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply disturbing\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  the appointment by Trump of Sriram Krishnan, an Indian-born US venture capitalist, as policy adviser on AI. She was alarmed by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe number of career leftists \u8230\'20\'26 appointed to serve in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s admin\u8221\'20\'1D whose views \u8220\'20\'1Care in direct opposition to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s America first agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Then \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  published a long post blaming \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican culture\u8221\'20\'1D for the need to import foreign engineers. A former presidential rival turned Trump supporter, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to run, with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the proposed Department of Government Efficiency, Ramaswamy claimed that \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican culture has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/VivekGRamaswamy/status/1872312139945234507"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 venerated mediocrity over excellence for way too long}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CA culture that celebrates the prom queen over the maths olympiad champ, or the jock over the valedictorian,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not produce the best engineers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The post inevitably enraged Maga loyalists and anti-immigration activists, from one-time Trump confidant \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  to former governor of South Carolina \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 . While many simply pushed back at the deprecation of American culture and the claim that US workers possess insufficient skills, there was also considerable {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/smashbaals/status/1872708368537952743"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outpouring of racist bile}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk waded in both to defend the H-1B scheme, of which he has long been a fervent advocate, and to demand that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1872797210066436560"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Chateful, unrepentant racists\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1872744295884841262"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cremoved from the Republican party\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Trump himself, who in 2016 described the programme as being \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very bad for workers\u8221\'20\'1D and one that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businesstoday.in/latest/world/story/h-1b-visas-skilled-foreign-workers-should-end-unfair-to-american-jobs-donald-trump-58398-2016-03-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI frankly use and\u8230\'20\'26 shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed to\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , and who four years ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/22/us/politics/trump-h1b-work-visas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily suspended the scheme}}}\uc2 , last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/12/28/us-news/donald-trump-backs-h-1b-visa-program-supported-by-elon-musk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed his new Silicon Valley friends against their Maga critics}}}\uc2 . Policy walks to where money talks.\par \par \uc2 Drawing a line between \u8216\'20\'18immigrants we hate\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18immigrants we like\u8217\'20\'19 is a fool\u8217\'20\'19s errand when you\u8217\'20\'19ve made all immigrants fair game for bigotry\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a bit rich, though, for the likes of Musk and Ramaswamy to cry racism about those objecting to their favoured visa scheme when they themselves have been so fervidly disseminating racist tropes about immigrants. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1833180704869626035"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Musk helped promote}}}\uc2  the notorious claim that Haitian immigrants to Springfield, Ohio, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/15/trumps-fantasy-that-migrants-are-eating-cats-proves-the-meme-has-prevailed-over-real-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ceating pets\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . He and Ramaswamy have been advocates of the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat replacement theory\u8221\'20\'1D, the belief that the elites are \u8220\'20\'1Cimporting\u8221\'20\'1D millions of illegal immigrants to replace white people. Ramaswamy called it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/therecount/status/1732585595958919467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca basic statement of the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s platform\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , while Musk claimed it was part of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 attempt to create {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1770030227390914624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csingle party rule\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Last month, Musk backed the far-right AfD as the only party that can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1869986946031988780?lang=en-GB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csave Germany\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Having unleashed the racist hounds, to claim now that the pack is pursuing the wrong hares carries little credibility. Trying to draw a line between \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigrants we hate\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cimmigrants we like\u8221\'20\'1D becomes a fool\u8217\'20\'19s errand when you\u8217\'20\'19ve nurtured conspiracy theories that make all immigrants fair game for bigotry.\par \par \uc2 The argument of Maga supporters that their opposition to H-1B rests on a desire to defend American workers is, in most cases, equally fallacious. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unherd.com/2024/12/the-maga-battle-over-foreign-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 There is certainly evidence}}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/tech-and-outsourcing-companies-continue-to-exploit-the-h-1b-visa-program-at-a-time-of-mass-layoffs-the-top-30-h-1b-employers-hired-34000-new-h-1b-workers-in-2022-and-laid-off-at-least-85000-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 employers manipulate the visa system}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insider.govtech.com/california/news/jury-finds-discrimination-in-h-1b-visa-tech-worker-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discriminate against local workers}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/27/trump-elon-musk-sriram-krishnan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 help keep wages low}}}\uc2 . Many describe the visa programme as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SohrabAhmari/status/1872365368637075851"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cindentured servitude\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  because any worker complaining about pay or conditions can have their visa rescinded by their employer and be deported.\par \par \uc2 Hostility towards such abuse should be directed against not immigrants but the employers who exploit both US and foreign workers. I have previously observed about Britain that rightwing critics of immigration portraying themselves as champions of British workers rarely support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/aug/18/defending-working-class-interests-requires-more-than-simply-opposing-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working class interests in other spheres}}}\uc2 . Most want to strip down trade union rights, support labour market \u8220\'20\'1Cflexibility\u8221\'20\'1D, are hostile to strikes and nurture intolerance towards benefit claimants.\par \par \uc2 The same is true of the American debate. While there are good reasons to oppose the exploitation of H-1Bs by big business, most critics are more concerned with creating hostility to immigration than with defending workers. If they truly wanted to champion working-class interests, they would call for the expansion of union rights, proper socialised healthcare, a progressive taxation system, sanctions against price gouging, and so on. Few on either side of the Trumpsphere split are willing to do so. Workers get championed, it seems, primarily when there are immigrants to deprecate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can fawn over \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  or you can run a populist political campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newstatesman.com/comment/2024/08/trump-will-have-to-choose-populism-or-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 But you can\u8217\'20\'19t do both.}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D So wrote the American conservative Sohrab Ahmari three months before the US election. He pointed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decision to frame Democrat candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cas a \u8216\'20\'18communist\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D rather than as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newstatesman.com/cover-story/2024/08/donald-trump-identity-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Can Obama-style neoliberal Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  as revealing the shallowness of his populist argument.\par \par \uc2 While he is perceptive about tensions within the Trumpsphere, Ahmari\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion that Trump could solve his dilemma by leaning \u8220\'20\'1Cin hard into a pro-labour, anti-corporate stance\u8221\'20\'1D is less convincing. Certainly, there are strands of conservatism sympathetic to working-class needs. But any \u8220\'20\'1Canti-corporate stance\u8221\'20\'1D is always limited, shackled by conservative conceptions of social order and the championing of the profit motive. Class politics for conservatives means the working class knowing its place within the social and economic order.\par \par \uc2 The H-1B debate does not pit the elite against the working class but rather is a tussle between two sections of the elite with different strategies for US capitalism, a debate in which the working class becomes merely a commodity to be exploited, before being discarded when no longer needed. This is true not just of America, but of similar debates in Britain and Europe over immigration, the working class and political realignment. On both sides of the Atlantic what is too often missing is the organised voice of labour.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Kenan Malik is an Observer columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020250108el15002ku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
