\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Party City shutters after nearly 40 years, firing workers without severance pay\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 313 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par 21:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company went into bankruptcy in January 2023 under $1.7bn in debt, but remaining $800m too much to overcome\par \par \uc2 The party is over at Party City, once the largest supplier of balloons and other fun-time supplies in the US, as the company announced Friday it was closing down all of its stores, ending nearly 40 years in business.\par \par \uc2 Barry Litwin\uc2 , the Party City CEO, told employees that the chain was \u8220\'20\'1Cwinding down\u8221\'20\'1D operations immediately and that today would be their last day of employment.\par \par \uc2 Staff were told they would not receive severance pay, and they were told their benefits would end as the company goes out of business, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/12/20/business/party-city-shut-down?Date=20241220&Profile=cnnbrk&utm_content=1734716189&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Litwin said the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cvery best efforts have not been enough to overcome\u8221\'20\'1D its financial challenges that had included inflation that had contributed to higher costs and dragged on consumer spending.\par \par \uc2 The abrupt end comes just four months after Litwin was appointed CEO of the New Jersey-based company. Party City went into bankruptcy in January 2023 under $1.7bn in debt.\par \par \uc2 The bankruptcy cleared nearly $1bn in debt and managed to keep most of around 800 stores open. But the remaining $800m in debt proved too much to overcome. All corporate employees were sent home earlier this month. Staff were reportedly caught off-guard by the move.\par \par \uc2 On the call with staff Friday, Litwin reportedly apologized for the lack of communication, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe recognize the flow of communication has not been how we typically handle sensitive matters like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like many brick-and-mortar chains, Party City was unable to adapt to the rise of e-commerce sites and pop-up concepts such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/business/2022/10/26/markets-now-halloween-spirit-popular-costumes-zw-orig.cnn-business"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spirit Halloween}}}\uc2 , CNN said. It also had to deal with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/27/global-helium-shortage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helium shortage}}}\uc2 , a critical component of the party balloon business.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241220ekck002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
