\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: US \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers go on their \u8216\'20\'18largest\u8217\'20\'19 strike amid holiday rush\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,256 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par 12:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at seven facilities including in New York, Atlanta and San Francisco take action. Plus, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  sinks congressional spending bill\par \par \uc2 Good morning \u8211\'20\'13 and happy holidays! This is the last First Thing of 2024. We will be back on 2 January.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday morning, workers at seven \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities across the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/19/amazon-workers-strike-union-teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike}}}\uc2  early during the holiday shopping rush, aiming to pressure the retailer into union contract talks.\par \par \uc2 Warehouse workers in cities \u8211\'20\'13 including New York, Atlanta and San Francisco \u8211\'20\'13 are taking part in the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest\u8221\'20\'1D strike at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , said the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , which represents about 10,000 workers at 10 of the firm\u8217\'20\'19s facilities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf your package is delayed during the holidays, you can blame \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insatiable greed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, the union\u8217\'20\'19s general president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are the details of the dispute? The union had given \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a 15 December deadline to begin negotiations and warehouse workers had recently voted to authorize a strike. \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  says \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfails to pay its workers enough to make ends meet\u8221\'20\'1D and has \u8220\'20\'1Cpushed workers to the limit\u8221\'20\'1D, despite \u8220\'20\'1Cobscene profits\u8221\'20\'1D. The company reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/31/amazon-quarterly-earnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 above-expected revenue growth}}}\uc2  in the third quarter, with revenue of $158.9bn, 11% higher than the same period in 2023.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How disruptive will the strike be? \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said it did not expect any effect on its operations during one of the busiest times of the year. Analysts said the company was unlikely to come to the table to bargain as that could open the door to more union actions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why? Unions represent only about 1% of the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workforce, with the company \u8211\'20\'13 one of America\u8217\'20\'19s largest by market cap \u8211\'20\'13 accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/03/amazon-union-warehouse-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-union practices}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was founded by \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , whose personal wealth Forbes estimates to be $239bn.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  showcases grip on Washington by impeding bipartisan spending bill\par \par \uc2 Using the power of the social media platform he owns and the threat of spending millions against Republicans in primaries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/19/elon-musk-trump-government-shutdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk helped tank a bipartisan congressional spending bill}}}\uc2  that would have kept the government running.\par \par \uc2 After their initial failure at Musk\u8217\'20\'19s hands, House Republicans on Thursday scrambled to put together another deal. But the pared-down spending bill failed to pass the House of Representatives in a vote on Thursday evening, in a humiliating setback for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/19/bernie-sanders-elon-musk-funding-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked}}}\uc2  the exercise of unelected power from Musk, who is worth about $40bn, according to Forbes estimates. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats and Republicans spent months negotiating a bipartisan agreement to fund our government,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe richest man on Earth, President \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like it. Will Republicans kiss the ring?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the debt ceiling? Congress is in charge of setting the debt limit, which currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/19/what-is-the-debt-ceiling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stands at $31.4tn}}}\uc2 . This limits the amount of money the government can borrow to pay for services such as social security, Medicare and the military. The debt ceiling has been raised 78 times since 1960, under both Democrat and Republican presidents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happens now? Without action from Congress, a government shutdown looms, starting tomorrow at 12.01am.\par \par \uc2 Inside Aleppo: the Guardian visits the city Assad left to rot for the first time in ten years\par \par \uc2 Aleppo, a cosmopolitan and ancient merchant city on the silk road between the Mediterranean port of Antioch, now Antakya in Turkey, and the Euphrates, which flows to the Gulf, has survived calamity and catastrophe in its 8,000-year history: earthquakes, plagues and millennia of wars between Arab, Turkic, Persian and Christian kingdoms.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/20/inside-aleppo-the-city-assad-left-to-rot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a decade on from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s last visit}}}\uc2 , during the four-year-long battle for Aleppo between the regime of Bashar al-Assad and rebel forces, it is clear that Syria\u8217\'20\'19s vicious civil war has ripped it apart, tearing at the social fabric and wreaking physical destruction that cannot easily be mended.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The brutal toll of\par \par \uc2 Assad\u8217\'20\'19s war: at least 30,000 people were killed in Aleppo, hundreds of thousands more lives ruined and centuries\u8217\'20\'19 human heritage destroyed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The\par \par \uc2 conditions in Aleppo today: entire neighborhoods in the east and south of the city are still rubble, their residents long gone. The destruction was left as a silent reminder of the price to be paid for opposing the regime. Bodies buried under the mounds of rebar and concrete have never been retrieved.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  has said Russia is ready for a missile \u8216\'20\'18duel\u8217\'20\'19 with the US, in his end-of-year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/19/putin-claims-ukraine-war-has-made-russia-much-stronger-phone-in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press conference}}}\uc2 . He also said in hindsight he would have invaded Ukraine earlier than 2022.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 35 children have died and six others were seriously injured in a crowd crush in\par \par \uc2 Ibadan\par \par \uc2 , Nigeria. A homicide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/19/at-least-35-children-killed-in-crowd-crush-at-school-fair-in-nigeria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  had been opened.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Luigi Mangione, the suspect in the killing of UnitedHealthcare\u8217\'20\'19s CEO \uc2 Brian Thompson\uc2 , has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/19/luigi-mangione-unitedhealthcare-extradition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  in Manhattan federal court on four counts, including murder, stalking and firearms offenses.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mediators have pushed on with Gaza ceasefire talks in Egypt and Qatar, amid continued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/dec/20/middle-east-crisis-live-gaza-ceasefire-talks-fresh-strikes?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-6764ce448f08c3692f1e0bfc#block-6764ce448f08c3692f1e0bfc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 airstrikes from Israel}}}\uc2  on the devastated Palestinian territory \u8211\'20\'13 which killed 44 people on Thursday, Gaza health officials said.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: 55 people died crossing Dari\u233\'00\'E9n Gap this year trying to reach the US, Panama says\par \par \uc2 Fifty-five people trying to reach the US have died and 180 children have been abandoned this year while crossing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/dec/19/darien-gap-deaths-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 treacherous Dari\u233\'00\'E9n jungle}}}\uc2  from Colombia, according to Panama\u8217\'20\'19s president, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Ra\u250\'00\'FAl Mulino. Panamanian authorities suspect the total death toll is higher. Non-profits say a lack of limited legal pathways to the US helps drive people to take the deadly Dari\u233\'00\'E9n route.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The most striking photojournalism images of the year\par \par \uc2 Guardian\uc2  and Observer picture editors highlight the work of photojournalists \u8211\'20\'13 often working in treacherous conditions \u8211\'20\'13 who captured the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/2024/dec/20/from-gaza-to-ghana-celebrating-the-agency-photographers-of-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking moments of 2024}}}\uc2 , from airstrikes in Gaza to the fall of the Assad regime in Syria to the floods of Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: Clairo on making one of 2024\u8217\'20\'19s best albums\par \par \uc2 Clairo\u8217\'20\'19s third album, Charm, pairs Claire Cottrill\u8217\'20\'19s distinctive voice with vintage soul. \uc2 Guardian\uc2  critics voted it the fourth-best album of the year. \u8220\'20\'1CCharm is kind-of the dust settling, picking up the pieces, feeling a little more grown-up and refined,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/dec/19/clairo-on-making-one-of-2024-best-albums-charm-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the artist tells the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Elle Hunt}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Blob-headed fish and amphibious mouse among 27 new species found in \u8216\'20\'18thrilling\u8217\'20\'19 Peru expedition\par \par \uc2 Researchers in the Alto Mayo region of north-west Peru have discovered 27 species that are new to science, including a rare amphibious mouse, a tree-climbing salamander and an unusual {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/dec/20/blob-headed-fish-and-amphibious-mouse-among-27-new-species-found-in-thrilling-peru-expedition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cblob-headed fish\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe function of this \u8216\'20\'18blob\u8217\'20\'19 remains a complete mystery,\u8221\'20\'1D one scientist said.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ve been eating the same batch of my mother\u8217\'20\'19s frozen mince pies for 20 years\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Richard Newson\u8217\'20\'19s mother was known for her delicious homemade mince pies. When she died in 2003, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/dec/20/experience-ive-been-eating-the-same-batch-of-mince-pies-for-20-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found a container of pies}}}\uc2  in the freezer. \u8220\'20\'1CFor the past 20 years, I have been slowly making my way through them by eating one on 1 December every year,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CEach pie fills me with joy and nostalgia, as I reminisce about past Christmases.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wishing you a great festive period. See you in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241220ekck001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
