\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Why are \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers on strike \u8211\'20\'13 and what does it mean for Christmas deliveries?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 837 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2024\par 19:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amazon Labor Union \u8211\'20\'13 comprising 10,000 workers across the US \u8211\'20\'13 is striking over the company\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to negotiate\par \par \uc2 With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/christmas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christmas}}}\uc2  less than a week away, thousands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  warehouse workers across the countries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/19/amazon-workers-strike-union-teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are on strike}}}\uc2  after the company refused to start contract negotiations with the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Though it\u8217\'20\'19s been well over two years since the first \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse union was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/09/amazon-union-organization-staten-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formed in New York City}}}\uc2 , and workers at several other warehouses across the country have started to unionize, the company has refused to recognize and negotiate a contract with the union.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  gave \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a 15 December deadline to come to the bargaining table, which the company refused to acknowledge.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what you need to know about the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse strike.\par \par \uc2 Which \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are striking?\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employs more than 1.5 million people around the world. The Amazon Labor Union (ALU) has gained about 10,000 workers across 10 facilities in the US over the last two years. In June, the ALU voted to affiliate with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , which has 1.3 million union members across the country.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said that seven of the 10 facilities with unions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/teamsters-launch-largest-strike-against-amazon-in-american-history/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on strike}}}\uc2 . The warehouses include one in the borough of Queens in New York, one in Atlanta, three in southern California, one in San Francisco and a seventh in a Chicago suburb. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said that Amazon Teamsters at other facilities \u8220\'20\'1Care prepared to join them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The union says the strike is the largest against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in the company\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 How will the strike affect deliveries?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how the strike will affect operations. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has hundreds of thousands of employees still working at delivery hubs and facilities that aren\u8217\'20\'19t unionized.\par \par \uc2 The company said it does not anticipate the strike affecting its operations heading into Christmas.\par \par \uc2 But the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Teamsters/status/1869546520812408910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Thursday morning that if \uc2 Amazon\uc2  customers have package delays, \u8220\'20\'1Cyou can blame \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insatiable greed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe gave \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a clear deadline to come to the table and do right by our members. They ignored it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese greedy executives had every chance to show decency and respect for the people who make their obscene profits possible. Instead, they\u8217\'20\'19ve pushed workers to the limit and now they\u8217\'20\'19re paying the price. The strike is on them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said its local unions will also put up picket lines at hundreds of other non-unionized \uc2 Amazon\uc2  fulfillment centers across the country.\par \par \uc2 How long will the strike last?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  has not specified how long the strike will last, meaning it could go on past Christmas and into the new year.\par \par \uc2 Why are \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers striking?\par \par \uc2 Though thousands of its employees have voted to unionize, the company has staunchly opposed efforts to increase union membership and has refused to recognize some employees as \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 The union wants \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to negotiate a contract with its members, who are demanding better wages, job security and benefits.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers and delivery drivers have long reported conditions that can be taxing on workers. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-releases-sweeping-report-exposing-how-amazons-obsession-with-speed-injures-workers-at-unprecedented-rates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  committee, led by the Democratic senator Bernie Sanders, released this week accused \uc2 Amazon\uc2  of putting workers under heavy quotas that risk their safety. The committee said that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses recorded 30% more injuries at its warehouses over the industry average. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has said that the report is \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally flawed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Why won\u8217\'20\'19t \uc2 Amazon\uc2  negotiate with the union?\par \par \uc2 Some Amazon Teamster members are delivery drivers who work for third-party companies, called \u8220\'20\'1Cdelivery service partners\u8221\'20\'1D, who drive vans with \uc2 Amazon\uc2  logos but are technically not employed by the company.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, two regional directors with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) issued initial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/10/business/economy/amazon-delivery-drivers-labor-nlrb.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaints}}}\uc2  that said \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is technically a joint employer of the drivers, even if they are hired by third parties. The hearing over an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  complaint in southern California is scheduled for March.\par \par \uc2 In September, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  filed its own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/amazon-nlrb-50ee06d87d4eaef22386382761335ef8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaint}}}\uc2  challenging the structure of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , arguing that it is unconstitutional because board members cannot be removed by the president. Though the company, along with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , which filed a similar suit, argued in front of a panel of judges from the US court of appeals for the fifth circuit in November, the court has yet to issue a ruling.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all to say that \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resistance to recognizing the union is still tied up in court, and the company maintains that many of the unionized members are not its employees and that the union harasses and intimidates employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor more than a year now, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have continued to intentionally mislead the public \u8211\'20\'13 claiming that they represent \u8216\'20\'18thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees and drivers\u8217\'20\'19. They don\u8217\'20\'19t, and this is another attempt to push a false narrative,\u8221\'20\'1D an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241219ekcj002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
