\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers go on \u8216\'20\'18largest\u8217\'20\'19 strike against company, \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  says\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato and wires \par \uc2 572 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2024\par 18:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at seven facilities including New York, Atlanta and San Francisco take action in demand of contract talksWhy are \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers on strike \u8211\'20\'13 and what does it mean for Christmas deliveries?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  workers at seven US facilities walked off the job early on Thursday during the holiday shopping rush, aiming to pressure the retailer into contract talks with their union.\par \par \uc2 Warehouse workers in cities including New York, Atlanta and San Francisco are taking part in the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest\u8221\'20\'1D strike against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , said the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , which represents about 10,000 workers at 10 of the firm\u8217\'20\'19s facilities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re doing is historic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Leah Pensler, a warehouse worker at DCK6 in San Francisco in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/teamsters-launch-largest-strike-against-amazon-in-american-history/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release }}}\uc2  announcing the strike. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting against a vicious union-busting campaign, and we are going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  locals are also starting picket lines at hundreds of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  sites around the US in support of the strike, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said, and argued \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers and delivery drivers have the legal right to honor those picket lines.\par \par \uc2 The company, however, said it does not expect any effect on its operations during one of the busiest times of the year.\par \par \uc2 Unions represent only about 1% of the workforce of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , one of the largest companies in the US by market value, and it has multiple locations in several metro areas.\par \par \uc2 The union had given {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/dec/16/amazon-workers-strike-new-york-atlanta-chicago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon a 15 December deadline}}}\uc2  to begin negotiations and warehouse workers had recently voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/dec/17/amazon-worker-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorize a strike}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf your package is delayed during the holidays, you can blame \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s insatiable greed,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 general president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, said late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe gave \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a clear deadline to come to the table and do right by our members. They ignored it. This strike is on them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The retailer\u8217\'20\'19s shares were trading 1.5% higher in premarket hours, a sign that investors do not expect a big disruption from the strike.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have \u8220\'20\'1Cintentionally misled the public\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthreatened, intimidated and attempted to coerce\u8221\'20\'1D employees and third-party drivers to join them, an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Observers said \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was unlikely to come to the table to bargain as that could open the door to more union actions. The corporation employs more than 1.5 million people globally and has said it prefers direct relationships with workers.\par \par \uc2 Still, the company has responded to recent organization efforts with legal challenges. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has filed objections with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/13/amazon-labor-nlrb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Labor Relations Board}}}\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) over a 2022 union vote in Staten Island, alleging bias among agency officials.\par \par \uc2 In August 2024, the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrbedge.com/p/08302024-board-rejects-amazons-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected }}}\uc2  those objections but \uc2 Amazon\uc2  won a temporary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/government/amazon-wins-temporary-pause-nlrb-case-over-nyc-union-election-2024-10-01/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pause}}}\uc2  in October on the board issuing a bargaining order pending \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appeals.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2024/10/amazon-illegally-refused-to-bargain-with-drivers-union-nlrb-alleges/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  issued }}}\uc2  complaints involving \uc2 Amazon\uc2  refusing to bargain with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  as a joint employer of delivery drivers in California and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc3340.com/news/local/alabama-jefferson-county-bessemer-amazon-facility-labor-laws-union-rwdsu-unfair-labor-practices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered }}}\uc2  another rerun union election at an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Bessemer, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also challenged the constitutionality of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  in a September federal lawsuit. Earlier this year, the company announced a $2.1bn investment to raise pay for fulfillment and transportation employees in the US, increasing base wages for employees by at least $1.50 to around $22 per hour, a roughly 7% increase.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed to this story.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241219ekcj0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip