\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Threat of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers\u8217\'20\'19 strike spreads during peak holiday season\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2024\par 21:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Threats started in New York and spread to Chicago and Atlanta after company failed to meet negotiation deadline\par \par \uc2 Thousands of workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  are threatening to strike at the company after giving the company a deadline of 15 December to agree to begin negotiating a first contract with the union representing employees.\par \par \uc2 The strike threats, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/13/amazon-new-york-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started in New York}}}\uc2 , have now spread to Chicago and Atlanta. They come during \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s peak holiday season and after the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://press.aboutamazon.com/2024/12/amazons-record-breaking-black-friday-week-and-cyber-monday-deal-event-was-its-biggest-thanksgiving-holiday-shopping-event-ever"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced}}}\uc2  record sales during its 2024 Black Friday and Cyber Monday events.\par \par \uc2 The workers at the company\u8217\'20\'19s JFK8 warehouse in Staten Island became the first \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 win a union election}}}\uc2  in March 2022. But the company has yet to begin negotiating a first contract with Amazon Labor Union (ALU-IBT Local 1). Workers are pushing for improvements to pay, safety and job security.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers at another New York City site, the delivery station DBK4 in Queens, also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/amazon-teamsters-vote-to-authorize-strike-at-two-major-nyc-warehouses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  to strike in solidarity with the contract fight and their push for union recognition from the company.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/amazon-teamsters-vote-to-authorize-strike-at-two-major-nyc-warehouses/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing}}}\uc2  workers at 10 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities around the US in California, Illinois, Georgia and New York.\par \par \uc2 Workers at two \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities near Atlanta, Georgia, and a delivery facility in Skokie, Illinois, outside of Chicago, also voted to authorize strikes and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atlantanewsfirst.com/2024/12/16/amazon-delivery-drivers-atlanta-could-strike-ahead-holidays/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked out}}}\uc2  on strike along with New York City workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDriving for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is tough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Luc Rene, a worker at DBK4, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s even tougher is fighting a mega-corporation that constantly breaks the law and games the system. But we won\u8217\'20\'19t give up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike comes in the wake of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  health, education, labor and pensions (Help) committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-releases-sweeping-report-exposing-how-amazons-obsession-with-speed-injures-workers-at-unprecedented-rates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  released on 16 December into high injury rates at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . According to the report senior \uc2 Amazon\uc2  executives rejected internal recommendations that would have relaxed productivity quotas because of concerns about how it would impact the company\u8217\'20\'19s performance.\par \par \uc2 The report also backed up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thesoc.org/health-and-safety-at-amazon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union-sponsored research}}}\uc2  that claimed injury rates at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  were far higher than those of its peers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s beyond unacceptable that \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the 2nd largest corporation in America, owned by \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , the 2nd wealthiest person on Earth, continues to put their huge profits ahead of the health & safety of their workers,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator Bernie Sanders, the Help committee chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenSanders/status/1868708608701292720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X.}}}\par \par \uc2 Amazon{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/policy-news-views/amazon-response-to-senator-bernie-sanders-report-on-workplace-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disputed}}}\uc2  the report\u8217\'20\'19s findings, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally flawed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241216ekcg003h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
