\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 UK firms slash jobs after budget, but US economy booms; \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  takeover gets government clearance \u8211\'20\'13 business live\b0\par\par\uc2 Graeme Wearden \par \uc2 6,279 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2024\par 15:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UK staffing levels fall and government clears EP Group\u8217\'20\'19s takeover of Royal MailCanal+ listing is \u8216\'20\'18vote of confidence\u8217\'20\'19 in UK stock market, says ReevesRevealed: the business dealings of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  bidder \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing post\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The sale of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company to the Czech billionaire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/daniel-kretinsky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD}}}\uc2  has been approved by the \uc2 UK government\uc2  after a review under national security laws.\par \par \uc2 The \u163\'00\'A33.6bn takeover of \uc2 International Distribution Services\uc2  (IDS) \u8211\'20\'13 the owner of the 508-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/royal-mail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Royal Mail}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 by Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\u8217\'20\'19s EP Group was confirmed on Monday morning.\par \par \uc2 It will be the first time \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  has been controlled by an overseas owner in its history, which can be traced as far back as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/shortcuts/2013/apr/28/royal-mail-privatisation-where-thatcher-feared-tread"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1516 under Henry VIII}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government will retain a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden share\u8221\'20\'1D in IDS, which means any changes to \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ownership, tax residency or headquarters will need its assent. The \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  brand will also be protected for as long as EP owns the company.\par \par \uc2 EP has also reached agreement with the \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unions, having offered guarantees on job security, and the corporate governance of the company.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-daniel-kretinsky-uk-ids"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Royal Mail takeover by Czech billionaire Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD approved}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-675ff3568f08ed05bce5de8b#block-675ff3568f08ed05bce5de8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Britain\u8217\'20\'19s private-sector firms are cutting jobs at the fastest pace since the Covid-19 pandemic}}}\uc2 , as they reacts to the tax rises in October\u8217\'20\'19s budget.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-676007428f08ed05bce5df71#block-676007428f08ed05bce5df71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Footfall at UK shops has slowed in the last fortnight}}}\uc2 , suggesting a poor Christmas in on the cards for shops.\par \par \uc2 But the picture is brighter in the US, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-676046548f0809492d273bea#block-676046548f0809492d273bea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 private sector growth is running at a 33-month high}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Canada\u8217\'20\'19s finance minister \uc2 Chrystia Freeland{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with%3Ablock-67603a528f08b3a58e462897#block-67603a528f08b3a58e462897"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has resigned}}}\uc2 , in an apparent policy clash with prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  over how to response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shares in French broadcaster Canal+ have dropped by 20% after making its market debut in London this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US private sector growth fastest since Covid-19 reopening\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s economy is ending the year much stronger than the UK, it seems.\par \par \uc2 Data firm S&P Global reports that US private sector output growth is running at a 33-month high in December, amid a service sector surge.\par \par \uc2 Its Flash US PMI composite output index has jumped to 56.6 this month, up from November\u8217\'20\'19s 54.9, which shows the fastest expansion since the reopening of the economy from COVID lockdowns in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The latest poll of purchasing managers also found that expectations of output in the coming year have hit a two-and-a-half year high, reflecting growing optimism about business conditions under the incoming Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Employment also edged higher, up for the first time in five months, as firms expanded workforce numbers amid the brighter outlook.\par \par \uc2 Encouragingly for US central bankers, firms also reported that inflationary pressures cooled again this month, with the average prices charged for goods and services rising at the slowest rate since June 2020.\par \par \uc2 But while the service sector appears to be booming, manufacturers are report falling output and higher prices.\par \par \uc2 Chris Williamson, chief business economist at S&P Global Market Intelligence, explains:\par \par \uc2 The service sector expansion is helping drive overall growth in the economy to its fastest for nearly three years, consistent with GDP rising at an annualized rate of just over 3% in December.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a different picture in manufacturing, however, where output is falling sharply and at an increased rate, in part due to weak export demand.\par \par \uc2 Encouragingly, confidence in the 12-month outlook has lifted to a two-and-a-half year high, suggesting the robust economic upturn will persist into the new year and could also become more broad-based by sector. However, some of the high spirits seen after the election in the manufacturing sector have been checked over concerns surrounding tariffs and the potential impact on inflation resulting from the higher cost of imported materials. December saw raw material prices spike sharply higher amid supplier-led price rises and higher shipping costs,\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US stock market has opened slightly higher, as investors await the final interest rate decision of the year on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 index of US stocks has risen by 0.2%, while the narrower Dow Jones Industrial Average is down less than 4 points, or 0.0088%, at 43,824 in early trading.\par \par \uc2 Tech stocks are picking up, lifting the Nasdaq Composite by 0.4% or 78 points to 20,005 points.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Canada's finance minister resigns after policy clash\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a shake-up in the \uc2 Canadian government\uc2  today, where finance minister \uc2 Chrystia Freeland\uc2  has resigned.\par \par \uc2 In a letter posted on X, Freeland reveals that prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  had asked her to relinquish the post for another cabinet position.\par \par \uc2 Writing to Trudeau, she says the pair have been \u8220\'20\'1Cat odds over the best path forward for Canada,\u8221\'20\'1D explaining:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Friday, you told me you no longer want me to serve as your Finance Minister and offered me another position in the Cabinet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUpon reflection, I have concluded that the only honest and viable path is for me to resign from the Cabinet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Freeland, a former \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  and Reuters journalist, goes on to argue that Canada must push back against \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica First economic nationalism\u8221\'20\'1D being pushed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 frltrSee my letter to the Prime Minister below // Veuillez trouver ma lettre au Premier ministre ci-dessous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NMMMcXUh7A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NMMMcXUh7A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Chrystia Freeland\uc2  (@cafreeland) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cafreeland/status/1868659332285702167?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After a boom in November, conditions in the New York state private sector have cooled this month.\par \par \uc2 The Empire State Manufacturing Survey, released a few minute ago, shows that business activity held steady in New York State in December.\par \par \uc2 After rising sharply last month, the headline general business conditions index retreated thirty-one points to 0.2.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe New York Fed Empire State Manufacturing Survey\u8217\'20\'19s General Business Conditions index snapped back to a flat reading at 0.2 in December, down from 31.2 in November and below expectations of a decline to 6.4. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/manufacturing?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #manufacturing}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PMI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PMI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iX1w9MGxe4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iX1w9MGxe4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MTS Insights (@MTSInsights) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MTSInsights/status/1868653989107282004?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NY Fed\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 New orders and shipments increased modestly. Delivery times shortened somewhat, and supply availability was little changed. Inventories increased at a substantial clip. Labor market indicators pointed to small decline in employment and a slightly shorter average workweek. Both input and selling price increases moderated. Firms remained optimistic about the six-month outlook, though somewhat less so than in November.\par \par \uc2 enltr??BREAKING:\par \par \uc2 *\uc2 NY FED\uc2  DECEMBER EMPIRE STATE MANUFACTURING INDEX PLUNGES TO +0.2; EST. +6.4; PREV. +31.2\par \par \uc2 ???????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/33eQcwvAQ9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/33eQcwvAQ9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Investing.com (@Investingcom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Investingcom/status/1868651972062261469?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 PureTech\uc2  publishes positive results from lung disease trial\par \par \uc2 The UK biotech \uc2 PureTech Health\uc2  has published positive clinical trial results for its lung fibrosis drug, sending its FTSE 250-listed shares up by more than 6%.\par \par \uc2 Idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis (IPF) affects more than 230,000 patients in the US and Europe, and there have been no new therapies approved in the past decade. IPF has a median survival time of two to five years. More deadly than many cancers, IPF is a progressive disease where over time, scar tissue spreads throughout the lungs and makes the absorption of oxygen increasingly hard.\par \par \uc2 Over a six-month intermediate (phase 2) trial, patients on \uc2 PureTech\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s drug deupirfenidone experienced a decline in lung function that was similar to what is expected in healthy older adults over the same time frame, suggesting that deupirfenidone has the potential to stabilise the lung function decline that is the hallmark of IPF, the company said. It added that no other study has shown this at six months. The drug was generally well tolerated.\par \par \uc2 While there are other treatments, antifibrotics, that are effective, their use is limited by tolerability concerns that contribute to nearly three quarters of people with IPF in the US foregoing treatment.\par \par \uc2 Chief executive \uc2 Bharatt Chowrira\uc2  said that if \uc2 PureTech\uc2  could repeat the results in a phase 3 trial, it would \u8220\'20\'1Crepresent a step change in the treatment of IPF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 PureTech\uc2  has replaced hydrogen atoms in the pirfenidone (one of the approved therapies for IPF - made by Roche) structure with three heavy hydrogen atoms. This changes how the drug is broken down in the body, and makes it easier to tolerate, it explained.\par \par \uc2 The Boston-based firm is known for its spinoff companies, including \uc2 Karuna Therapeutics\uc2 , which was bought by US drugmaker \uc2 Bristol Myers Squibb\uc2  a year ago, and \uc2 Vedanta Biosciences\uc2 . Deupirfenidone is \uc2 PureTech\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s only internal drug programme.\par \par \uc2 PureTech\uc2  was co-founded by the American entrepreneur \uc2 Daphne Zohar\uc2  in 2005 and floated on the London stock exchange in June 2015. It is also listed on the Nasdaq. Zohar left in April to lead Seaport Therapeutics, another \uc2 PureTech\uc2  spinoff company.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s Office for Budget Responsibility (OBR)\uc2  has been commissioned for an Economic and Fiscal Forecast which will be published on 26 March 2025.\par \par \uc2 This is in line with the Budget Responsibility and National Audit Act 2011 which requires the \uc2 OBR\uc2  to produce two forecasts each financial year. This will be accompanied by a statement to Parliament from the Chancellor, the Treasury has announced.\par \par \uc2 They add:\par \par \uc2 The Chancellor remains committed to one major fiscal event a year to give families and businesses stability and certainty on upcoming tax and spending changes and, in turn, to support the government\u8217\'20\'19s growth mission.\par \par \uc2 That suggests it will be more of a \u8216\'20\'18spring statement\u8217\'20\'19 than a full-blown budget (following the one at the end of October).\par \par \uc2 enltr?? UK TO PUBLISH LATEST OBR ECONOMIC AND FISCAL FORECASTS ON 26 MARCH - GOVT STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 **UK FINANCE MINISTER REMAINS COMMITTED TO ONE MAJOR FISCAL EVENT A YEAR\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 PiQ (@PiQSuite) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PiQSuite/status/1868644288630030633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 French broadcaster Canal+ is having a rather bruising start to life on the London stock markets.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Canal+ have fallen by over 20% since trading began. Having started trading at 290p at 8am, they\u8217\'20\'19ve now fallen to 227p, a drop of 22%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/dec/15/canal-listing-vote-confidence-uk-stock-market-reeves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canal+ listing is \u8216\'20\'18vote of confidence\u8217\'20\'19 in UK stock market, says Reeves}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s UK PMI report reinforces fears that growth risks are to the downside and inflation risks are to the upside as we head into 2025.\par \par \uc2 So warns Daniel Mahoney, UK economist at Handelsbanken, who says:\par \par \uc2 There now seems to be growing evidence that firms are responding to the increase in employer\u8217\'20\'19s NI and other measures around employment with a reduction in hiring, and it is notable that this is something that we have been hearing anecdotally from a range of clients. Moreover, the \uc2 PMI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s price pressure indicators appear to be indicating that inflation could be turning higher.\par \par \uc2 This backdrop leaves the [\uc2 Bank of England\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s] MPC with a difficult set of trade-offs, with the rate cutting cycle likely to continue at a very cautious pace. Our central view remains that rate cuts will only happen at a pace of just one 0.25pp reduction per quarter through 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 The drop in staffing levels at UK companies this month, and the fall in business optimism, suggest the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  should cut interest rates at its meeting this week.\par \par \uc2 So argues Professor Costas Milas of the \uc2 University of Liverpool\uc2 , who tells us:\par \par \uc2 The latest surveys ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?page=with:block-675ff3568f08ed05bce5de8b#block-675ff3568f08ed05bce5de8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 you reported on today}}}\uc2  ) suggest, or at least hint, that we are \u8220\'20\'1Csleepwalking\u8221\'20\'1D towards a recession. Whether this turns out to be true (or not), the \uc2 BoE\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s MPC has a unique opportunity to take action this week by cutting interest rates. Many worry that inflation will rise based on data to be released this week. Such a rise should only be temporary.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=4987701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new work of mine}}}\uc2  (co-authored with Dr Papapanagiotou) on the out-of-sample forecasting performance of UK inflation, we find that both Divisia M4 growth and global supply pressures forecast future inflation (up to four quarters ahead) better than almost every other variable you can think of. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/boeapps/database/fromshowcolumns.asp?Travel=NIxAZxSUx&FromSeries=1&ToSeries=50&DAT=RNG&FD=1&FM=Jan&FY=1999&TD=31&TM=Dec&TY=2025&FNY=Y&CSVF=TT&html.x=66&html.y=26&SeriesCodes=LPMB6F5&UsingCodes=Y&Filter=N&title=LPMB6F5&VPD=Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Divisia M4 growth}}}\uc2  is extremely weak (just above 0% and, indeed, at historical lows) whereas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorkfed.org/research/policy/gscpi#/interactive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 global supply pressures}}}\uc2  are also extremely weak.\par \par \uc2 A great chance for the MPC to surprise positively this week rather than waiting for February 2025 when, perhaps, it will have left it too late!\par \par \uc2 A cut on Thursday would indeed be a surprise, though. The money markets are indicating there\u8217\'20\'19s an 84% chance of no change in UK interest rates this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 UK retail footfall drops in blow to shops\par \par \uc2 UK retailers are facing the prospect of \u8216\'20\'18bleak\u8217\'20\'19 Christmas trading, after a drop in visits to the high street, retail parks and shopping centres in the last fortnight.\par \par \uc2 Footfall at retailers over the last two weeks has averaged -3.1% below the same weeks last year according to new data from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rendleintelligenceandinsights.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rendle Intelligence and Insights}}}\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s a blow, as Christmas trading in 2023 was not great either.\par \par \uc2 Diane Wehrle, CEO of Rendle Intelligence and Insights, explains:\par \par \uc2 The subsequent two weeks trading since Black Friday seems to have been lacklustre at best. Experience has shown that trading plateaus in the week or so following Black Friday, however, a week on week drop in footfall into stores of -9.1% followed by a rise of only +7.5% is exceptionally disappointing.\par \par \uc2 Particularly as it means that footfall over the last two weeks has averaged -3.1% below the same weeks last year, which was recognised as a pretty disastrous Christmas trading period. Moreover, footfall into stores last week dropped further behind 2023 than the week before (-3.3% last week vs -2.8%) the week before last.\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But\u8230\'20\'26 with Christmas falling on a Wednesday there is a full week and then two additional days left to capture consumer spend.\par \par \uc2 Wehrle says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe might yet see a Super Saturday on 21st December!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 enltrUK companies cut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/jobs?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #jobs}}}\uc2  at the fastest rate in nearly 4 years in December amid slowing demand and rising employment costs. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/UK?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #UK}}}\uc2  Flash {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PMI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PMI}}}\uc2  remains at 50.5 (Nov: 50.5).\par \par \uc2 Find out more: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uP2dtyRDcB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uP2dtyRDcB}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/economy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #economy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/services?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #services}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/manufacturing?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #manufacturing}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lX54uY0cJs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lX54uY0cJs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 S&P Global PMI\u8482\'21\'22 (@SPGlobalPMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SPGlobalPMI/status/1868604513327722914?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Unite\uc2  general secretary Sharon Graham is also backing the \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  agreement\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis agreement opens the door to a better future for \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  and its workforce.\par \par \uc2 It is now vital that EP and the government continue to work closely with Unite CMA and the \uc2 CWU\uc2  to ensure that \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  delivers positive outcomes for its staff and its customers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 PMI\uc2  report suggests the UK economy could contract by 0.3% in the final quarter of 2024, suggests Elias Hilmer, assistant economist at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hilmer adds:\par \par \uc2 That said, we doubt the economy will be quite as weak as that given the PMIs do not capture rises in government spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\uc2  says his EP Group is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery pleased\u8221\'20\'1D to have reached an agreement with the Business Secretary to allow its takeover of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD promises to be a good custodian of the postal operator, saying:\par \par \uc2 We would like to thank the Business Secretary for the constructive negotiations that have resulted in unprecedented commitments and undertakings that demonstrate the high regard EP Group has for \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  as an institution, the service it provides to millions of UK homes and businesses, and \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  employees.\par \par \uc2 EP Group is a long term and committed investor with a mission to make \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  a successful modern postal operator with high quality service and products for its customers. We look forward to delivering on this mission alongside our partners in government.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 UK taking 'golden share' in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  to smooth takeover\par \par \uc2 Back to the \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  takeover, where the government has just confirmed it has reaches agreement with \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s prospective new owners, and approved EP Group\u8217\'20\'19s takeover.\par \par \uc2 Business secretary, Jonathan Reynolds says it shows the government is working hand in hand with private sector to improve crucial public services.\par \par \uc2 Under the deal, the UK has negotiated a \u8216\'20\'18Golden Share\u8217\'20\'19 in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 . This should prevent the headquarters of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 , or its tax base, being moved abroad without \uc2 UK government\uc2  approval.\par \par \uc2 Reynolds said :\par \par \uc2 For too many years progress on securing a stable future at \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  has stalled, but from day one we have been committed to providing a secure future for thousands of workers and customers.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s agreement is yet another example of this Government\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to working hand in hand with business to generate reform give respite to people right across the UK, as we are working towards ensuring a financially stable \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  with protected links between communities other providers can\u8217\'20\'19t reach.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d like to thank EP Group and \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\uc2  for their constructive approach to our discussions and their commitment to protecting this national icon. I look forward to working with them to fix the foundations and ensure \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  continues to deliver for the communities and businesses who rely on it most.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 UK firms cut staffing by most in almost four years\par \par \uc2 Newsflash: UK companies are cutting jobs at the fastest rate since early in the Covid-19 pandemic, a new survey of British purchasing managers shows.\par \par \uc2 S&P Global\u8217\'20\'19s latest flash \uc2 PMI\uc2  report, just released, shows that staffing numbers are falling in December, for the third month in a row, as firms react to October\u8217\'20\'19s tax-raising budget.\par \par \uc2 The rate of job shedding across the private sector economy was the fastest for almost four years, led by services companies.\par \par \uc2 Firms are choosing not to replace voluntary leavers due to rising employment costs, the report says, such as forthcoming increases in employers\u8217\'20\'19 National Insurance contributions and the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 The increase in employers\u8217\'20\'19 NICs rates is also leading to cutbacks to working hours and longer-term efforts to restructure workforces, S&P Global says\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PMI\uc2  report shows that there was marginal growth across the private sector this month; its Composite Output Index was unchanged at 50.5, just over the 50-point mark showing stagnation.\par \par \uc2 But while the services sector grew, there was another contraction in manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 Worryingly, business optimism fell to the lowest level since December 2022, largely due to an ongoing slide in service sector confidence.\par \par \uc2 Chris Williamson, chief business economist at S&P Global Market Intelligence says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBusinesses are reporting a triple whammy of gloomy news as 2024 comes to a close, with economic growth stalled, employment slumping and inflation back on the rise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEconomic growth momentum has been lost since the robust expansion seen earlier in the year, as businesses and households have responded negatively to the new Labour government\u8217\'20\'19s downbeat rhetoric and policies. Business confidence has sunk to a two-year low as companies weigh up a tougher outlook for sales alongside rising costs, notably for staff as a result of changes announced in the Budget. The survey\u8217\'20\'19s price gauges are indicating that inflation is turning higher again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirms are responding to the increase in National Insurance contributions and new regulations around staffing with a marked pull-back in hiring, causing employment to fall in December at the fastest rate since the global financial crisis in 2009 if the pandemic is excluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the December \uc2 PMI\uc2  is indicative of the economy more or less stalled in the fourth quarter, the loss of confidence and increased culling of jobs hints at worse to come as we head into the new year. Policymakers at the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  may be cautious about cutting interest rates, however, given the resurgence of inflation being signalled, adding further to downturn risks in 2025.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 French government bonds weaken after surprise \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrade\par \par \uc2 Back in the financial markets, France\u8217\'20\'19s risk premium has risen this morning after a surprise credit rating downgrade.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  surprised Paris on Friday night by lowering its rating on French debt to \u8220\'20\'1CAa3\u8221\'20\'1D (its forth-highest rating) from \u8220\'20\'1CAa2\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  took the unscheduled move following the collapse of \uc2 Michel Barnier\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government this month, after MPs refused to accept \u8364\'20\'AC60bn of tax hikes and spending cuts in his proposed budget.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/dec/04/france-government-vote-no-confidence-barnier-lepen-europe-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 French government ?of Michel Barnier toppled ?a?fter losing no-confidence vote \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened}}}\par \par \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLooking ahead, there is now very low probability that the next government will sustainably reduce the size of fiscal deficits beyond next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, we forecast that France\u8217\'20\'19s public finances will be materially weaker over the next three years compared to our October 2024 baseline scenario.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 French bonds are a little weaker this morning, pushing up the yield (or interest rate) on its 10-year debt by around 2 basis points, to 3.05%.\par \par \uc2 German 10-year bunds are little changed, at a yield of 2.25%, so the gap between Paris and Berlin\u8217\'20\'19s borrowing costs has widened.\par \par \uc2 Kathleen Brooks\uc2 , research director at XTB, says:\par \par \uc2 The move by \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  brings it in line with \uc2 Fitch\uc2  and S&P, but it highlights the focus on French budget deficits and the risks they pose to bond market stability. French bond yields are a touch higher on Monday, but are generally stable.\par \par \uc2 This comes after bonds sold off in Europe and in the US last week. The French 10-year bond yield rose 16bps last week, the UK yield rose by 18bps, and the 10-year Treasury yield also rose by 18bps. If we see continued upward pressure on yields, then bond market risk could be front and centre after the New Year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Full story: Gambling giant deliberately hid identities of high risk customers, financial crime watchdog alleges\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s financial intelligence agency has taken gambling giant \uc2 Entain\uc2  to the federal court, alleging it \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliberately obscured the identities\u8221\'20\'1D of high risk customers and failed to stop a \u8220\'20\'1Cserious risk of criminal exploitation\u8221\'20\'1D, my colleague Henry Belot explains.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Australian Transaction Reports and Analysis Centre\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s (\uc2 Austrac\uc2 ) civil penalty proceedings allege that \uc2 Entain\uc2 , which runs the \uc2 Ladbrokes\uc2  and Neds betting brands, committed \u8220\'20\'1Cserious and systemic non-compliance with Australia\u8217\'20\'19s anti-money laundering and counter-terrorism financing laws\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/dec/16/gambling-giant-deliberately-hid-identities-of-high-risk-customers-financial-watchdog-alleges-in-unique-court-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gambling giant deliberately hid identities of high risk customers, financial crime watchdog alleges in unique court case}}}\par \par \uc2 Entain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are now down 5%, extending their earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Unions announce 'groundbreaking' agreement over \uc2 Royal Mail\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s Communication Workers Union\uc2  says it has reached a \u8220\'20\'1Cgroundbreaking agreement in principle\u8221\'20\'1D with EP Group over its takeover of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Communication Workers Union\uc2  general secretary \uc2 Dave Ward\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time as this agreement is announced, we are pleased to have reached a negotiators settlement with EP Group covering crucial areas such as job security, the governance of the company, a meaningful stake in the business for employees, restoring quality of service, legally binding commitments and improving the terms and conditions of our members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis agreement provides the foundation to rebuild \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese have been challenging negotiations but through the support of our members we have delivered what by any measure is a groundbreaking agreement which puts postal workers and customers back at heart of everything we do in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 EP Group has told the City that it has reached an agreement in principle with the \uc2 CWU\uc2 , which represents frontline workers in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 , and one with CMA Unite, which represents \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s managerial workforce, to help clear its takeover offer \u8211\'20\'13 alongside {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?page=with:block-675fe5998f082fbec06c232a#block-675fe5998f082fbec06c232a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the agreement with the government just announced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ward adds that the \uc2 CWU\uc2  will always campaign for \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  to be returned to public ownership, but took the decision to protect its members once it was clear the government would support the takeover by \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ward adds:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe other major factor here is whilst many will fear \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  falling into the hands of a foreign equity investor, the truth is that the status quo is what will kill off postal services in the UK.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Royal Mail Group Board have been running the company into the ground over a sustained period and in the process have completely alienated their own workforce. It is time for a fresh start and a complete re-set of employee and industrial relations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the takeover is completed, we will make sure every aspect of our agreement with EP Group is upheld in full.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 IDS chair: this is an important milestone in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  takeover\par \par \uc2 Keith Williams\uc2 , non-executive chair of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s parent company IDS, says today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/dec/16/royal-mail-takeover-czech-billionaire-daniel-kretinsky-government-approval-bitcoin-record-uk-economy-business-live?page=with:block-675fe5998f082fbec06c232a#block-675fe5998f082fbec06c232a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an agreement between EP Group and the government}}}\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Can important milestone in the approvals process\u8221\'20\'1D for the takeover of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Williams explains:\par \par \uc2 The IDS Board welcomes the Government\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement and legal backing for the comprehensive package of undertakings and commitments we negotiated. These provide our customers, colleagues, unions, regulators and broader stakeholders with safeguards for the provision of the Universal Service Obligation, the ongoing financial stability of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 , the maintenance of colleague benefits, and \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s broader role in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe welcome the Government\u8217\'20\'19s commitment today to secure a stable future for \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 . This will not come from a change in ownership alone but must also be backed by urgent reform of the Universal Service and the continued transformation of this great British business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Newsflash: Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD enters legally binding agreement with government over \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  takeover\par \par \uc2 Newsflash: Czech billionaire \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s EP Group has announced it has reached agreement with the UK goverment, and UK unions, over its proposed takeover of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As flagged earlier, this appears to clear the way for Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD to take control of the postal operator.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the City, EP Group says it has entered into \u8220\'20\'1Clegally binding undertakings\u8221\'20\'1D, having worked closely with the Secretary of State for the \uc2 Department for Business and Trade\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These new undertakings include ensuring that \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  continues as the Universal Service Provider in the UK, until there is a further change of control in \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There is also a five-year pledge not to transfer any surplus from \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pension fund, and also to keep IDS and \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in the UK.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Over in Vilnius, the president of the \uc2 European Central Bank\uc2  has hinted that further interest rate cuts are likely in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  says the \uc2 ECB\uc2  will cut interest rates further if inflation continues to ease towards its 2% target.\par \par \uc2 On a trip to mark the 10th anniversary of Lithuania adopting the euro, Lagarde said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the incoming data continue to confirm our baseline, the direction of travel is clear and we expect to lower interest rates further\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last week the \uc2 ECB\uc2  cut interest rates for the fourth time this year:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/12/european-central-bank-cuts-rates-for-fourth-time-this-year"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European Central Bank cuts rates for fourth time this year}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Entain\uc2  hit with money-laundering lawsuit in Australia\par \par \uc2 Gambling firm \uc2 Entain\uc2  has been hit by a money-laundering lawsuit in Australia.\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s financial crime watchdog has alleged that \uc2 Entain\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which operates a string of betting companies including \uc2 Ladbrokes\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has breached Australian anti-money laundering (AML) and counter-terrorism financing (\uc2 CTF\uc2 ) laws by its online betting platforms.\par \par \uc2 AUSTRAC\uc2  CEO Brendan Thomas said the agency considers there were systemic failures in \uc2 Entain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approach to its AML/CTF obligations, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 AUSTRAC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proceedings allege that \uc2 Entain\uc2  did not develop and maintain a compliant anti-money laundering program and failed to identify and assess the risks it faced. We are alleging this left the company at serious risk of criminal exploitation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMoney laundering is often a symptom of serious criminal activity, including fraud, scams and corruption, all of which have equally serious effects on our communities.\par \par \uc2 Entain\uc2  says it has co-operated fully with \uc2 AUSTRAC\uc2  throughout its investigation.\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 Gavin Isaacs\uc2 , told shareholders this morning that \uc2 Entain\uc2  takes the allegations \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely seriously\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Isaacs said:\par \par \uc2 We have co-operated fully with \uc2 AUSTRAC\uc2  throughout its investigation and we are implementing further enhancements to Entain Australia\u8217\'20\'19s AML and \uc2 CTF\uc2  compliance arrangements. Whilst we still have some further improvements to make, we expect these to be implemented in line with the plan we communicated to \uc2 AUSTRAC\uc2  in 2023.\par \par \uc2 We are committed to keeping financial crime out of gambling and continue to play our part in supporting a well-regulated and compliant sector for our customers, stakeholders and the wider community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Entain\uc2  have fallen around 3%, making it the top faller on the FTSE 100 share index.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Canal+ makes London stock market debut\par \par \uc2 Although the London stock market may soon lose \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 , it has gained a new member this morning.\par \par \uc2 Canal+, the international pay-TV company and owner of the studio behind the Paddington film franchise, has floated in the City this morning.\par \par \uc2 Canal+ is being spun out of French media conglomerate \uc2 Vivendi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chancellor \uc2 Rachel Reeves\uc2  has hailed the floatation as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvote of confidence\u8221\'20\'1D in the UK\u8217\'20\'19s capital markets.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/dec/15/canal-listing-vote-confidence-uk-stock-market-reeves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Canal+ listing is \u8216\'20\'18vote of confidence\u8217\'20\'19 in UK stock market, says Reeves}}}\par \par \uc2 Maxime Saada\uc2 , chair of Canal+, told Radio 4\u8217\'20\'19s Today Programme that the company wanted to reach global investors, as two-thirds of its 27m subscribers are outside France.\par \par \uc2 Saada says:\par \par \uc2 It was very important for us to appeal to international investors, and London has a strong base of international investors investorss and a very strong global reputation.\par \par \uc2 But despite that, the \uc2 London Stock Exchange\uc2  is on course for its worst year for departures since the financial crisis.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/aef053ce-c94d-4a72-8dce-bdbf56dd67e1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New figures show}}}\uc2  that 88 companies have delisted or transferred their primary listing from London\u8217\'20\'19s main market this year with only 18 taking their place, according to the \uc2 London Stock Exchange Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin surges above $106,000 on strategic reserve hopes\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has soared to new alltime highs in the early hours of this morning, as the crypto rally gathers pace.\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency is up around 4% since Friday night, hitting $106,533, and extending its rise over the $100k mark.\par \par \uc2 enltr??BREAKING:\par \par \uc2 *BITCOIN EXTENDS GAINS TO SET AN ALL-TIME HIGH ABOVE $106,000 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BITCOIN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BITCOIN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zNqBthUQu8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zNqBthUQu8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Investing.com (@Investingcom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Investingcom/status/1868457427575996650?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 These latest gains came as traders bet that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new administration will bring in a friendlier regulatory environment for crypto, and could even create a new \u8216\'20\'18bitcoin strategic reserve\u8217\'20\'19, similar to its gold reserves.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Trump pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo something great with crypto\u8221\'20\'1D, to avoid other countries getting ahead of the US on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Analyst Naeem Aslam of Zaye Capital Markets says:\par \par \uc2 There is no shortage of good news in the crypto world, and it seems that bitcoin traders are going to continue to get more presents from Santa in terms of higher highs for the bitcoin price.\par \par \uc2 There was a time when 100K was a real profit-taking target for most traders and investors, but with new momentum, many traders think and believe that they need to adjust their expectations, and the new realistic target for them is bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price hitting the level of 150K at minimum and with 200K a real potential by the end of this next year at this time. This means that traders are going to hold their horses and wait patiently while celebrating every single victory as the bitcoin price makes new highs.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Average UK house asking price drops by \u163\'00\'A36,000 this month\par \par \uc2 Christmas is coming, which means the UK housing market is cooling.\par \par \uc2 With winter setting in, a potential house buyer\u8217\'20\'19s fancy is lightly turning to more pressing concerns than a move \u8211\'20\'13 such as present-buying, food options, and juggling visiting the in-laws.\par \par \uc2 And this means that asking prices set by new sellers coming to market have dropped by \u163\'00\'A36,395, or 1.7%, this month to \u163\'00\'A3360,197, new data from \uc2 Rightmove\uc2  shows, as sellers\u8217\'20\'19 pricing power diminished in the face of advent.\par \par \uc2 But Boxing Day could bring a bounce \u8211\'20\'13 last year, on 26th December there was a record number of new sellers launching to the market for that time of year.\par \par \uc2 Rightmove\uc2  reports that the number of sales being agreed is up by 22% compared with this time last year, while the number of new buyers contacting estate agents about homes for sale is up by 13%.\par \par \uc2 Rightmove\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Tim Bannister\uc2  says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew sellers in December have to work particularly hard to capture the attention of Xmas-party and festivity-distracted buyers, and the 1.7% average monthly fall is a fitting gift for those who are still buying homes rather than presents.\par \par \uc2 Despite this monthly drop, prices have risen by 1.4% compared with this time in 2023, broadly in line with our prediction of a 1% rise in prices this year.\par \par \uc2 We are now looking ahead to the traditional Rightmove Boxing Day bounce in home-mover activity, which has increasingly become a key date in the housing market calendar.\par \par \uc2 The online estate agent is forecasting a 4% rise in 2025 as falling interest rates stimulate the market.\par \par \uc2 enltrSellers hope pre-Christmas discount sales may attract buyers who are otherwise shopping elsewhere for others. New seller asking prices dropped 1.7% (-\u163\'00\'A36,395) in December 2024 to \u163\'00\'A3360,197.\par \par \uc2 As the New Year beckons so the door to making the stamp duty threshold begins to close; as\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DIUnAqjZZ4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DIUnAqjZZ4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emma Fildes (@emmafildes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emmafildes/status/1868560717471006968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Introduction: \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  takeover by Czech billionaire 'approved'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CCzech Sphinx\u8221\'20\'1D has reportedly triumphed in his bid to take control of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British government\uc2  has approved Czech billionaire \uc2 Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u163\'00\'A33.57bn takeover of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s owner International Distribution Services, according to reports this morning.\par \par \uc2 This green light should pave the way for the formerly state-owned postal service provider to pass into foreign ownership for the first time in its history.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg93390808o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg93390808o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BBC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckg93390808o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is reporting}}}\uc2  that the sale has been approved, and that the takeover will be announced on Monday morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe post is in the Czech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rOEvi5UjEl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/rOEvi5UjEl}}}\uc2  foreign billionaire to buy \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2 . \uc2 Daniel Kretinsky\uc2  told BBC he intends to invest heavily in the roll out of delivery lockers to make online deliveries more efficient & will keep one price letter delivery 6 days a week for now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kqDKBL7Odi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kqDKBL7Odi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Paul Lewis (@paullewismoney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/paullewismoney/status/1868546223474627033?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 As part of the final deal, the \uc2 UK government\uc2  will retain a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden share\u8221\'20\'1D in the postal service giving it special rights over the governance of the company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/cecec030-10e0-4ec5-979a-6c4defa89874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/cecec030-10e0-4ec5-979a-6c4defa89874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Financial}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/cecec030-10e0-4ec5-979a-6c4defa89874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Times}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/cecec030-10e0-4ec5-979a-6c4defa89874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Once the deal goes through, \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  would leave the stock market, 11 years after being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2013/oct/11/royal-mail-shares-trading-privatisation-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floated by David Cameron\u8217\'20\'19s coalition goverment at a value of \u163\'00\'A33.3bn}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/may/29/royal-mail-owner-agrees-to-takeover-by-czech-billionaire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IDS accepted the terms and conditions of the bid}}}\uc2 , from Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\u8217\'20\'19s EP Group, in May. That offer was worth 360p per share, for the 73% of \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t already own.\par \par \uc2 Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD has made various commitments, including to keep the Universal Service Obligation (\uc2 USO\uc2 ) under whch letters are delivered six days per week, not to raid its pension surplus, and to keep \uc2 Royal Mail\uc2  headquartered and tax resident in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 Officials had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/25/government-review-launched-into-czech-billionaires-daniel-kretinsky-royal-mail-stake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reviewing whether the deal poses a risk to national security interests}}}\uc2 , including looking at Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD\u8217\'20\'19s links to Russia.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/dec/07/revealed-the-business-dealings-of-royal-mail-bidder-daniel-kretinsky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revealed: the business dealings of Royal Mail bidder Daniel Kret\u237\'00\'EDnsk\u253\'00\'FD}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/royal-mail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Royal Mail}}}\uc2  failed to deliver about a quarter of first-class post on time in recent months, marking a worsening in its recent delivery performance, when it is already under investigation for missing delivery targets.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/29/royal-mail-fails-to-deliver-first-class-post-on-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Royal Mail fails to deliver about a quarter of first-class post on time}}}\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 8.15am GMT: \uc2 European Central Bank\uc2  president \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  gives a speech to mark the 10th anniversary of the introduction of the euro in Lithuania\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9am GMT: Eurozone flash \uc2 PMI\uc2  survey for December\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9.30am GMT: UK flash \uc2 PMI\uc2  survey for December\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm GMT: NY Empire State Manufacturing Index\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2.45pm GMT: US flash \uc2 PMI\uc2  survey for December\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241216ekcg000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
