\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Amazon workers threaten strike in New York ahead of holidays\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 593 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2024\par 21:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 If company fails to meet deadline, it could lead to Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s first large-scale unfair labor practice strike in the US\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  workers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  have set a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/petitions/demand-amazon-come-to-the-bargaining-table-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadline}}}\uc2  for Sunday 15 December demanding the company agree to begin bargaining a first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union}}}\uc2  contract with the union or else workers at the warehouse, along with other Amazon workers around the US, will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazonlaborunion.org/strike-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begin}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice strike.\par \par \uc2 Amazon workers at the JFK8 warehouse in Staten Island, New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made history}}}\uc2  in March 2022 when they became the first warehouse at the retail giant to win a union election in the US.\par \par \uc2 A strike would be the first large-scale unfair labor practice strike at Amazon in the US.\par \par \uc2 Since the union win, Amazon has yet to begin negotiating a first contract with the union after filing objections to the election, which were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrbedge.com/p/08302024-board-rejects-amazons-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ). Amazon had also accused \uc2 NLRB\uc2  officials of bias and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/whats-behind-the-corporate-effort-to-kneecap-the-national-labor-relations-board-spacex-amazon-trader-joes-and-starbucks-are-trying-to-have-the-nlrb-declared-unconstitutional/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged}}}\uc2  the constitutionality of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are done asking nicely for Amazon to stop breaking the law. Amazon must commit to come to the table and bargain a \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  contract with its workers \u8211\'20\'13 or face the consequences of its inaction,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  general president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/teamsters-tell-amazon-agree-to-bargaining-dates-by-dec-15/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcing}}}\uc2  the demand and strike threat.\par \par \uc2 Amazon Labor Union \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2  Local 1 (ALU-IBT Local 1), represents the workers at JFK8.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens on Staten Island has an impact on Amazon workers across the country. Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s steadfast refusal to come to the bargaining table sends a message that employers can flout their legal obligations under the National Labor Relations Act with impunity,\u8221\'20\'1D stated the union in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/petitions/demand-amazon-come-to-the-bargaining-table-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  calling on Amazon to come to the bargaining table. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Amazon continues to engage in illegal actions against the workers of ALU-IBT Local 1, the company is also seeking to abolish the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 further demonstrating its blatant disregard for the law and the working-class.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have been organizing Amazon workers around the US for over a year, including delivery drivers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/12/atlanta-amazon-drivers-join-teamsters-union-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta}}}\uc2 , Georgia, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/08/more-amazon-drivers-in-illinois-organize-with-the-teamsters-demand-union-recognition/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Illinois}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/11/southern-california-amazon-drivers-at-dax5-join-teamsters-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several delivery driver sites}}}\uc2  in California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2024/11/teamsters-file-charges-after-amazon-union-buster-wages-homophobic-attack/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Amazon DBK4 warehouse in Queens, New York,}}}\uc2  Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://unionizeamazonkcvg.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KCVG air hub}}}\uc2  in Kentucky, and more than 1,000 workers recently demanding union recognition from Amazon at the company\u8217\'20\'19s KSBD air hub in southern California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon workers across the country are organizing with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  because we have had enough. The disrespect we face every day from management while working long hours and doing back-breaking work is a disgrace,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daniel Salinas, an air hub worker at KSBD, in a statement announcing the demand. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve worked at Amazon for three years, and it\u8217\'20\'19s past time we made some changes at this company. That starts with a union and a voice on the job for workers like me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon spokesperson Eileen Hards, said in a statement on the strike and bargaining demands, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor more than a year now, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have continued to intentionally mislead the public \u8211\'20\'13 claiming that they represent \u8216\'20\'18thousands of Amazon employees and drivers\u8217\'20\'19. They don\u8217\'20\'19t, and this is another attempt to push a false narrative. The truth is that the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have actively threatened, intimidated, and attempted to coerce Amazon employees and third-party drivers to join them, which is illegal and is the subject of multiple pending unfair labor practice charges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241213ekcd0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
