\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Project 2025: the Trump picks with ties to ultra-rightwing policy manifesto\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,274 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2024\par 19:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president-elect has tried to distance himself from Project 2025, but several key choices have direct links to it\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeatedly disavowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/nov/04/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , saying he had \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing to do\u8221\'20\'1D with the blueprint for a conservative presidency and didn\u8217\'20\'19t know the people behind it. But as he starts to assemble his cabinet and White House staff, it seems likely he\u8217\'20\'19ll get to know the people involved very well soon.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to disavow the project before winning re-election seemed improbable, given that it was written by various members of his first administration and aligned on policy goals with his own proposed second term agenda.\par \par \uc2 His transition team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/10/02/us-news/conservative-war-of-words-erupts-over-project-2025-with-trump-transition-team-vowing-not-to-tap-radioactive-recruits-and-critics-saying-project-is-too-big-to-fail/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed }}}\uc2  it would not hire any people associated with Project 2025 because it was \u8220\'20\'1Cradioactive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But, in his selections for key roles, he has already tapped people with direct ties to the rightwing manifesto.\par \par \uc2 James Braid\par \par \uc2 Braid, chosen by Trump as the director of the Office of Legislative Affairs, taught a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.project2025.org/training/conservative-governance-advancing-policy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 course }}}\uc2  as part of Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s leadership training program, one of the four pillars in the project\u8217\'20\'19s plan.\par \par \uc2 The course is called \u8220\'20\'1CCongressional Relations: How to Work with Members\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a conservative governance certificate program. The program was designed to teach potential appointees how to \u8220\'20\'1Cdevelop a comprehensive understanding of how to advance the President\u8217\'20\'19s agenda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Brendan Carr\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to chair the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2  wrote the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static.project2025.org/2025_MandateForLeadership_CHAPTER-28.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chapter }}}\uc2  on the \uc2 FCC\uc2  in Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 In the chapter, Carr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/19/betting-markets-come-for-everything-and-the-fbi-comes-for-a-betting-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocates }}}\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Creining in big tech\u8221\'20\'1D, in part by limiting the immunity tech platforms have from content posted by third parties. He specifically mentions abuses by \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Meta\uc2  and \uc2 YouTube\uc2  as examples of platforms requiring such reining in.\par \par \uc2 Monica Crowley\par \par \uc2 Crowley, named by Trump for a state department role including chief of protocol, is listed as a contributor to Project 2025, though it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what her exact contribution entailed. Her name is listed in Project 2025 alongside the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nixonseminar.com/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nixon Seminar }}}\uc2 , of which she is a member. The seminar is a monthly gathering that \u8220\'20\'1Creasserts and advances the visionary international policies rooted in conservative realism that President Nixon brought to fore\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pete Hoekstra\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for ambassador to Canada is listed as a contributor to Project 2025 in the \u8220\'20\'1CMandate for Leadership\u8221\'20\'1D document, though it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what his contribution entailed.\par \par \uc2 Tom Homan\par \par \uc2 Homan, chosen as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cborder czar\u8221\'20\'1D, is listed as a contributor to Project 2025, though his name is not listed on any specific chapter or policy ideas.\par \par \uc2 He also worked as a visiting fellow at \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . He penned op-eds, promoted by Heritage, that attacked the Biden administration over immigration and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/immigration/commentary/the-senate-immigration-deal-would-only-make-the-border-crisis-worse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 panned }}}\uc2  the bipartisan immigration deal. He wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/immigration/commentary/race-baiting-dems-smeared-me-heartless-bigot-demanding-secure-borders-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one op-ed }}}\uc2  that \u8220\'20\'1Crace-baiting Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D had called him names when he led Ice.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt\par \par \uc2 The incoming White House press secretary, Karoline Leavitt, appeared in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.project2025.org/training/conservative-governance-101/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 training videos }}}\uc2  for Project 2025. In addition to the policy manifesto, the project\u8217\'20\'19s four pillars involved amassing a database of potential employees and creating a training program for conservatives who wanted positions in a rightwing presidency.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1vsrXQp_w1Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video }}}\uc2  called \u8220\'20\'1CThe Art of Professionalism\u8221\'20\'1D, obtained by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  and Documented, Leavitt talks about her advice for people who would serve as staff. While she was the national press secretary for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/project-2025/trump-official-karoline-leavitt-criticized-media-talking-about-project-2025-which-has"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed }}}\uc2  the project had nothing to do with Trump.\par \par \uc2 She also appears in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.project2025.org/training/presidential-administration-academy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promotional video }}}\uc2  for the project.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  will be back in the White House, this time as deputy chief of staff for policy. He is the president of the America First Legal Foundation, a legal attack dog non-profit for rightwing causes.\par \par \uc2 America First Legal was listed as a supporter of Project 2025 and appeared as a member of the project\u8217\'20\'19s advisory board, though the group then asked to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2024/07/17/project-2025-advisory-board/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed }}}\uc2  from it. Miller also appeared in a promotional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.project2025.org/training/presidential-administration-academy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video }}}\uc2  for the project, which is still posted on the project\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 Peter Navarro\par \par \uc2 Navarro was named by Trump as a senior counselor for trade and manufacturing, and he spent time in prison for refusing to cooperate with the congressional inquiry into the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 He authored a chapter for Project 2025 called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe case for fair trade\u8221\'20\'1D, part of a dueling chapter on trade policy in which he argued for tariffs and restrictions while other conservatives argued for free trade. The chapter details plans to counter China via trade policy, which is likely to be part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe obvious political problem in adopting many of the policies proposed here is that they will be opposed by the special-interest groups that benefit from open borders and offshoring and that contribute lavishly to both political parties,\u8221\'20\'1D Navarro wrote of the trade plans he suggested in the chapter. \u8220\'20\'1CThese special-interest groups range from the hedge funds of Wall Street and tech entrepreneurs of Silicon Valley to big-box retailers that stuff their aisles particularly with cheap \u8216\'20\'18Made in China\u8217\'20\'19 goods.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 John Ratcliffe\par \par \uc2 Ratcliffe, offered the role of CIA director by Trump, was a visiting fellow at \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , where he was tasked with chairing a project to hold China accountable for Covid-19 and \u8220\'20\'1Chelping Project 2025 build out policy recommendations for intelligence reform in the next presidential administration\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/staff/john-ratcliffe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Heritage website }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ratcliffe is listed as a contributor to Project 2025. He also is interviewed for the project, and excerpts of the interview went into a chapter on the intelligence community. In the chapter, Ratcliffe is quoted multiple times, on issues such as making sure the intelligence community is accountable to the director of national intelligence and on countering China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI had an $85bn combined annual budget for both the national intelligence program and military intelligence program,\u8221\'20\'1D he is quoted in Project 2025. \u8220\'20\'1CMy perspective was, \u8216\'20\'18Whatever we\u8217\'20\'19re spending on countering China, it isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 JD Vance\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president has close ties with Roberts, the Heritage president. Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/30/jd-vance-project-2025-book-foreword"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote the foreword }}}\uc2  for Roberts\u8217\'20\'19s book, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/08/project-2025-kevin-roberts-book-burning-fbi-new-york-times"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released }}}\uc2  after the election.\par \par \uc2 Roberts \u8220\'20\'1Cis somebody I rely on a lot who has very good advice, very good political instincts\u8221\'20\'1D, Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.notus.org/republicans/heritage-foundation-kevin-roberts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told news outlet Notus }}}\uc2  in January 2024. In the foreword, Vance praises Roberts\u8217\'20\'19s ideas and boldness, saying the book advances a \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally Christian view of culture and economics\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Csurprising \u8211\'20\'13 even jarring\u8221\'20\'1D path forward for conservatives.\par \par \uc2 Russ Vought\par \par \uc2 Vought, the founder and president of the Center for Renewing America, wrote a chapter for Project 2025 focused on the role of the president\u8217\'20\'19s office. He is seen as one of the project\u8217\'20\'19s key contributors. His organization is also on the project\u8217\'20\'19s advisory board.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/22/trump-russ-vought-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 picked }}}\uc2  Vought to be the director of the \uc2 US Office of Management and Budget\uc2 , reprising the role Vought played in the first Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 In the chapter, Vought rails against the supposed deep state of federal civil servants, saying agencies have too much power that needs to be curtailed. He offers suggestions for various ways the president\u8217\'20\'19s office and staff positions can be used to quickly install the president\u8217\'20\'19s priorities and loyalists.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President must set and enforce a plan for the executive branch,\u8221\'20\'1D Vought wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, however, a President today assumes office to find a sprawling federal bureaucracy that all too often is carrying out its own policy plans and preferences \u8211\'20\'13 or, worse yet, the policy plans and preferences of a radical, supposedly \u8216\'20\'18woke\u8217\'20\'19 faction of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241209ekc9002uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
