\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We were demonized\u8217\'20\'19: labor unions win big in ruling on Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Act 10\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,136 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2024\par 12:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge overturned ex-governor Scott Walker\u8217\'20\'19s notorious law that stripped employees\u8217\'20\'19 collective bargaining rights\par \par \uc2 As the labor movement braces for a second Trump term, union members and their leaders are celebrating a major victory over a controversial law that stripped public sector unions of collective bargaining rights.\par \par \uc2 In response to a lawsuit alleging that a notorious law passed by the former Republican governor of Wisconsin Scott Walker in 2011 is unconstitutional, a county judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://captimes.com/news/government/dane-county-judge-strikes-more-than-60-sections-of-act-10/article_4c698b68-b0e6-11ef-8ddf-0b7906b6c3ed.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled  }}}\uc2  on Monday that more than 60 sections of the law and several sections of a follow-up law in 2015, Act 55, are unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Walker called the decision \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wisn.com/article/unions-former-gov-scott-walker-react-to-court-ruling-overturning-act-10/63075365"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brazen political activism }}}\uc2  at its worst\u8221\'20\'1D and Republicans plan an appeal.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/feb/28/wisconsin-unions-protests-scott-walker-right-to-work-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thousands protested }}}\uc2  the introduction of the law, which crippled unions\u8217\'20\'19 funding and powers. Following the passage of Act 10, several Republican-dominated states pushed to pass similar legislation, including Florida which passed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/general-news-3812d5febe1442f29d2ae9471d221edb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar law }}}\uc2  in May 2023 targeting public sector unions, and Iowa, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/general-news-3812d5febe1442f29d2ae9471d221edb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed }}}\uc2  legislation that took away collective bargaining rights from many state employees in 2017.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/wisconsin-unions-collective-bargaining-b8b73dc8d08ab07b6ffe961b66fa9f96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Act 10 }}}\uc2  stripped collective bargaining rights from thousands of state employees in Wisconsin, limiting their ability to bargain solely on wage increases that cannot exceed inflation. It also forced public sector labor unions to annually vote, with a majority of members participating and voting, to maintain certification.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were kind of just demonized, not just teachers, but public sector workers in general,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Havlicek, a high school Spanish teacher in La Crosse, Wisconsin and former president of the La Crosse Education Association which represents teachers in the school district. \u8220\'20\'1CTeachers don\u8217\'20\'19t go into it for the money but I also have groceries to buy and bills to pay and stuff like that. A lot of public sector workers, in my experience teachers, really felt like we were being scapegoated. It was really bad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The act has had a significant impact on union membership, pay and benefits. In 2010 Wisconsin had a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/regions/midwest/data/unionmembershiphistorical_wisconsin_table.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union density rate }}}\uc2  of 15.1%. That number dropped to 8.4% in 2023.\par \par \uc2 The law also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/2024/12/02/wisconsin-act-10-overturned-what-to-know-about-controversial-law/76710354007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced }}}\uc2  public sector workers to pay more for healthcare and retirement benefits, resulting in around an 8.5% decrease in their pay for workers making $50,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 An April 2024 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dpi.wi.gov/news/releases/2024/education-workforce-crisis-report-analysis#:~:text=According%20to%20the%20DPI's%20analysis,voluntary%20basis%20in%20fall%202023.https://dpi.wi.gov/news/releases/2024/education-workforce-crisis-report-analysis#:~:text=According%20to%20the%20DPI's%20analysis,voluntary%20basis%20in%20fall%202023."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report  }}}\uc2  by the Wisconsin department of public instruction found teacher pay had declined from 2010 to 2022 by nearly 20% and about four out of every 10 first year teachers either leave the state or the profession after six years.\par \par \uc2 Public school funding also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://captimes.com/news/local/education/local_schools/act-10-budget-cuts-have-lasting-effect-10-years-after-controversial-legislation/article_f77988aa-459b-5951-a1d8-c0e3dc71e279.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drastically declined }}}\uc2  in Wisconsin after Act 10 was enacted. Per pupil spending in Wisconsin out paced the national average by around $1,100 per student in 2011 and was $327 per pupil lower than the national average in 2021.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://econpapers.repec.org/article/eeeecoedu/v_3a67_3ay_3a2018_3ai_3ac_3ap_3a40-57.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study }}}\uc2  published in 2018 by Jason Baron, assistant professor in economics at \uc2 Duke University\uc2 , blamed a 20% drop in average student state test scores in Wisconsin on the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe saw school districts just tossing out 50 years of labor agreements that had been reached in our contracts,\u8221\'20\'1D added Havlicek. \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest things that we talked about we can no longer talk about. It\u8217\'20\'19s not salary and benefits, those things were limited by state budgets anyway. It was all the other things like how many classes you can teach, how many kids can be in a classroom, all kinds of stuff that would be considered working conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He explained he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Coptimistic\u8221\'20\'1D about the ruling to overturn the law, but if it withstands appeal it remains uncertain how long it will take to get back what teachers lost with their union contracts and restore the working conditions they had prior to the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA cohesive staff, people that are dedicated, who are willing to make teaching a calling in life, a lifestyle built around being an educator, is achieved by having an experienced veteran staff with low turnover. We\u8217\'20\'19ve lost that, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how long it\u8217\'20\'19ll take to get that back,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Police officers, firefighters and other public safety officers were exempted from the Act 10 legislation.\par \par \uc2 Ben Gruber worked as a firefighter-paramedic in Wisconsin when the law was enacted, so he was unaffected until 2019 when he became a conservation warden, a job that was covered by Act 10.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a pretty drastic change for me,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI went from having full collective bargaining rights, the ability to have a say in my working conditions and contract and a grievance procedure to immediately that stuff was gone,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gruber, who is currently president of AFSCME Local 1215 and a plaintiff in the lawsuit against Act 10.\par \par \uc2 Gruber argued the impacts of the law have been drastic on public sector workers in Wisconsin, from stripping workers of their rights to deteriorating working conditions and compensation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really impacted our ability to provide the highest quality service that we can to the public as public servants,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re all here to serve the public, and all we ask in return is a voice in our working conditions. I think one of the impacts that\u8217\'20\'19s often overlooked is the cost associated with all of the illegal terminations, discriminatory promotional practices, the lack of accountability for management and the loss of talent and professional experience that we see in increased turnover and hiring, all those hidden costs that don\u8217\'20\'19t get talked about and really are a degradation on our ability to go out and provide that really strong public service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Act 10 was passed in Wisconsin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wispolicyforum.org/research/state-government-workforce-churn-reaches-historic-heights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 employee turnover  }}}\uc2  for state employees soared; retirements increased from 3.3% in 2010 to 6.8% in 2011. Non-retirement separations, resignations and terminations, increased from 2.8% in 2010 to a record high in 2022 at 11.7%, according to a June 2023 report by the Wisconsin Policy Forum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAct 10 stripped workers of the freedom and power to have a voice on the job to bargain wages, benefits and working conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Randi Weingarten\uc2 , president of the \uc2 American Federation of Teachers\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere are many fights still to come, but this decision stands to make a huge difference for educators, nurses and public service workers and the people they proudly help each and every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican proponents of Act 10 have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wisn.com/article/wisconsin-republicans-appeal-judges-ruling-against-act-10/63086069"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed }}}\uc2  the court decision and are planning to seek a stay of the law pending appeal in a fight to preserve the law, citing budget savings from the law that have come from shifting benefit compensation for retirement pensions and health insurance onto employees.\par \par \uc2 Walker, who lost re-election in 2018, criticized the decision and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ScottWalker/status/1863673959792758942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed }}}\uc2  collective bargaining \u8220\'20\'1Cis not a right. It is an expensive entitlement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241208ekc80015t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
