\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 UK car parts firm \uc2 TI Fluid Systems\uc2  bought by Canadian rival in latest overseas takeover\b0\par\par\uc2 Mark Sweney \par \uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2024\par 14:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Up to 2,700 jobs worldwide likely to be cut at London-listed company, including at its base in OxfordBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 The car parts maker \uc2 TI Fluid Systems\uc2  has become the latest London-listed firm to succumb to an overseas takeover, in a \u163\'00\'A31bn deal.\par \par \uc2 The takeover by Canada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 ABC Technologies\uc2  includes cutting as many as 2,700 staff globally, 10% of its workforce, with staff levels at its headquarters in Oxford being reduced by a third.\par \par \uc2 The Oxford office is understood to employ about 50 staff, while TI\u8217\'20\'19s total UK employee numbers are unknown.\par \par \uc2 ABC said it intended to \u8220\'20\'1Cmaintain the balance of skills and functions of employees\u8221\'20\'1D of TI, and the job cuts are expected to primarily target employees in corporate, administration, research and development, and functions supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cplc-related functions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The board of TI said on Friday it had agreed the deal, which will fuel concerns of an exodus of businesses from the London stock market, after a spree of dealmaking which has accelerated in recent days.\par \par \uc2 Aviva revealed on Wednesday it had tried to buy smaller rival Direct Line for \u163\'00\'A33.3bn, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/28/uk-hospitality-group-loungers-to-be-bought-by-us-firm-for-338m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cafe bar business Loungers }}}\uc2  succumbed to a \u163\'00\'A3338m bid from the US private equity company \uc2 Fortress Investment Group\uc2 , and the Australian asset manager Macquarie {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/28/australia-macquarie-offers-to-buy-uk-listed-waste-management-firm-renewi-for-700m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck a \u163\'00\'A3700m deal to buy the waste management business Renewi }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Spire Healthcare\uc2  surged on Friday over speculation that the FTSE 250 company may be the next to sell up, after reports that India\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Narayana Health\uc2  is in talks to take a controlling stake.\par \par \uc2 A decision to maintain TI\u8217\'20\'19s main headquarters in the US, at Auburn Hills in Michigan, means the headcount and \u8220\'20\'1Cassociated footprint\u8221\'20\'1D of administration functions in Oxford will be reduced.\par \par \uc2 The cuts, which are subject to consultation after the deal closes, also include cutting 5% to 10% of TI\u8217\'20\'19s manufacturing facilities and offices globally.\par \par \uc2 TI, founded in 1922 as Harry Bundy & Co in Detroit, Michigan, started making parts for the Ford Model T. It has 98 manufacturing locations in 28 countries.\par \par \uc2 TI, which had rejected several offers from the Toronto-based ABC over the past few months, said it decided to accept the latest offer of 200p a share because of disruption and uncertainty in the global automotive sector. TI makes car parts including fuel tanks and pipes.\par \par \uc2 It also said it took the \u163\'00\'A31.04bn cash deal, which is worth \u163\'00\'A31.8bn when debt is included, because of the \u8220\'20\'1Clong-term potential\u8221\'20\'1D of the business not being reflected in its stock market valuation of \u163\'00\'A3860m.\par \par \uc2 TI said it was a 37.2% premium to its share price before the planned takeover was announced in September.\par \par \uc2 The diminishing number of UK-listed firms has prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/nils-pratley-on-finance/2024/feb/29/uk-stock-market-isnt-working-undervaluation-wincanton-currys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing concern about the health of the London market }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241129ekbt001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
