\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People forget their manners\u8217\'20\'19: US retail workers brace for Black Friday shopping rush\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato in New York \par \uc2 711 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2024\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sales employees complain of understaffing, overwork and violence in frenzied run-up to Christmas season\par \par \uc2 For workers in retail, the day after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/thanksgiving"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thanksgiving }}}\uc2 , Black Friday, marks the beginning of the busiest time of year.\par \par \uc2 Though the nature of shopping has changed in recent years, with online purchases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.retaildive.com/news/consumers-shop-online-holiday-season/731018/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 competing  }}}\uc2  more with brick and mortar sales and sales \u8220\'20\'1Cdays\u8221\'20\'1D lasting for weeks at a time, US retail sales between Black Friday and so-called Cyber Monday (at the end of the holiday weekend) are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.retaildive.com/news/consumer-spending-record-black-friday-cyber-monday-report/728916/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 projected }}}\uc2  to grow 5% this year in the US, hitting a record $75bn.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/ooh/sales/retail-sales-workers.htm#:~:text=The%20lowest%2010%20percent%20earned,was%20%2416.19%20in%20May%202023."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 4 million people }}}\uc2  in the US work in retail sales, with a median hourly wage of $16.30 an hour, but working conditions, benefits and pay can vary widely between employers, especially as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-workers-unions-reap-higher-wages-even-us-organizers-suffer-setbacks-2021-07-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than 5% }}}\uc2  of the workforce is unionized.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe holiday is a frenzied time for shopping. Sometimes stores will extend their hours, but unfortunately workers will remain an afterthought during the holidays,\u8221\'20\'1D Margaux Lantelme, a retail employee at \uc2 REI\uc2  in Chicago, told a press conference held by the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU) to address issues they face during holiday shopping seasons. Workers at \uc2 REI\uc2  in Chicago voted to unionize in May 2023 but are still fighting to secure a first union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are working longer hours, often understaffed for the amount of traffic. Rarely, if ever, is there any kind of holiday bonus time,\u8221\'20\'1D Lantelme said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to top it all off, workers are often met with even more impatience and rudeness from customers than usual.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She argued the issues that drove her and her coworkers to unionize are exacerbated during the holidays, such as scheduling issues and understaffing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn top of being overworked during the holidays, there is also the expectation that workers remain available to operate the store at a time that everyone wants to take it easy and be with family,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not fair that retail and service workers are expected to give up important time with family for a job that ultimately does not care about or value them at all. We are being asked to prioritize a business over our personal lives, and that business would never prioritize US workers over their profits.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other retail employees criticized the tendency of customers to take out holiday stress and frustrations on frontline employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou definitely notice stress for sure, people are short-tempered. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of disgruntled attitudes flying around during this time of the year with our local customers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cynthia Russo, who has worked at Bloomingdale\u8217\'20\'19s in New York City for over 18 years and is a member of RWDSU Local 3.\par \par \uc2 Kathryn Harper, a senior bookseller at McNally Jackson, an independent bookstore in New York City, said \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople just forget their manners\u8221\'20\'1D around November every year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to give you excellent customer service, but when you leave, you get to check those things off on your to-do list, and I have to go back to seven more hours of choosing gifts for people who are stressing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A produce manager at a Stop & Shop grocery store on Long Island, New York, Edwin Quezada, said the treatment of frontline workers during the Covid-19 pandemic as \u8220\'20\'1Cheroes\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cessential\u8221\'20\'1D has dissipated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not treated like we were treated during Covid, where we used to get the \u8216\'20\'18thank you\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19s and \u8216\'20\'18we appreciate what you do,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Quezada. \u8220\'20\'1CDuring this time of year we want to keep it joyful and to keep it joyful is to have patience with us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joan Solomon, a longtime \uc2 Macy\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  employee in New York City, noted the holiday shopping season isn\u8217\'20\'19t as busy as it used to be, but the stressors and concerns about the safety of employees remain. New York recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bsk.com/new-york-labor-and-employment-law-report/new-york-enacts-retail-worker-safety-act-addressing-workplace-violence-in-retail-settings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a law }}}\uc2  requiring retailers to adopt safety measures in response to a rise in workplace violence toward workers, but it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take effect until next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the holiday season is rough,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just have to do our jobs, be merry, be happy, and go home to our families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241129ekbt000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
