\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in 20 countries to protest or strike on Black Friday\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,097 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 November 2024\par 21:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Organizers demand better workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and climate action. Plus, Israeli killing of journalists in Lebanon could be war crime, experts sayDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are expected to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/25/amazon-protest-strike-black-friday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest or strike in more than 20 countries }}}\uc2  during Black Friday and Cyber Monday to agitate for better workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and climate action.\par \par \uc2 Action is planned in big cities across the US, Germany, the UK, Turkey, Canada, India, Japan, Brazil and other countries. It is coordinated by the Make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Pay campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cloud.progressive.international/s/4aY3xXLyYpfD7gs/download"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which calls }}}\uc2  on \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 founded by the billionaire \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to pay its workers fairly and respect their right to join unions, pay its fair share of taxes, and commit to environmental sustainability.\par \par \uc2 Spearheaded by the Swiss-based \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2  for service industries and the activist umbrella group \uc2 Progressive International\uc2 , Make Amazon Pay is made up of more than 80 trade unions, anti-poverty and garment worker rights groups, and others.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are organizers saying? Christy Hoffman, the general secretary of \uc2 UNI Global Union\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s relentless pursuit of profit comes at a cost to workers, the environment and democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda Gearing, a senior organiser at GMB, said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Amazon\uc2  represents everything that is broken about [the UK\u8217\'20\'19s] economy. Insecure work, poverty wages and often unsafe working conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How has \uc2 Amazon\uc2  responded? A spokesperson said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re always listening and looking at ways to improve\u8221\'20\'1D but insisted \u8220\'20\'1Cwe remain proud of the competitive pay, comprehensive benefits, and engaging, safe work experience we provide our teams\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds flee north Gaza as \uc2 IDF\uc2  orders more evacuations amid intense airstrikes and \u8216\'20\'18apocalyptic\u8217\'20\'19 conditions\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military has ordered the evacuation of new areas of northern Gaza, setting off a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/24/hundreds-flee-north-gaza-as-idf-orders-more-evacuations-amid-intense-airstrikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fresh wave of civilian displacements }}}\uc2  on Sunday as intense airstrikes continued across much of the territory.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  said the evacuation orders for the Shujaiya neighbourhood were issued after Palestinian militants fired rockets at Israel on Saturday from a location within the densely populated district. \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s armed wing said it had targeted an army base over the border.\par \par \uc2 The humanitarian situation in northern Gaza has been described as apocalyptic by humanitarian officials, with tens of thousands suffering acute lack of water, sanitation, food and medical supplies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s the humanitarian toll of the war? After the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack on Israel on 7 October 2023, which killed 1,200 people and during which 250 were taken hostage, Israel has bombarded the territory with airstrikes and a ground invasion. Infrastructure has been decimated, the population displaced multiple times and brought close to starvation, and more than 44,000 people have been killed, according to Gaza health officials, with the \uc2 UN Human Rights Office\uc2  reporting that 70% of those whose deaths it had verified were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/nov/08/gaza-unparalleled-suffering-jan-egeland-norwegian-refugee-council-aid-ceasefire-hostages-peace-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women and children }}}\uc2 . The death toll is understood to be an underestimate, with the \uc2 UN\uc2  estimating in May 2024 that more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/05/1149256"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10,000 }}}\uc2  people\u8217\'20\'19s bodies were under the rubble.\par \par \uc2 Republican senator: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll have lots of questions\u8217\'20\'19 for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial picks\par \par \uc2 A prominent Republican US senator pledged on Sunday that Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/24/trump-controversial-cabinet-picks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would not give blanket approval }}}\uc2  to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial cabinet picks ahead of the congressional confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  of Oklahoma predicted lawmakers in the upper chamber would have tough questions in particular for the former Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , who was chosen by the president-elect as director of national security for his second administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll have lots of questions,\u8221\'20\'1D Lankford, the newly elected vice-chair of the Senate policy committee, told CNN.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What can Gabbard expect during her Senate confirmation? She faces a potentially rough ride, after being accused of spreading Russian propaganda over the war in Ukraine, prompting critics to ask if she might be a \u8220\'20\'1CRussian asset\u8221\'20\'1D, as well as her making a clandestine visit to Syria to meet the country\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2 , who is accused of war crimes.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Legal experts say an Israeli strike that killed three journalists and wounded three more could be a war crime, in a 25 October attack in south Lebanon. Remnants of munitions found at the site revealed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/25/killing-of-journalists-in-israeli-strike-could-be-a-war-legal-experts-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least one of the weapons was US-made }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK is facing continued flooding and disruption after being hit by the deadly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2024/nov/25/travel-chaos-and-flooding-to-continue-as-uk-counts-cost-of-storm-bert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Storm Bert. }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China is increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/24/china-unnerved-russia-growing-ties-north-korea-claims-us-official"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unnerved }}}\uc2  about North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s engagement with Russia, the US deputy secretary of state has said.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Cop29 climate finance deal struck for $300bn-a-year \u8211\'20\'13 but criticized as \u8216\'20\'18abysmally poor\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The climate finance deal agreed at Cop29 early on Sunday morning has been labeled a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/24/cop29-climate-finance-deal-criticised-travesty-justice-stage-managed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctravesty of justice\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 . Developing nations urged rich countries to provide $1.3tn-a-year to help with decarbonization and extreme weather. But the deal pledges $300bn annually, with $1.3tn just a target. Chandni Raina, a negotiator for India, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cabysmally poor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The cut-throat world of theatre combat choreographers\par \par \uc2 When a scene calls for violence, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2024/nov/25/theatre-fight-directors-combat-choreographers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 combat choreographers }}}\uc2  prevent actors getting injured. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery step, every look, every moment is put together like a dance,\u8221\'20\'1D says Kate Waters, known as Kombat Kate.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: World will be \u8216\'20\'18unable to cope\u8217\'20\'19 with volume of plastic waste in 10 years, warns expert\par \par \uc2 This week sees the final round of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/24/world-unable-cope-10-years-talks-un-global-treaty-to-end-plastic-waste"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN talks on the first global treaty to end plastic waste }}}\uc2 . But Anne Beathe Tvinnereim, co-chair of a coalition of 60 nations, warned the world will be \u8220\'20\'1Cunable to cope\u8221\'20\'1D with the volume of plastic waste a decade from now \u8211\'20\'13 unless countries act.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Greek man in his 80s starts night school after life of toil\par \par \uc2 In his dark suit and polished loafers, Vasillis Panayiotaropoulos cuts a dapper figure and is by far the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/25/best-in-the-class-greek-man-in-his-80s-starts-night-school-after-life-of-toil"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oldest pupil }}}\uc2  attending the second night school of central Athens. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything I learn is interesting,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 26 November 2024 to clarify that the \uc2 UN human rights office\uc2  said 70% of the fatalities it had verified in Gaza were women and children. The office reported that at 2 September 2024 it had verified 8,119 of the war dead (through processes requiring at least three independent sources for each person).\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241125ekbp001bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
