\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Musk and Ramaswamy call for ending work-from-home for federal employees\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levine in New York \par \uc2 564 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2024\par 16:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pair suggest Trump could require government workers to be in-office five days a week as part of effort to trim workforce\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  suggested \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could require government employees to be in the office five days a week as part of an effort to trim the size of the federal workforce.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRequiring federal employees to come to the office five days a week would result in a wave of voluntary terminations that we welcome: If federal employees don\u8217\'20\'19t want to show up, American taxpayers shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t pay them for the Covid-era privilege of staying home,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk and Ramaswamy wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/opinion/musk-and-ramaswamy-the-doge-plan-to-reform-government-supreme-court-guidance-end-executive-power-grab-fa51c020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a Wednesday op-ed in the Wall Street Journal }}}\uc2 . Trump has tapped both men to lead the newly created department of government efficiency.\par \par \uc2 The two men, who have no previous experience in government, also suggested Trump would undertake \u8220\'20\'1Clarge-scale firings\u8221\'20\'1D and relocate government agencies outside of Washington.\par \par \uc2 Musk requires employees at \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to work in person and has described it as a moral issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople should get off the goddamn moral high horse with the work-from-home bullshit,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/05/16/elon-musk-work-from-home-morally-wrong-when-some-have-to-show-up.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he said in 2023 }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/OMB-Report-to-Congress-on-Telework-and-Real-Property.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Around 50% }}}\uc2  of federal government workers are not eligible for telework, according to a report released earlier this year from the Office of Management and Budget. Those who are eligible for telework, spent 60% of regular working hours at in-person job sites.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese numbers indicate that the Federal workforce has telework rates generally in line with the private sector,\u8221\'20\'1D the report said.\par \par \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , national president for the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 , a union that represents more than 800,000 federal workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/20/politics/doge-remote-work-federal-employees/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN }}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe implication that federal employees writ large are not working in-person is simply not backed up by data and reality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have pushed the Biden administration over the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s approach to telework, including a provision on a spending bill that the White House provide more information on workplace flexibility.\par \par \uc2 In April 2023, the Office of Management and Budget issued a memorandum telling federal agencies to \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially increase meaningful in-person work at Federal offices \u8230\'20\'26 while still using flexible operational policies as an important tool in talent recruitment and retention\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Some federal workers told CNN that a five-day in-person work mandate would upend their lives and not be feasible. One employee who spoke with the outlet works for the \uc2 Library of Congress\uc2  and took a $12,000 pay cut when they moved to the midwest during the Covid-19 pandemic and bought a home. Another employee told CNN they would have to commute two to three hours to the nearest office.\par \par \uc2 In their op-ed, Musk and Ramaswamy sketched out other ways they believed the federal government could save money, including audits, and improved procurement. They also suggested pushing to allow the president to block expenditures by Congress, a move they acknowledged would likely require a ruling from a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  Trump has shaped in his favor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith a decisive electoral mandate and a 6-3 conservative majority on the Supreme Court, DOGE has a historic opportunity for structural reductions in the federal government. We are prepared for the onslaught from entrenched interests in Washington. We expect to prevail,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241121ekbl0028m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
