\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Union calls Democratic party staff layoffs after record fundraising \u8216\'20\'18callous\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 543 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 November 2024\par 20:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leadership accused of betraying party values after sudden announcement of layoffs without severance\par \par \uc2 The union representing workers at the \uc2 Democratic National Committee (DNC)\uc2  has accused the party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership of a \u8220\'20\'1Ccallous\u8221\'20\'1D betrayal of party values after the sudden announcement of layoffs of permanent employees without severance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite record-breaking fundraising, the DNC failed to provide any financial support to those who have tirelessly served the Democratic Party and its mission,\u8221\'20\'1D said the union in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bsky.app/profile/dncstaffunion.bsky.social/post/3lb7onkze2c2j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They compared the lack of severance to laid-off employees with the Harris-Walz campaign, which provided three weeks of severance to laid-off employees. \u8220\'20\'1CThese cuts go far beyond typical campaign turnover and impact employees who were previously told their positions would be retained after the election,\u8221\'20\'1D the union claimed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m heartbroken. These are single parents. These are new parents. These are recent graduates. You can ask any laid-off employees, friend or family, and they will vouch for the toll this job takes on you. You already give up so much when you decide to work for this organization and now they\u8217\'20\'19re taking our financial security as well.\u8221\'20\'1D said a former DNC staffer and union member who was one of the workers laid off.\par \par \uc2 They requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation from future job prospects. \u8220\'20\'1CLosing an election does not absolve the organization of its responsibility to treat workers with basic dignity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over 100 staff at the DNC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/01/04/dnc-staff-unionize-overwhelming-margin-526490"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted  }}}\uc2  to unionize with Service Employees International Union Local 500 in January 2022.\par \par \uc2 Workers were notified at night on 13 November of the layoffs, according to the press release, and the union claimed the DNC had not disclosed to the union the full extent of the layoffs or if additional cuts were planned.\par \par \uc2 The former staffer argued that nothing in the union contract precludes the DNC from providing severance and transparency regarding layoffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow could we have raised record-breaking numbers and still find ourselves in this situation?\u8221\'20\'1D they added.\par \par \uc2 The press release claimed DNC leadership had not been responsive in the wake of the layoffs and criticized the layoffs in contrast to the staff management whose decisions \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated this situation\u8221\'20\'1D remain on payroll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery cycle, political organizations scale up to meet the demands, and as the cycle comes to a close, it\u8217\'20\'19s a tough reality of our industry that we must part with talented, hardworking staff,\u8221\'20\'1D a DNC spokesperson said in a statement to the Guardian \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the DNC has met the terms of the union agreement negotiated by the \uc2 CBA\uc2 , we share the entire DNC family\u8217\'20\'19s frustration and continue to provide resources to all members of the team to support them in this transition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They claimed, per the Warn Act, staffers were notified 60 days in advance of termination, that 95% of staffers laid off were cycle hires. They also claimed that all union contract terms were upheld and that the DNC union and DNC management had been in communication, adding that the current DNC staff were focused on the transition ahead of the new DNC chair election early next year, ongoing fundraising and infrastructure upkeep, and holding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party accountable.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241118ekbi0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
