\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  handpicked by Trump to carry out slash-and-burn cuts plan\b0\par\par\uc2 Blake Montgomery \par \uc2 775 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2024\par 12:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 World\u8217\'20\'19s richest man has been an enthusiastic cost-cutter \u8211\'20\'13 but he may find the public sector an entirely different beast\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , president-elect of the US, announced on Tuesday that he has selected \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  to lead the Department of Government Efficiency, with plans to reduce bureaucracy in the federal government by roughly a third.\par \par \uc2 Musk had pushed for a government efficiency department and has since relentlessly promoted it, emphasizing the acronym for the agency: Doge, a reference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to a meme }}}\uc2  of an expressive Shiba Inu dog. Trump said the agency will be conducting a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete financial and performance audit of the entire federal government, and making recommendations for drastic reforms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CollinRugg/status/1854716187512651808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video posted on X }}}\uc2  two days after the election, Trump said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately re-issue my 2020 executive order, restoring the president\u8217\'20\'19s authority to remove rogue bureaucrats\u8221\'20\'1D. He wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cclean out the deep state\u8221\'20\'1D. His promises echo his slogan on The Apprentice: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/project-2025-trump-plan-fire-civil-service-employees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , an influential and controversial blueprint for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term, lays out ways to make bureaucrats fireable.\par \par \uc2 Musk has extensive experience slashing corporate spending, and he has promised to cull federal payrolls in much the same way. He cut staff at X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , by 80% after buying it in 2022, a move he said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-12-21/musk-says-cost-cutting-averted-3-billion-twitter-shortfall?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevented a $3bn shortfall }}}\uc2 , but which has not otherwise paid off. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/27/technology/linda-yaccarino-x-ceo-elon-musk.html#:~:text=Internal%20documents%20obtained%20by%20The,decline%20from%20the%20previous%20year."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revenue is in steep decline }}}\uc2  and advertisers have absconded, making a comeback seem unlikely. As the CEO of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , however, he has garnered a reputation for launching rockets more cheaply than competitors by negotiating with suppliers and keeping operations lean.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire does not seem to be under any illusions of what will happen after his proposed cuts, admitting that reducing spending \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessarily involves some temporary hardship\u8221\'20\'1D. Americans do want to spend less \u8211\'20\'13 of their own money. Do they want austerity and less financial assistance from the federal government? Do they want the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person admonishing them to cut their expenses?\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy, meanwhile, is a wealthy biotech entrepreneur whose first time running for office was for the Republican nomination last year. He told ABC earlier this week that he was having \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-impact discussions\u8221\'20\'1D about possible roles in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet. He also has no government experience, but has pushed for cost-cutting in the corporate sector. After building a stake in the struggling online media firm \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2 , he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/28/vivek-ramaswamy-buzzfeed-staff-cuts-conservative-hires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged the company }}}\uc2  in May to cut staff and hire conservative commentators like \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk has already asked Trump to appoint \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  employees to top government positions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/06/us/politics/elon-musk-trump-benefits.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times has reported }}}\uc2 . The president-elect promised to ban bureaucrats from taking jobs at the companies they regulate. Such a rule would seem to bar \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lieutenants from the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s door. But Trump has never shied away from cronyism. The two are not trying to avoid the appearance of a conflict of interest: Musk\u8217\'20\'19s role in the government will be structured so that he can maintain control of his companies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/d207c4a9-0e6d-4ece-a44d-abf890316b5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Financial Times reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his first term, Trump and his team struggled to fill the thousands of government appointments needed to run the federal government. The former New Jersey governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2  said the administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/transcripts/nx-s1-5111947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 never fully recovered }}}\uc2  from its failure to find those appointees. Perhaps adding Musk to the equation is meant to prevent a repeat of such laggardness.\par \par \uc2 In an extreme version of the new administration, Trump and Musk simply eliminate any position for which they cannot find a friendly appointee. In John Kennedy Toole\u8217\'20\'19s Pulitzer-winning 1980 novel A Confederacy of Dunces, the idiot hero, tasked with organizing an intractable pile of files at his new job, eradicates the company\u8217\'20\'19s mess. Ignatius J Reilly is no genius of organization, though; he is just throwing cabinets full of records away. It is easy to imagine Trump and Musk following his example.\par \par \uc2 What will stand in Musk\u8217\'20\'19s way, however, is one of his sworn enemies: labor law. \uc2 Tesla\uc2  is the only major US carmaker that does not employ a unionized workforce. The billionaire CEO {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tesla_and_unions#:~:text=Tesla%20CEO%20Elon%20Musk%20has,United%20States%2C%20Germany%20and%20Sweden."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wants to keep it that way }}}\uc2 . Federal government employees, by contrast, enjoy strong employment protections that would hinder Musk\u8217\'20\'19s slash-and-burn approach to cost-cutting and possibly render it impossible.\par \par \uc2 For all the different companies he runs, Musk has little experience managing public sector employees. He may find them less pliable lions than he is used to taming.\par \par \uc2 Kira Lerner contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241113ekbd000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
