\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Afternoon Update: Worker dies in windfarm accident; fears over possible Trump cabinet picks; and \uc2 Mattel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s porn mishap\b0\par\par\uc2 Alan Vaarwerk \par \uc2 959 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2024\par 06:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Want to get this in your inbox every weekday? Sign up for the Afternoon Update here, and start your day with our Morning Mail newsletter.\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon. A man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/11/victoria-windfarm-death-rokewood-fan-blade-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died after being crushed beneath a turbine blade }}}\uc2  while working at a regional Victorian windfarm.\par \par \uc2 Victoria police said the man was working at Golden Plains windfarm on Bells Road in Rokewood, about 133km west of Melbourne, when he was crushed by the blade shortly after 8am on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Danish energy company Vestas, which is constructing the energy project, confirmed a subcontractor died after a turbine blade that was on the ground was being prepared for installation, and that the site had been closed while investigations into the accident are carried out. The rotor blades used in the project are more than 80 metres long, according to the organisation\u8217\'20\'19s website.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Australian Workers Union\uc2  claimed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/11/australia-news-live-greens-propose-74bn-plan-to-wipe-all-student-debt-nation-to-mark-remembrance-day?page=with:block-673171ec8f088b29b8c43612#block-673171ec8f088b29b8c43612"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it had raised safety concerns }}}\uc2  with Vestas on the pressure facing workers due to project delays. The AWU\u8217\'20\'19s Victoria state secretary, Ronnie Hayden, said delegates had recently told management \u8220\'20\'1Cit was only dumb luck that nobody had been killed on site yet\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Top news\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Selfless\u8217\'20\'19 soldier awarded Victoria Cross |\par \par \uc2 Pte Richard Norden, a 19-year-old Australian soldier who rescued his wounded commander while seriously injured and under enemy gunfire in the Vietnam war, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/11/private-richard-norden-posthumously-awarded-victoria-cross-for-heroic-act-in-vietnam-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was posthumously awarded the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest military honour }}}\uc2  at a Remembrance Day ceremony in Canberra.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Police officer faces trial over nursing home death |\par \par \uc2 Sen Const Kristian White pleaded not guilty to manslaughter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/11/clare-nowland-tasering-case-kristian-white-manslaughter-trial-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over the alleged tasering of 95-year-old Clare Nowland }}}\uc2 , at a Snowy Mountains nursing home in May 2023.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liberal senator flags opposition to social media ban |\par \par \uc2 South Australian conservative Alex Antic posted on X that the Albanese government\u8217\'20\'19s proposed social media ban (which has \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support) was aimed at enforcing \u8220\'20\'1Ca corporate left wing message\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/11/australia-news-live-greens-propose-74bn-plan-to-wipe-all-student-debt-nation-to-mark-remembrance-day?page=with:block-67313e4e8f08a0d8bfbd397d#block-67313e4e8f08a0d8bfbd397d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to prevent young Australians becoming \u8220\'20\'1Cred pilled\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and withdrawing support from Labor.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s MPs hopeful \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory \u8216\'20\'18not a catastrophe\u8217\'20\'19 for war effort |\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian politicians have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/10/ukraines-mps-hopeful-donald-trumps-victory-not-a-catastrophe-for-war-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed tentative hopes that Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return }}}\uc2  to the White House will not necessarily mean a rapid and humiliating forced peace, after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/10/trump-putin-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly reminded the Russian president in a phone call }}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1CWashington\u8217\'20\'19s sizeable military presence in Europe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Shooting at Alabama university homecoming event |\par \par \uc2 One person was killed and 16 others were injured {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/10/alabama-shooting-tuskegee-university"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when a shooter opened fire at Tuskegee University in Alabama  }}}\uc2  on Sunday, the fourth reported shooting at homecoming events across the US within the last three weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fears over extremist Trump cabinet picks |\par \par \uc2 The range of names being put forward varies from plutocrats and technocrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/10/trump-white-house-circle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to hardline ideologues on immigration and foreign policy, }}}\uc2  including 2020 election deniers, billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and vaccine conspiracy theorist \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chinese students flock to \u8216\'20\'18night biking\u8217\'20\'19 |\par \par \uc2 A night-time cycling trend that started with four Chinese students riding 50km in search of good soup dumplings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/11/china-midnight-dumpling-bike-ride-zhengzhou-kaifeng"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blew out to a reported 100,000 people on Friday }}}\uc2 , jamming major roads, overwhelming a small tourist city and drawing the attention of authorities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mattel\uc2  apologises over Wicked porn mishap |\par \par \uc2 The toy company said it was taking \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate action\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/nov/11/mattel-apologises-after-mistakenly-linking-to-porn-website-on-wicked-dolls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after mistakenly printing the web address for a porn website }}}\uc2  on the packaging for dolls released to tie in with the upcoming Wicked film.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trial to assess red grape chemical\u8217\'20\'19s health effects |\par \par \uc2 Researchers will assess whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/nov/11/uk-trial-red-grape-chemical-prevent-bowel-cancer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a low dose of resveratrol, also found in blueberries and peanuts, }}}\uc2  could help keep bowel cancer at bay, after the chemical was found to slow tumour growth in mice.\par \par \uc2 In pictures\par \par \uc2 Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18little school project\u8217\'20\'19 named World Building of the Year\par \par \uc2 Darlington public school in Chippendale won the major building design prize at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2024/nov/11/world-building-of-the-year-2024-darlington-public-primary-school-chippendale-sydney#:~:text=Darlington%20public%20school%20in%20Chippendale%20won%20the%20major%20building%20design,more%20than%20200%20shortlisted%20entrants."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 World Architectural festival in Singapore }}}\uc2 , beating more than 200 shortlisted entrants from towering skyscrapers, museums and major transport hubs to claim the title.\par \par \uc2 What they said \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we should just take a deep breath on trying to be Trump-esque here in Australia\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 David Littleproud\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win, several Nationals backbenchers suggested Australia should echo the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s policy of withdrawing from the Paris agreement and abandoning net zero targets. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/11/nationals-liberal-coalition-net-zero-policy-donald-trump-election-win-australia-impact"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Nationals leader has rejected those calls, }}}\uc2  saying that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only people that will hurt out of that will be our farmers and our mining sector\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In numbers\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/10/cop29-summit-financial-agenda-wealthy-polluters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 world leaders gathering at Cop29 }}}\uc2  argue over how much rich countries should pay to help poor countries adapt to the climate crisis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/11/extreme-weather-cost-2tn-globally-over-past-decade-report-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new report has found a gradual upward trend in the economic impact }}}\uc2  of extreme weather events. The report found the US suffered the greatest economic losses, followed by China and India. Germany, Australia, France and Brazil all made the top 10.\par \par \uc2 Before bed read\par \par \uc2 Three things with Yael Stone: \u8216\'20\'18Please just remember \u8211\'20\'13 I am not talking about a vibrator\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s weekly interview about objects, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/nov/11/yael-stone-actor-climate-activist-interview-three-things"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the actor turned activist tells us about her \u8220\'20\'1Cdooga dooga\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which, we must stress, is not a vibrator \u8211\'20\'13 as well as childhood diaries and a long-lost cassette tape.\par \par \uc2 Daily word game\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s starter word is: MORT. You have five goes to get the longest word including the starter word. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Play Wordiply }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive this Afternoon Update to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/oct/13/afternoon-update-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here }}}\uc2 , or start your day with a curated breakdown of the key stories you need to know with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/23/morning-mail-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up-inbox-subscribe?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our Morning Mail newsletter }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And check out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the full list of our local and international newsletters }}}\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/election-newsletter-sign-up-stakes?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Stakes }}}\uc2 , your guide to the twists and turns of the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Contact us\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241111ekbb000ru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
