\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Union urges striking \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers to back improved pay offer\b0\par\par\uc2 Jack Simpson and agency \par \uc2 500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 10:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Members to vote on terms that include 38% rise, raising hopes of end to seven-week stoppage\par \par \uc2 Striking \uc2 Boeing\uc2  staff have been urged by their union to vote for an improved contract offer that includes a 38% pay rise over four years, raising hopes of an end to the stoppage after more than seven weeks.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM)\uc2  that represents the 33,000 workers has endorsed the new deal, which also includes a bigger bonus for signing up, and will ballot members on Monday in a vote that could end the dispute.\par \par \uc2 Workers who produce \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strongest-selling 737 Max commercial jet and other planes have been on strike since 13 September and have rejected two earlier offers.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest proposal includes a $12,000 (\u163\'00\'A39,304) ratification bonus and the reinstatement of an annual bonus scheme that was not included in a previous offer.\par \par \uc2 Workers have been pushing for a 40% wage increase and the return of a defined-benefit pension that they lost a decade ago. The 38% deal compares with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25% first offered by Boeing}}}\uc2  at the start of the dispute.\par \par \uc2 Last week, about 64% of the company\u8217\'20\'19s US west coast factory workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/24/boeing-strike-workers-reject-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected an offer of a 35% general wage increase}}}\uc2  over four years that was not endorsed by the union.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the IAM on social media after the latest offer said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for our members to lock in these gains and confidently declare victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe asking members to stay on strike longer wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be right as we have achieved so much success.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares rose 2.5% in after-hours trading following the announcement of the offer after an exclusive report by Reuters. Shares had closed down 3.2% earlier on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 An end to the dispute will mark a positive moment in what has been a difficult year for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  as it has faced a number of expensive safety problems.\par \par \uc2 In January {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/feb/06/faa-regulation-boeing-blowout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a door panel blew out}}}\uc2  in mid-air from one of its 737 Max 9s shortly after it took off from Portland, Oregon. The \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2  then enforced a cap on the production of the Max jets. In July it pleaded guilty {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/08/boeing-737-max-crashes-guilty-plea-indonesia-ethiopia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to a US criminal fraud charge}}}\uc2  stemming from the crashes of two 737 Max jetliners in 2018 and 2019, which killed 346 people, and agreed to pay a fine of almost $250m.\par \par \uc2 The company disclosed this month that it was seeking to raise up to $25bn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/15/boeing-stock-and-debt-offering-credit-agreement-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to shore up its finances}}}\uc2  to help it deal with production delays caused by the strike, alongside other financial pressures. According to Reuters, the strike was estimated to have cost the company up to $1bn, as of 15 October.\par \par \uc2 The company previously said it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/11/boeing-job-cuts-worker-strike-plane-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to shed 17,000 jobs}}}\uc2 , about a tenth of its workforce, as part of a cost-cutting drive.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb7002t8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
