\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers end bitter seven-week strike after clinching new pay deal\b0\par\par\uc2 Jasper Jolly and agency \par \uc2 857 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 10:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 40\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Joe Biden congratulates company and union for reaching a deal, after direct mediation by the White HouseBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US west coast factory workers have accepted a new contract offer, ending a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/25/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bitter seven-week strike}}}\uc2  that halted most jet production and deepened a financial crisis at the troubled aircraft manufacturer.\par \par \uc2 The workers\u8217\'20\'19 union said on Monday that members voted 59% in favour of the new contract, which includes a 38% pay rise spread over four years, easing pressure on the new \uc2 Boeing\uc2  chief executive, \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2 , after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/04/boeing-strike-contract-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two previous offers were voted down}}}\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a victory. We can hold our heads high,\u8221\'20\'1D the union\u8217\'20\'19s lead negotiator, Jon Holden, told members after the results were announced. \u8220\'20\'1CNow it\u8217\'20\'19s our job to get back to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The end of the first strike in 16 years by \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s largest union is welcome relief for a company that has lurched from one setback to the next since a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/06/alaska-airlines-grounds-boeing-737-max-9-planes-after-mid-air-window-blowout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 door panel blew off a near-new 737 Max plane}}}\uc2  in mid-air in January. Before that happened, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  had been trying to ramp up production after years of crisis after two fatal crashes and the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares rose by 1.9% in pre-market trading.\par \par \uc2 In a message to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employees, Ortberg said he was pleased the union had ratified a deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the past few months have been difficult for all of us, we are all part of the same team,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will only move forward by listening and working together. There is much work ahead to return to the excellence that made \uc2 Boeing\uc2  an iconic company.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 About 33,000 machinists who work on the bestselling 737 Max jet, as well as the 767 and 777 wide-body airliners, have been on strike since 13 September. The dispute is likely to affect US economic growth as \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest exporter.\par \par \uc2 The strike also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/01/kamala-harris-shock-us-jobs-figures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contributed to a steep decline last week in the final US jobs numbers}}}\uc2  before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election. The data \u8211\'20\'13 also heavily affected by hurricanes \u8211\'20\'13 showed a drop of 44,000 in people employed in the transport equipment manufacturing sector, suggesting that the effects of the strike had spread through the supply chain.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first US president to join a union picket line}}}\uc2 , on Tuesday congratulated the company and the union for reaching a deal, after direct mediation in the dispute by the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the last four years, we\u8217\'20\'19ve shown collective bargaining works,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CGood contracts benefit workers, businesses, and consumers \u8211\'20\'13 and are key to growing the American economy from the middle out and the bottom up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The end of the strike will also be a relief to \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s airline customers. \uc2 Ryanair\uc2 , Europe\u8217\'20\'19s largest airline, on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/04/ryanair-profits-lower-and-boeing-737-michael-oleary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut back its forecasts for growth}}}\uc2  in passenger numbers, blaming delays in \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deliveries.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ryanair\uc2  chief financial officer, \uc2 Neil Sorahan\uc2 , said that the company did not expect to receive new \uc2 Boeing\uc2  planes until January or even February, because of the time it takes to restart complex supply chains.\par \par \uc2 The company had initially offered a pay rise of 25%. The workers had demanded a 40% wage increase and the restoration of a defined-benefit pension they lost a decade ago for a less generous 401(k) retirement plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m ready to get back to work,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Lemon, a worker in equipment calibration certification in Seattle who voted in favour of the contract.\par \par \uc2 The old pension will not be restored, but workers received a bump to company matching contributions for their 401(k) plans.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  also promised to build its next aircraft in the Seattle area. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve never given us a commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to a new airplane before launch, Holden said.\par \par \uc2 It will now take weeks to ramp up plane output and boost cashflow, with 737 Max output expectedin the single digits each month for some time, according to two people briefed on the matter, far short of the 38 a month targeted before the strike.\par \par \uc2 Workers can start returning to building planes from Wednesday and must be back to work by 12 November, the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM)\uc2  said, although \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has warned that some people will have to be retrained due to the prolonged period away from the factory floor.\par \par \uc2 The strike was costing \uc2 Boeing\uc2  about $100m a day in lost revenue, analysts said, prompting the manufacturer to raise $24bn from investors last week \u8211\'20\'13 the most equity ever raised by a US company \u8211\'20\'13 in an attempt to preserve its investment-grade credit rating.\par \par \uc2 S&P Global Ratings\uc2 , the rating agency, last week said the post-strike ramp-up of production posed a key risk to \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s finances.\par \par \uc2 The pay increase may add $1.1bn to \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wage bill over the four years, while a $12,000 ratification bonus for each union member could result in a further $396m in outflows, according to analysts at Jefferies.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb7001jq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
