\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump Media outsources jobs to Mexico despite threats to businesses doing so\b0\par\par\uc2 Victoria Bekiempis \par \uc2 709 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2024\par 17:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump has warned of enormous tariffs for items imported into US, apparently to create more domestic jobs\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s social media company outsourced jobs to Mexico despite the Republican presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s threats to punish businesses who outsource jobs in such a fashion \u8211\'20\'13 and racist comments about Latinos during his campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/donald-trump-media-outsourced-jobs-mexico-truth-social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2  has reported.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the company, Trump Media, confirmed the outsourced jobs to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 whose report arrived amid the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s threats to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/trump-tariffs-price-hikes-warnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impose steep tariffs}}}\uc2  on all items imported into the US, ostensibly to create more domestic jobs.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media\u8217\'20\'19s workers in Mexico, which Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/reality-check/2015/jul/07/fact-checking-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed in 2015}}}\uc2  was sending \u8220\'20\'1Cdrug dealers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crapists\u8221\'20\'1D to the US \u8211\'20\'13 produce code and perform other technical support, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnother entity\u8221\'20\'1D hired these workers, the investigative outlet said.\par \par \uc2 The outsourcing spurred a whistleblower letter to Trump Media\u8217\'20\'19s board of directors, which \uc2 ProPublica{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/trump-media-whistleblower-complaint-devin-nunes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on in October. Staff at Trump Media \u8211\'20\'13 which owns the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/29/truth-social-trading-suspended"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social}}}\uc2  platform \u8211\'20\'13 was reportedly outraged by the company\u8217\'20\'19s use of overseas labor, believing that it flew in the face of its America first ideology.\par \par \uc2 Notably, Trump had previously reportedly threatened enormous tariffs on cars made in Mexico, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll put 200[%] or 500[%] \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Upset Trump Media staff members also demanded the firing of their chief executive officer, the former Republican congressman \uc2 Devin Nunes\uc2 , claiming he ran the company poorly and had an \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica last\u8221\'20\'1D philosophy with hiring. Nunes allegedly implemented a policy to utilize only foreign contractors, neglecting \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican workers who are deeply committed to our mission\u8221\'20\'1D, said their letter, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis approach not only contradicts the America First principles we stand for but also raises concerns about the quality, dedication, and alignment of our workforce with our core values,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  quoted the letter as saying.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media\u8217\'20\'19s representative told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that there were \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo individual workers\u8221\'20\'1D in Mexico and then railed against the outlet\u8217\'20\'19s reporting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresenting the fact that [Trump Media] works with precisely two specialist contractors in Mexico as some sort of sensational scandal is just the latest in a long line of defamatory conspiracy theories invented by the serial fabricators at \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson reportedly said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report came just three days before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election between Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the White House. Throughout the campaign, Trump has gone on the attack against outsourcing, warning companies that there would be dire consequences if they moved jobs south of the border \u8211\'20\'13 and claiming at various times that his threats had protected US jobs.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric about outsourcing has also invoked falsehoods, claiming in October that Chinese automakers were building expansive factories in Mexico. These cars, he claimed, would then enter the US without taxes.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press, citing auto industry experts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-united-auto-workers-electric-vehicles-9b0b0e3fe8464f8a054f5364af6d5eb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that there were no such factories under construction. Rather, there was a single, small Chinese car assembly plant in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Trump also claimed that the farm equipment manufacturer John Deere announced that it would probably scrap plans to move jobs to Mexico following his tariff threats. But John Deere told several outlets that the company had neither changed its plan nor announced any policy change, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/16/politics/trump-fact-check-john-deere-economy/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Trump Media\u8217\'20\'19s employment of workers in Mexico also clashes with his anti-immigrant tirades throughout his campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of our jobs are being taken by the migrants that come into our country illegally and many of those migrants happen to be criminals, and some of them happen to be murderers,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-rally-warren-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at a rally in Michigan on Friday.\par \par \uc2 No evidence shows immigrants to the US commit crimes at higher levels than people born with citizenship. And economic data does not support the claim that migrants are taking \u8220\'20\'1Call\u8221\'20\'1D US jobs.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most incendiary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/trump-springfield-pets-false-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments}}}\uc2  about immigrants in his campaign against Harris lied about how immigrants in Ohio were \u8220\'20\'1Ceating the dogs, the people that came in, they\u8217\'20\'19re eating the cats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His camp has also incensed Latino US citizens. During a recent Trump rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , the podcaster and comedian Tony Hinchcliffe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/trump-rally-puerto-rico-joke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described}}}\uc2  Puerto Rico as \u8220\'20\'1Ca floating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241104ekb4001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
