\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s canvassing operation sued in California for alleged labor law violations\b0\par\par\uc2 Andrew Gumbel in Los Angeles \par \uc2 552 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2024\par 22:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Plaintiffs accuse America Pac of several violations during its operation to support Orange county\u8217\'20\'19s Michelle Steel\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s troubled canvassing operation on behalf of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  party is now facing a lawsuit in southern California filed by two women who say they were cheated out of wages and expenses as they knocked on doors for an embattled Republican congresswoman.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25263303-241030-anderson-complaint"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suit}}}\uc2  accuses Musk\u8217\'20\'19s America Pac, which has poured {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00879510/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $100m}}}\uc2  into this year\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2  campaign, of \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful violations of the California labor code\u8221\'20\'1D by paying the plaintiffs less than it promised and refusing to make up the difference.\par \par \uc2 The women, Tamiko Anderson and Patricia Kelly, say they were hired last month and promised an hourly wage \u8211\'20\'13 about $25, according to their lead lawyer \u8211\'20\'13 to help turn out votes for Michelle Steel, who represents a closely contested swing district in Orange county, south of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 It was only once the women started working, the suit alleges, that they found out they were being paid instead by the number of houses they visited. The suit further alleges that they were not reimbursed for work-related expenses, including the use of personal cellphones to track their movements along their designated routes.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s ground-game operation has come under repeated scrutiny in recent days following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/trump-campaign-leaked-data-voters-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report in the Guardian}}}\uc2  that canvassers may have skipped as many as a quarter of the houses they claimed to have visited in Arizona and Nevada, and a second {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/elon-musk-america-pac-blitz-canvassing-michigan-uhaul/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report in Wired}}}\uc2  that revealed hired canvassers in Michigan were not told which campaign they were working for until they had already signed on.\par \par \uc2 The Orange county lawsuit, also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/elon-musk-america-pac-class-action-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  by Wired, did not specify how much less the women had earned than they were expecting, or how much they had unsuccessfully claimed in expenses. The lead plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, Larry Lee, said that they did not have a signed contract for their work, only a \u8220\'20\'1Csheet of paper\u8221\'20\'1D detailing the hourly wage they should expect.\par \par \uc2 These, however, were not reasons to consider the suit some kind of political stunt days before the 5 November election, according to a prominent national labor lawyer, Ryan Hancock of Willig, Williams & Davidson in Philadelphia. He said it was common for such suits to be light on details when first filed, and amended and fleshed out later. \u8220\'20\'1CThis appears to be a legitimate lawsuit based on an employer failing to pay compensation owed under state and federal law,\u8221\'20\'1D Hancock said.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Pac is one of several named defendants in the suit, along with a hiring and payroll company, Liberty Staffing Services; a national canvassing company, the Blair Group; and Representative Michelle Steel\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign.\par \par \uc2 The campaign, however, was quick to disavow any association with the canvassing operation. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Steel campaign has no knowledge of these individuals,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey did not and do not work for the Steel campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pac like Musk\u8217\'20\'19s usually operate independently of candidates\u8217\'20\'19 campaigns, under rules that make it illegal to coordinate activities. When asked why he had named Steel\u8217\'20\'19s campaign among the defendants, Lee, the plaintiff\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to comment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241102ekb2001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
