\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  workers fired over Gaza vigil say company \u8216\'20\'18crumbled under pressure\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,083 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2024\par 15:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Abdo Mohamed and Hossam Nasr organized event outside headquarters to reject company doing business in Israel\par \par \uc2 Two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/microsoft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Microsoft}}}\uc2  employees who were fired last week after organizing a vigil for Palestinians killed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  say the company retaliated against them for their pro-Palestinian activism.\par \par \uc2 The two, Abdo Mohamed, a researcher and data scientist, and Hossam Nasr, a software engineer, organized the event outside \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  headquarters in Redmond, Washington, on 24 October. They were fired later that evening.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Microsoft\uc2  really crumbled under pressure, internally and externally, to fire me and to shut down and retaliate against our event, not because of policy violations, simply because we were daring to humanize Palestinians, and simply because we were daring to say that \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  should not be complicit with an army that is plausibly accused of genocide,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nasr, who has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/StopAntisemites/status/1818312718123737228"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  on social media and in internal \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  employee communication groups over his support for Palestine.\par \par \uc2 Both employees were members of No Azure for Apartheid, a group of \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  workers protesting the company\u8217\'20\'19s sale of its cloud computing technology to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@noazureforapartheid/microsoft-fired-our-members-for-organizing-a-vigil-for-palestinian-victims-of-microsoft-powered-2f4c1dcd8665"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2 Microsoft\uc2  sever all Azure contracts and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.transcend.org/tms/2024/09/microsofts-ceo-for-israel-to-appear-at-event-celebrating-israeli-military-ai/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 partnerships }}}\uc2  with the Israeli military and government, disclose all ties with Israel, call for an immediate and permanent ceasefire in the conflict in Gaza, and protect and uphold the free speech of employees.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  denied that the two, who are originally from Egypt, were fired for their activism. \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain dedicated to maintaining a professional and respectful work environment and provide many avenues for all voices to be heard. But, importantly, we ask that this be done in a way that does not disrupt business operations and be aligned to our company policies and behavior expectations,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do not permit employees to use devices like bullhorns and speakers in public areas to disrupt the work of their colleagues. We were clear about our policies in advance with the event organizers and instructed that this gathering take place on public property. The organizers chose to disregard this guidance and were terminated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Mohamed and Nasr reject allegations that the vigil was disruptive and claim it was in accordance with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  policies. They say that the event, which sought to raise money for humanitarian efforts in Gaza, followed the same procedures as other employee charity events regularly held by other employee groups. The vigil was set up outdoors during lunchtime on the \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  headquarters campus, with a microphone for speakers and some chairs and signs set up for attenders.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@noazureforapartheid/microsoft-fired-our-members-for-organizing-a-vigil-for-palestinian-victims-of-microsoft-powered-2f4c1dcd8665"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No Azure for Apartheid,}}}\uc2  more than 200 employees attended the vigil in person and virtually .\par \par \uc2 Nasr and Mohamed both claimed they were in communications with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  ahead of time, and addressed any concerns that were brought up before the lunchtime event, the purpose of which they said was to honor Palestinian lives lost in the conflict and call attention to \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ties to Israel. They said police were called to the event but only observed it, and that only a microphone for speakers was used.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey never at any point said that termination was on the table or even the disciplinary consequences were on the table,\u8221\'20\'1D Nasr told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 They both questioned how it happened that Nasr\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal was publicized by the group Stop Antisemitism before they themselves were notified they had been fired. Nasr provided a call log showing he received a call from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  at 9pm on 24 October, while the group posted on social media that Nasr was \u8220\'20\'1Cno longer with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D an hour and a half earlier.\par \par \uc2 Nasr also alleged a double standard at the company, arguing that he had experienced repeated internal investigations and reprimands for comments about Gaza that he had posted on \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  internal employee groups, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/microsoft-war-over-israel-hamas-gaza-war-satya-nadella-2023-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posts}}}\uc2  he flagged internally for racism or personal attacks against him did not result in any disciplinary actions.\par \par \uc2 He pointed to posts insinuating he and another employee are \u8220\'20\'1Cmembers of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  or just supporters\u8221\'20\'1D. As far has he knows, these never resulted in reprimands. He also said HR opened an investigation into a post of his that said: \u8220\'20\'1CWith or without your sympathy, Palestinians will attain the dignity, the freedom, the respect, and the liberation that they deserve, everywhere from the Jordan River to the Mediterranean Sea.\u8221\'20\'1D However, he reported, the company did not act when another employee wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the river to the sea, Israel will forever be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  representative declined to comment on the specific examples.\par \par \uc2 The No Azure for Apartheid group characterized the firings as retaliatory and alleged \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  has engaged in intimidation toward Palestinian voices. The group disputed \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims of policy violations by the employees and is calling for their reinstatement and an explanation for the leak of their termination before the employees were themselves notified.\par \par \uc2 A Palestinian employee at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation told the Guardian that \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s internal message board has been full of messages in recent days expressing anger at the firings. They also accused \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  of double standards when it comes to enforcing harassment and behavior policies toward Palestinian voices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was unjust and very intentional as a message to the community to silence the loudest voice in our community,\u8221\'20\'1D said another Palestinian worker at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  who requested to remain anonymous.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  did not comment on the \u8216\'20\'18No Azure for Apartheid\u8217\'20\'19 campaign, its demands, or allegations of bias.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson added the company was investigating the allegation that a social media post about the terminations was published by Stop Antisemitism before the employees were informed.\par \par \uc2 A report by the Israeli-Palestinian outlet +972 Magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.972mag.com/cloud-israeli-army-gaza-amazon-google-microsoft/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the Israeli military has increased the purchase of services from Microsoft Azure since October 2023 and for years it had been the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@notechforapartheid/a-marriage-made-in-hell-an-introduction-to-microsofts-complicity-in-apartheid-and-genocide-d7dfad65a196"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 main cloud service provider}}}\uc2  for Israel. The company has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@notechforapartheid/a-marriage-made-in-hell-an-introduction-to-microsofts-complicity-in-apartheid-and-genocide-d7dfad65a196"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 funded}}}\uc2  several Israeli startups that provide services to the military.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Microsoft\uc2  is refusing to hear its worker demands,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mohamed. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what\u8217\'20\'19s happening within \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . People are calling them out, and they\u8217\'20\'19re even refusing to engage and look at serious concerns that come with the use of these technologies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US tech firms who do business with Israel have faced rising unrest internally in the last year. In April, \uc2 Google{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/27/google-project-nimbus-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  more than 50 workers in response to a protest over the company\u8217\'20\'19s military ties to the country.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241102ekb20018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
