\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US adds only 12,000 jobs in October in final report before election\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2024\par 16:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 46\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Average monthly job gains in 2024 had been about 200,000, but new figures affected by \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike and hurricanes\par \par \uc2 The US added just 12,000 jobs in October, the last snapshot of the employment market before election day, in a report heavily affected by the strike at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and two recent hurricanes.\par \par \uc2 The unemployment rate was unchanged at 4.1%.\par \par \uc2 The closely watched jobs report is the last piece of economic news before next week\u8217\'20\'19s election. Many polls report that the economy is the top issue for voters.\par \par \uc2 Economists had expected the temporary impacts from Hurricane Helene, Hurricane Milton and the ongoing strike by 33,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers in the Pacific north-west to reduce job growth numbers in October. But the number of jobs created was far lower than their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/jobs-election-economy-hurricane-hiring-unemployment-rate-c19551c5ffbff5e0f8d06e1fcee2370e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimate of 120,000 jobs}}}\uc2  for the month.\par \par \uc2 The US jobs market has been cooling after years of robust growth. October\u8217\'20\'19s figure was the weakest since December 2020.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign seized on the weak growth figures. \u8220\'20\'1CThis jobs report is a catastrophe and definitively reveals how badly \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  broke our economy,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican presidential campaign said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The White House\u8217\'20\'19s council of economic advisers moved to downplay the poor jobs growth figures blaming the \u8220\'20\'1Cdistortionary factors\u8221\'20\'1D of the hurricanes and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike. The number of people not at work due to bad weather rose by 460,000 in October, it said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the data signal gets jammed, look to the underlying trend,\u8221\'20\'1D the council added in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/cea/written-materials/2024/11/01/when-the-signal-gets-jammed-look-to-the-trend/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blogpost.}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Joe Biden blamed the October reading on storm \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastation\u8221\'20\'1D and strikes. \u8220\'20\'1CJob growth is expected to rebound in November as our hurricane recovery and rebuilding efforts continue,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said.\par \par \uc2 The US economy \u8220\'20\'1Cremains strong, with 16 million jobs created since I took office\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden added. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more work to do. We are working every day to lower costs for working families on rent, prescription drugs, health insurance, and child care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Job creation accelerated unexpectedly in September as the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/04/us-jobs-report-september"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added a revised 223,000 jobs}}}\uc2 , in the strongest month of jobs growth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/payrolls-report-show-healthy-gains-job-seekers-are-increasingly-luck-rcna173942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since}}}\uc2  March 2024. Until October the average number of jobs gained per month in 2024 has been about 200,000.\par \par \uc2 Manufacturing jobs fell by 46,000 in October, probably led by the strike at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/31/boeing-workers-strike-pay-raise-bonus-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may end next week}}}\uc2  when workers vote on a new deal. Leisure and hospitality \u8211\'20\'13 usually a major source of new jobs \u8211\'20\'13 dropped 4,000 positions. The latest report from the labor department also shaved a combined 112,000 jobs off August and September\u8217\'20\'19s hiring totals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is likely that payroll employment estimates in some industries were affected by the hurricanes; however, it is not possible to quantify the net effect on the over-the-month change in national employment, hours, or earnings estimates because the establishment survey is not designed to isolate effects from extreme weather events,\u8221\'20\'1D the labor department reported.\par \par \uc2 The continuing strength of the jobs market has surprised some economists who expected job losses as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  increased interest rates to tackle inflation.\par \par \uc2 The US now seems to be heading towards a \u8220\'20\'1Csoft landing\u8221\'20\'1D with interest rates falling, the rate of inflation slowing and employers still hiring.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in the US hit a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/11/august-inflation#:~:text=US%20inflation%20softens%20to%20lowest,rates%20%7C%20US%20economy%20%7C%20The%20Guardian"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three-year low }}}\uc2  in August 2024, falling to its lowest level since February 2021, with the consumer price index annual rate at 2.5% ahead of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first cut to interest rates since the start of the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Polling, however, shows that Americans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/poll-economy-recession-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deeply unhappy}}}\uc2  with the state of the economy and the cumulative price rises that they have experienced thanks to three years of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 And while economic indicators have shown a resilient, strong economy, Republican elected officials and Trump have sought to portray the economy negatively.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/trump-biden-harris-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsely claimed }}}\uc2  the US currently has \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst economy ever\u8221\'20\'1D. Last month, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VrsNG8E9VKM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed }}}\uc2  back on Republican claims that the last jobs report was fake, stating, \u8220\'20\'1Canything the Maga Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t like, they call \u8216\'20\'18fake\u8217\'20\'19. Anything. The job numbers are what the job numbers are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241101ekb1001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
