\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump wants you to believe that the US economy is doing terribly. It\u8217\'20\'19s untrue\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par 11:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Despite his claims to the contrary, unemployment is low, inflation is way down, and job growth is remarkably strong\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins next week\u8217\'20\'19s election, it would be the first time in US history that a candidate wins based on such a huge lie \u8211\'20\'13 his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=836424705310494"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsehood}}}\uc2  that we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/09/26/biden-record-republicans-improvements/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst economy ever\u8221\'20\'1D. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s big lie has distorted the views of millions of Americans, wrongly convincing many that the US economy is in bad shape.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no denying that many Americans are struggling economically and that inflation was painfully high back in 2022, but inflation is far lower now, and most economists agree that our economy is strong. The unemployment rate is low, inflation is way down, economic growth is solid, and job growth has been remarkably strong. Indeed, the country has added {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/PAYEMS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 18m jobs}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a record \u8211\'20\'13 under the Biden-Harris administration. Not only that, median household income has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statista.com/statistics/200838/median-household-income-in-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climbed to $80,610}}}\uc2 , higher than it was in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last year in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the 35 years I\u8217\'20\'19ve been an economist, I\u8217\'20\'19ve rarely seen an economy performing as well as it is,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Mark Zandi\uc2 , chief economist of \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  Analytics, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-kamala-harris-policies-how-strong-is-the-economy-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said recently}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d give it an A+.\u8221\'20\'1D But the US public, still upset about the surge in inflation several years ago, sees things very differently: 62% say the economy is in bad shape, while just 38% say it\u8217\'20\'19s in good shape, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnorc.org/projects/registered-voters-are-split-on-trusting-harris-or-trump-to-handle-economic-issues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an October AP-NORC poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The public holds this negative view even though there\u8217\'20\'19s been very good news for blue-collar workers: the US has added {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MANEMP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 700,000 factory jobs}}}\uc2  under the Biden-Harris administration, far more than during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, indeed more than under any president since the 1970s. There\u8217\'20\'19s also been good news for small businesses \u8211\'20\'13 a record {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/08/14/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-a-record-19-million-new-business-applications/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 19m new business applications}}}\uc2  have been filed under Biden. There\u8217\'20\'19s also good news for the wealthy \u8211\'20\'13 the stock market has climbed to record levels, which is Wall Street\u8217\'20\'19s way of saying the economy is in excellent shape. Let\u8217\'20\'19s not forget that Trump warned that if Biden was elected president, the stock market would crash. Wrong again, Donald. Under Biden, the Dow Jones Industrial Average is 36% higher than when Trump left office, and the S&P 500 is 53% higher.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated claim that today\u8217\'20\'19s economy is the worst ever shows either an appalling ignorance of history or an appalling contempt for the truth. The truth is that the economy was in far worse shape during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last year in office, when the unemployment rate soared to 14.8% during the pandemic, compared with 4.1% now. Moreover, there were many other times when the economy was in worse shape \u8211\'20\'13 it was worse during the 2008 recession under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , far worse during the 1980-81 and 1974-75 recessions, and catastrophically worse during the Great Depression of the 1930s. When Trump tells his Maga crowds that today\u8217\'20\'19s economy is the worst ever, he\u8217\'20\'19s taking everyone for an idiot.\par \par \uc2 The US economy has grown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/sn02784/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the fastest among major industrial nations}}}\uc2  since the pandemic began. Our economy has grown twice as fast as Canada\u8217\'20\'19s, three times as fast as France\u8217\'20\'19s and Japan\u8217\'20\'19s, and four times as fast as Britain\u8217\'20\'19s. Under Biden, the average unemployment rate has been lower than under any president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.investopedia.com/unemployment-rate-by-president-8637843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since Lyndon Johnson}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If Harris loses to Trump, historians and economists will long debate why she lost while \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  was re-elected in a landslide in 1984 even though unemployment was far higher back then (7.2% versus 4.1% today), inflation was higher (4% versus 2.4% today), and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest rates were far higher (10% versus 5% today). One thing working for Reagan was that GDP growth was strong in 1984.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t get me wrong, today\u8217\'20\'19s economy has serious problems. Millions of Americans are struggling, but it\u8217\'20\'19s wrong to blame Biden and Harris for that. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been writing about America\u8217\'20\'19s workers and economy for more than 40 years \u8211\'20\'13 from Reagan to Clinton to Trump to Biden \u8211\'20\'13 and under every president, millions of American have struggled economically. Trump makes believe that far more Americans are struggling now than ever before, but that\u8217\'20\'19s just not true. Take this important statistic: 11.1% of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statista.com/statistics/200463/us-poverty-rate-since-1990/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently fall below}}}\uc2  the poverty line. That\u8217\'20\'19s essentially the same percentage as under Trump and is only slightly above its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statista.com/statistics/1225017/poverty-share-by-race-race-us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lowest point in half a century}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many Americans say the economy is in poor shape mainly because of their lingering dismay about the high inflation from mid-2021 to mid-2023. But they may not know that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.poynter.org/reporting-editing/2024/wage-growth-vs-inflation-biden-presidency/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wages have risen faster}}}\uc2  than inflation over the past two years and that real wages are higher than before the pandemic. Trump blames Biden and Harris for causing inflation, but they weren\u8217\'20\'19t the cause. The two main causes were the pandemic\u8217\'20\'19s closing factories and disrupting supply chains worldwide and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war against Ukraine, which increased energy and food prices. Americans complain that gas prices are higher, but that\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Opec\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fault, not Biden\u8217\'20\'19s or Harris\u8217\'20\'19s. US oil production {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/leafhandler.ashx?n=pet&s=mcrfpus2&f=m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has hit}}}\uc2  record levels.\par \par \uc2 Housing affordability remains a big problem. Not only have housing prices soared, but high interest rates \u8211\'20\'13 which are finally coming down \u8211\'20\'13 have made it far too difficult for many Americans to buy a house. Again, the housing squeeze is not Biden\u8217\'20\'19s or Harris\u8217\'20\'19s fault; it was caused by a huge slowdown in housing production that began during the 2008 recession.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dishonesty and deceit too often make us focus on his lies rather on something far more important: the future, and what a second Trump term would mean for the country. Many economists warn of disaster if Trump wins. They warn that his plan to impose tariffs or taxes on all imported goods will send inflation soaring and ignite a dangerous trade war that could cause a recession and throw millions out of work. Economists also warn that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans, including his plan to slash taxes on the wealthy and corporations, not only will increase the federal debt by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/papers/fiscal-impact-harris-and-trump-campaign-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 colossal $7.8tn}}}\uc2 , but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/24/opinion/trump-social-security.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could bankrupt}}}\uc2  the social security system and lead to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/blogs/what-would-trump-campaign-plans-mean-social-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 33% across-the-board cut}}}\uc2  in social security benefits.\par \par \uc2 No wonder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25247867-23-nobel-economists-sign-letter-saying-harris-agenda-vastly-better-for-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 23 Nobel Prize-winning economists}}}\uc2  signed a recent letter calling Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda \u8220\'20\'1Ccounterproductive\u8221\'20\'1D and warning that it \u8220\'20\'1Cwill lead to higher prices, larger deficits, and greater inequality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to Trump, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has specific plans to improve the economy and help Americans cope with high prices. She has pledged to build 3m new housing units to help bring down housing prices. She also plans to give $25,000 in down payment assistance to first-time homebuyers. To help with the high cost of raising a family, she has called for creating a $3,600 tax credit per child and $6,000 for newborns. Recognizing how expensive caregiving needs can be, she wants to create a trailblazing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mailchi.mp/kamalaharris.com/fact-sheet-a-historic-medicare-at-home-plan-to-support-the-sandwich-generation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medicare at Home program}}}\uc2  to help pay for care for ageing parents.\par \par \uc2 Nobel-winning economists said Harris\u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/23/politics/nobel-prize-economists-harris-economic-plan/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vastly superior}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s and \u8220\'20\'1Cwill improve our nation\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D employment opportunities, health, investment and fairness.\par \par \uc2 American voters have a clear choice. They can choose Harris\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, which promises a stronger, fairer economy, or Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, which will bring a worse, less stable economy with higher prices and less fairness.\par \par \uc2 Unlike Trump, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be honest and won\u8217\'20\'19t claim that his economic agenda will bring the worst economy ever, even though his agenda looks plenty dangerous.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steven Greenhouse is a journalist and author, focusing on labour and the workplace\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241030ekau001h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
