\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 At least 22 people killed in deadliest Israeli strike on central Beirut since start of war, officials say \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Philip Wen (now), L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Joanna Walters, Amy Sedghi and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 16,453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2024\par 11:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read our latest report from the region here and all our Middle East coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. You can read our latest report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/un-peacekeepers-in-lebanon-say-israel-has-fired-on-their-bases-deliberately"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the region here}}}\uc2  and all our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/middleeast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East coverage here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Some more eyewitness accounts are filtering out from central Beirut, after the Israeli strikes that killed at least 22 people.\par \par \uc2 From AFP:\par \par \uc2 In the working-class district of Basta, whose inhabitants are largely Sunni and Shiite Muslim, two old buildings of three or four floors had collapsed.\par \par \uc2 Around a kilometre away (less than a mile), a Beirut resident was still reeling from the terrifying sound of the blast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not scared usually, but it was like an earthquake,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that she wanted to flee the area.\par \par \uc2 Hassan Jaber, who lives in a nearby building, said he was wounded in the hand and leg.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI went out to throw out the rubbish, opened the door of the lift and the strike hit\u8221\'20\'1D and he was propelled to the ground, he said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, CNN reports that people could be seen overwhelmed with grief outside the American University of Beirut Medical Center, where some of the casualties of Thursday night\u8217\'20\'19s strikes on the city centre were being treated.\par \par \uc2 Outside the emergency ward, an elderly woman rocked back and forth with a dazed look in her eyes.\par \par \uc2 A man came to her with terrible news: \u8220\'20\'1CAbbas\u8217\'20\'19s son and daughter are martyrs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, his hand on her shoulder. \u8220\'20\'1CThank God for everything. Don\u8217\'20\'19t forget to say thank God for everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A few moments later, the woman burst into tears.\par \par \uc2 Two witnesses told CNN they saw an entire building collapse from one of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s strikes in central Beirut, saying the structure was full of recently displaced people and residents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe bomb hit. And the entire building fell down,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the witnesses, Hassan, told CNN outside a hospital near Beirut\u8217\'20\'19s Upper Basta neigborhood. \u8220\'20\'1CThere were so many people in the building. Not just the residents but also people who were displaced from other parts of the country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 There continues to be an outpouring of outrage after the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission in Lebanon said on Thursday that Israeli forces had deliberately fired on its positions, injuring two peacekeepers from Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military confirmed its troops opened fire in the area of the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission\u8217\'20\'19s base, claiming that \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  fighters operate from within and near civilian areas in southern Lebanon, including areas near Unifil posts. Unifil said in a statement that any attack on peacekeepers is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave violation of international humanitarian law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The safety and security of the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s more than 10,400 peacekeepers in Lebanon are \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D and operations have virtually halted since late September, \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  chief \uc2 Jean-Pierre Lacroix\uc2  told the Security Council.\par \par \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  said it had fired a missile salvo at Israeli forces on Thursday as they were trying to pull casualties out of the Ras al-Naqoura area, and they were directly hit.\par \par \uc2 In New York, Israel \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Danny Danon\uc2  said Israel was focused on fighting \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and recommended Unifil relocate 5 km (3 miles) north \u8220\'20\'1Cto avoid danger as fighting intensifies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The United States said it was deeply concerned by reports that Israeli forces fired on \uc2 UN\uc2  positions and was pressing Israel for details.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe understand Israel is conducting targeted operations near the Blue Line to destroy \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  infrastructure that could be used to threaten Israeli citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D a White House spokesperson said, referring to the demarcation line between Israel and Lebanon. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile they undertake these operations, it is critical that they not threaten \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers\u8217\'20\'19 safety and security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 France \u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  said it \u8220\'20\'1Cexpresses its deep concern following the Israeli shots that hit the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) and condemns any attack on the security of UNIFIL.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Turkey \u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael\u8217\'20\'19s attack on \uc2 UN\uc2  forces, following its massacres against civilians in Gaza, the West Bank and Lebanon is a manifestation of its perception that its crimes go unpunished.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military said in a statement its troops operated in the Naqoura area, \u8220\'20\'1Cnext to a UNIFIL base.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccordingly, the \uc2 IDF\uc2  instructed the \uc2 UN\uc2  forces in the area to remain in protected spaces, following which the forces opened fire in the area,\u8221\'20\'1D Israel\u8217\'20\'19s statement said, adding it maintains routine communication with UNIFIL.\par \par \uc2 Italy \u8217\'20\'19s defense minister defined the recent Israeli attacks on \uc2 U.N. peacekeeping\uc2  bases in southern Lebanon as possible \u8220\'20\'1Cwar crimes\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvery serious violations\u8221\'20\'1D of international laws Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Italy\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister Guido Crosetto said he has asked for a formal explanation from Israeli authorities on the attacks on Unifil bases, which he said \u8220\'20\'1Cwere not an accident nor a mistake\u8221\'20\'1D, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t accept the justification that Israeli military forces had previously alerted UNIFIL that some of its bases had to be abandoned,\u8221\'20\'1D Crosetto said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , also sharply condemned Israeli strikes on the \uc2 U.N. peacekeeping\uc2  mission in Lebanon as \u8220\'20\'1Can inadmissible act, for which there is no justification.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnother line has been dangerously crossed in Lebanon,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on social media platform X.\par \par \uc2 Jordan \u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  also denounced the Israeli strikes on the \uc2 U.N.\uc2  base as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous escalation\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrant violation of international law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Strike on central Beirut is deadliest since start of war\par \par \uc2 At least 22 people were killed after Israeli airstrikes hit residential areas of central Beirut on Thursday evening, making them the deadliest attacks to target central Beirut since the start of the war.\par \par \uc2 Wafiq Safa\uc2 , a top \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  security official, eluded an Israeli assassination attempt on Thursday in Beirut, Reuters reported citing three security sources, as \uc2 UN\uc2  said its peacekeepers in southern Lebanon were in growing danger.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli strikes hit a densely packed residential neighbourhood of apartment buildings and shops in working class districts in the heart of Beirut. Israel had not previously struck the area, which is removed from Beirut\u8217\'20\'19s southern suburbs where \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters have been repeatedly bombed by Israel.\par \par \uc2 More from Reuters:\par \par \uc2 The number of casualties rose quickly, and as midnight approached the \uc2 Lebanese Health Ministry\uc2  reported 22 people killed and 117 wounded. Among the dead was a family of eight, including three children, who had evacuated from the south.\par \par \uc2 After Israel killed a series of top \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  officials in recent weeks, including top leader \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 , Safa was among the few surviving senior figures as the group\u8217\'20\'19s upper echelons struggled to reorganise.\par \par \uc2 The attempt to kill Safa, whose role merges security and political affairs, marked a widening of targeting of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  officials by Israel, which had so far focused on the group\u8217\'20\'19s military commanders and top leaders.\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera reporter Laura Khan, meanwhile, describes scenes of chaos in central Beirut.\par \par \uc2 The hospitals have asked for no one to come and donate blood at the moment because they are already overwhelmed, so having more people come in to donate is just going to push them even further.\par \par \uc2 I was about a kilometre and a half (about 1 mile) away when the attack occurred. I heard a very deep rumble.\par \par \uc2 People outside told our colleagues that they saw streaks in the sky and, of course, big explosions.\par \par \uc2 We know that people were running and screaming in these neighbourhoods, absolutely traumatised.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am BST\par \par \uc2 A quick dispatch from Reuters on the campaign trail with vice-president and Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Las Vegas:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said on Thursday that de-escalation was needed in the Middle East, a region which has been on edge for months amid Israel\u8217\'20\'19s wars in Gaza and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  moved closer to an understanding on the scope of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s planned retaliation against Iran during their call on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/10/biden-netanyahu-call-israel-attack-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios is reporting}}}\uc2 , citing three unnamed US and Israeli officials.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration accepts that Israel will soon launch a major attack on Iran, but it fears that current plans are more aggressive than the White House would like, the report said, and potentially escalate the regional war dramatically.\par \par \uc2 However, after the Biden-Netanyahu call, a U.S. official said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are moving in the right direction.\u8221\'20\'1D Another U.S. official said the administration was a little less nervous about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s plans after the call, Axios reported.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli security cabinet convened on Thursday night local time for a briefing about the plans to attack Iran and about the understandings with the Biden administration, Axios reported, citing Israeli officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 1am in Beirut, Gaza and Tel Aviv. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 22 people were killed and more than 100 others injured after Israeli airstrikes hit residential areas of central Beirut on Thursday evening. The strikes hit the working-class district of Basta and the Nweiri neighbourhood, the deadliest attacks to target central Beirut since Israel intensified its bombardment campaign on the country two weeks ago. \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Al Manar TV reported that the strikes were an attempt to assassinate \uc2 Wafiq Safa\uc2 , a top security official with the group, which it said had failed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 28 people, including women and children, have been killed after an Israeli airstrike hit a school sheltering displaced people in central Gaza on Thursday morning. The \uc2 Palestine Red Crescent Society\uc2  (PRCS) said it had responded to 27 fatalities and 54 injuries after the strike on the school turned shelter in Deir al-Balah. The Israeli military said it targeted militants who were operating in the compound.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 42,065 Palestinians have been killed and 97,886 injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza since 7 October 2023, the Gaza health ministry said in a statement on Thursday. In Lebanon, the health ministry said 2,169 killed and 10,212 wounded over the past year of conflict. The Lebanese figure did not include the casualties from the latest Israeli strikes on central Beirut on Thursday evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Unifil, the \uc2 UN\uc2 -peacekeeping force in Lebanon, said its headquarters and nearby positions in southern Lebanon have been repeatedly hit amid recent escalation along the blue line. A Unifil spokesperson said it was \u8220\'20\'1Calarmed\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D after it said Israeli forces deliberately fired on its positions, injuring two peacekeepers. The alleged attacks brought expressions of outrage from \uc2 UN\uc2  member states who contribute troops to Unifil. The two injured \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers were Indonesian. The Israeli military confirmed its troops opened fire in the area of the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission\u8217\'20\'19s base, claiming that \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  fighters operate from within and near civilian areas in southern Lebanon, including areas near Unifil posts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military continued to push on with an offensive that began six days ago, when it sent its troops into Jabaliya, the largest of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s eight historic refugee camps and the nearby towns of Beit Hanoun and Beit Lahiya. Palestinian health officials say at least 130 people have been killed so far in the operation, which Israel says is aimed at preventing \uc2 Hamas\uc2  from regrouping. The military has told residents to evacuate an area in which the \uc2 UN\uc2  estimates more than 400,000 people are trapped.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three hospitals in northern Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 Indonesian, Al-Awda and Kamal Adwan hospitals \u8211\'20\'13 have been ordered by Israeli forces to evacuate, putting patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives at risk, medics say. The director of Kamal Adwan hospital n northern Gaza said eight patients, mostly children, were at risk inside the intensive care units should the Israeli army force them to evacuate. Israeli bombardment near Kamal Adwan hospital has already caused some damage to the facility, medics said. Officials said they know of many fatalities lying on the roads outside the hospital because of Israeli fire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , the head of the \uc2 UN Palestinian refugee agency\uc2 , \uc2 Unrwa\uc2 , said some \uc2 Unrwa\uc2  shelters and services were being forced to shut down for the first time since the war began and that with almost no basic supplies available, hunger was spreading again in northern Gaza, amid witness accounts of bodies lying uncollected in the streets because of the renewed fighting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  spoke for the first time in weeks on Wednesday amid expectations of an imminent Israeli strike on Iran. The US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also joined the call. The White House said Biden emphasised \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need to minimize harm to civilians, in particular in the densely populated areas of Beirut\u8221\'20\'1D. The readout did not directly mention possible retaliation for the Iranian missile strike but said Biden had condemned Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally\u8221\'20\'1D and pledged \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US called on Israel to urgently address \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic conditions\u8221\'20\'1D among Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip and stop \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying suffering\u8221\'20\'1D by limiting aid deliveries. Speaking to the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council on Thursday, \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  also warned Israel against trying to permanently expel Palestinians from Gaza or seize any territory for itself.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister, Yoav Gallant, warned its next strike on Iran will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdeadly, precise and surprising\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhoever attacks us will be hurt and will pay a price. Our attack will be deadly, precise and above all surprising, they will not understand what happened and how it happened, they will see the results,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallant said in a video message on Israeli media on Wednesday night, broadcast after he postponed a scheduled trip to Washington, and a few hours after the conversation between \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gulf states have been lobbying Washington to stop Israel from attacking Iran\u8217\'20\'19s oil sites because they are concerned their own oil facilities could come under fire from Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s proxies if the conflict escalates. As part of their attempts to avoid being caught in the crossfire, Gulf states including Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates and Qatar are also refusing to let Israel fly over their airspace for any attack on Iran and have conveyed this to Washington, three sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military said it had \u8220\'20\'1Celiminated\u8221\'20\'1D a \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  member in Syria who it claimed had relayed intelligence against Israel in the Israeli-occupied Golan Heights. Syrian state TV said early on Thursday that Israel had carried out airstrikes targeting an industrial site in the Syrian city of Homs and a military site in the countryside near the city of Hama, causing \u8220\'20\'1Csome material damage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UN\uc2  inquiry said it found that Israeli actions in Gaza amounted to both war crimes and the crime against humanity of extermination. A statement by ex-\uc2 UN\uc2  high commissioner for Human Rights Navi Pillay on Thursday accused Israel of \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless and deliberate attacks on medical personnel and facilities\u8221\'20\'1D in the war in Gaza, and said Israel carried out a concerted policy of destroying Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare system.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian organisations including \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2 , \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  and \uc2 War on Want\uc2  called on the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to stop all arms transfers to Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CThe escalation of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Lebanon underscore our concerns and the need for the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to immediately suspend all weapons licences to Israel, and ensure it is not complicit in atrocities,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  staff stepped up their criticism over Europe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinaction\u8221\'20\'1D in response to the Israel-Gaza war, in a letter calling on the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s senior officials to start a dialogue with them aimed at changing course on the Middle East crisis. The war has sharply divided EU member states: Hungary and the Czech Republic are Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strongest supporters, while Spain, Ireland and non-EU Norway have recognised the Palestinian state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Unicef\uc2  confirmed that the second round of polio vaccination for children in the Gaza Strip will start on 14 October. \uc2 Unicef\uc2  executive director \uc2 Catherine Russell\uc2  in a statement on Thursday said \u8220\'20\'1Carea-specific humanitarian pauses\u8221\'20\'1D had been agreed for the vaccination, adding that it was \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical that these pauses are respected by all parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A young person has been detained in Sweden after a shooting at an Israeli defence company on Thursday. Police are investigating the incident, at Elbit Systems Sweden in Kalleb\u228\'00\'E4ck, Gothenburg on Thursday morning, as attempted murder and aggravated weapons offences. Nobody was injured.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers determined to stay in Lebanon despite Israeli attacks, says Unifil\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission in Lebanon (Unifil) said its peacekeepers are determined to remain at their posts in southern Lebanon despite Israeli attacks in recent days that have wounded \uc2 UN\uc2  staff.\par \par \uc2 Unifil spokesperson Andrea Tenenti said recent Israeli attacks on the force was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most serious events or incidents that we\u8217\'20\'19ve been witnessing in the last 12 months\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Unifil\u8217\'20\'19s 50 contributing countries agreed on Thursday to keep deploying more than 10,400 peacekeepers between the Litani River in the north and the Blue Line in the south. Tenenti said:\par \par \uc2 We are there because the Security Council has asked us to be there. So we are staying until the situation becomes impossible for us to operate.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-670839608f08c777d30088eb#block-670839608f08c777d30088eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s peacekeeping chief, \uc2 Jean-Pierre Lacroix\uc2 , warned that its forces are \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D and confined to their bases, and that one Unifil contractor had already been killed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mystery surrounded the whereabouts and health of the Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps (IRGC) commander \uc2 Esmail Ghaani\uc2 , amid reports that he was being investigated over how Israel managed to penetrate and crush the command structure of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , the Lebanese militia at the heart of the Iranian \u8220\'20\'1Caxis of resistance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is known that Ghaani, who leads the IRGC\u8217\'20\'19s al-Quds force, was in Beirut at the time of the killing of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leader, \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 , but Iranian authorities have insisted he is alive, and even in line for an award for valour.\par \par \uc2 The news outlet Middle East Eye claimed Ghaani had been put under house arrest and was being investigated over the failures that allowed Israel to penetrate the \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  network so effectively. Another Arabic outlet claimed Ghaani had suffered a heart attack during questioning.\par \par \uc2 Israeli sources said the reports, regardless of their veracity, showed the degree of stress inside the IRGC over the destruction of the \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  leadership in Lebanon.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/iran-esmail-ghaani-al-quds-beirut-lebanon-israeli-strikes-hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/iran-esmail-ghaani-al-quds-beirut-lebanon-israeli-strikes-hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran general\u8217\'20\'19s whereabouts in question after Israeli strikes on Hezbollah}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 24 October 2024. An earlier version referred to Middle East Eye as \u8220\'20\'1CQatari-backed\u8221\'20\'1D. While links with the Gulf state have previously been suggested, representatives for the London-based news site have told the Guardian that it not backed, directly or indirectly, by the state of Qatar \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether in terms of ownership, financially, managerially or, most importantly, editorially\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/iran-esmail-ghaani-al-quds-beirut-lebanon-israeli-strikes-hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran general\u8217\'20\'19s whereabouts in question after Israeli strikes on Hezbollah}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Canada, which has been largely supportive of Israel\u8217\'20\'19 s military offensive in Lebanon, on Thursday said an incident in which Israeli troops fired on \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers was \u8220\'20\'1Calarming and unacceptable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A statement from the Canadian foreign ministry reads:\par \par \uc2 Canada calls for the protection of peacekeepers and humanitarian workers, and for all parties to comply with international humanitarian law.\par \par \uc2 enltr1/2 The \uc2 IDF\uc2  firing on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/UNIFIL?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #UNIFIL}}}\uc2  peacekeepers and first responders in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Lebanon?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Lebanon}}}\uc2  is alarming and unacceptable. Canada reiterates its full support for UNIFIL and its critical role in contributing to a diplomatic settlement consistent with UNSCR 1701.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Foreign Policy CAN (@CanadaFP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CanadaFP/status/1844468029905830012?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr2/2 Canada calls for the protection of peacekeepers and humanitarian workers, and for all parties to comply with international humanitarian law.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Foreign Policy CAN (@CanadaFP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CanadaFP/status/1844468031629689227?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The two \uc2 United Nations peacekeeping\uc2  troops {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN_News_Centre/status/1844459181983813696"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wounded}}}\uc2  by weapons fired by the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) earlier today were at a Unifil observation post known as OP-14 in Naquora, southern Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  posted to X also that \u8220\'20\'1Cclose by, also early this morning, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers fired on a \uc2 UN\uc2  position UNP 1-31 from an opening in the fence made by the \uc2 IDF\uc2  the previous day during adjacent ground works. Several vehicles and a communications system were damaged.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrClose by, also early this morning, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers fired on a \uc2 UN\uc2  position UNP 1-31 from an opening in the fence made by the \uc2 IDF\uc2  the previous day during adjacent ground works\par \par \uc2 Several vehicles and a communications system were damaged\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 UN News (@UN_News_Centre) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN_News_Centre/status/1844459183997087927?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It added that: \u8220\'20\'1CJust yesterday Israeli forces fired at cameras at the same \uc2 UN\uc2  position, and small arms fire hit another \uc2 UN\uc2  position also near Labuneh damaging lighting and a radio relay station.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also, in this thread on X, the \uc2 UN{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN_News_Centre/status/1844459179769200856"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CClashes in the Labuneh/Naqoura area since 8 October have involved tank and small arms fire, airstrikes, Iron Dome interceptions and multiple explosions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Head of \uc2 UN Peacekeeping\uc2  lambasts Israel firing on troops\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre Lacroix\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/unitednations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Nations}}}\uc2  under-secretary-general for peace operations, has spoken out at the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  in New York, lambasting Israeli military fire on peacekeeping troops\u8217\'20\'19 position in southern Lebanon earlier today.\par \par \uc2 This situation has put our peacekeepers at serious risk,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThis situation has put our peacekeepers at serious risk\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jean-Pierre Lacroix\uc2 , head of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UNPeacekeeping?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UNPeacekeeping}}}\uc2  at the Security Council, 10 Oct 24 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GwsH5xz6eP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GwsH5xz6eP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 UN News (@UN_News_Centre) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN_News_Centre/status/1844458723768758724?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Two soldiers were wounded when the Unifil \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  force in Lebanon \u8211\'20\'13 headquarters in Naqoura, on the coast, close to the line between Lebanon and Israel, was hit by tank fire.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yemen\u8217\'20\'19s Houthi group have claimed responsibility for an attack on a Liberian-flagged tanker in the Red Sea, which they said they targeted with 11 ballistic missiles and two drones on Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 The Olympic Spirit was hit about 73 nautical miles (135 kilometres) southwest of the Yemen i port of Hodeidah, British maritime security firm Ambrey said.\par \par \uc2 The tanker, en route from Saudi Arabia \u8217\'20\'19s Jeddah to Muscat in Oman, was struck on its starboard side, Reuters reported. The projectile hit the bridge causing minor damage, Ambrey said.\par \par \uc2 Four hours later, two additional projectiles reportedly detonated within 0.27 nautical mile of the vessel\u8217\'20\'19s port side. A maritime security source told Reuters:\par \par \uc2 The damage is minor. The vessel has some technical issues, but it is seaworthy and continues its journey. They (the crew members) are all safe.\par \par \uc2 The Houthis said they had also targeted a vessel it identified as St. John in the Indian Ocean with a winged missile.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli strikes on central Beirut kill 22, 117 wounded\par \par \uc2 The death toll from Israeli airstrikes on central Beirut on Thursday has risen to 22, according to the country\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry.\par \par \uc2 In addition, 117 people have been injured, it said.\par \par \uc2 One of the strikes hit the lower half of an eight-story apartment building in the area of Ras al-Nabaa, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The second strike, in the area of Burj Abi Haidar, collapsed an entire building, which was engulfed in flames.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate statement from the Israeli military, which has launched frequent strikes on Beirut\u8217\'20\'19s southern suburbs in recent weeks, but strikes in central Beirut are rare.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli military confirms troops fired in area of \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers' base in Lebanon\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military has confirmed its troops {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6707f2f18f08c777d3008564#block-6707f2f18f08c777d3008564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened fire }}}\uc2  in the area of the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission\u8217\'20\'19s base in southern Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The Unifil force said Israeli forces fired on positions used by its peacekeepers in Lebanon on Wednesday and Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Two peacekeepers were injured when an Israeli tank fired at a watchtower at the force\u8217\'20\'19s main headquarters in Ras al-Naqoura, hitting the tower and causing them to fall, Unifil said. There were no casualties in the other two incidents, according to a \uc2 UN\uc2  source.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) said \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  fighters operate from within and near civilian areas in southern Lebanon, including areas near Unifil posts.\par \par \uc2 It said the \uc2 IDF\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Coperating in southern Lebanon and maintains routine communication with Unifil\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, Israeli media reported that the target of the airstrikes in central Beirut tonight was \uc2 Wafiq Safa\uc2 , one of the top political officials of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and the head of its liaison and coordination unit.\par \par \uc2 Quoting a source in \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 -affiliated TV channel al-Mayadeen said that the assasination attempt on Safa failed.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  could not verify this information.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is deeply concerned about reports that Israeli forces fired on \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers\u8217\'20\'19 positions in southern Lebanon and is pressing Israel for details on the incidents, a White House national security council spokesperson said moments ago in Washington DC. The spokesperson said:\par \par \uc2 We understand Israel is conducting targeted operations near the Blue Line to destroy \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  infrastructure that could be used to threaten Israeli citizens. While they undertake these operations, it is critical that they not threaten \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers\u8217\'20\'19 safety and security.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Israel warned Lebanese civilians not to return to homes in the south to avoid harm from fighting.\par \par \uc2 The Unifil force, the \uc2 United Nations peacekeeping\uc2  force in Lebanon, said two of its peacekeepers were injured in an incident when an Israeli tank fired at a watchtower at the force\u8217\'20\'19s main headquarters in Ras al-Naqoura, hitting the tower and causing them to fall. There were no casualties in two other incidents, a \uc2 UN\uc2  source said.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6708016f8f084fc69f7f2724#block-6708016f8f084fc69f7f2724"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  Unifil said \u8220\'20\'1Cany deliberate attack on peacekeepers is a grave violation of international humanitarian law\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that it was following up with the Israeli military.\par \par \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  said it had fired a missile salvo at Israeli forces on Thursday as they were trying to pull casualties out of the Ras al-Naqoura area, and they were directly hit.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll from Israeli strikes on central Beirut rises to 18\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from the newswires from the aftermath of Israel i airstrikes on central Beirut on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 The latest figure from \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry\uc2  states that 18 people were killed and 92 others wounded in the two Israeli strikes.\par \par \uc2 Rescue efforts are still ongoing, the Lebanese ministry said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least 11 killed, dozens injured in Israeli strikes on central Beirut\par \par \uc2 At least 11 people have been killed and a further 48 wounded in the two Israeli strikes on central Beirut on Thursday night, the \uc2 Lebanese Ministry of Health\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Urgent rescue work continues at the sites of the airstrikes. A passerby told the Guardian that families were fleeing the scene carrying mattresses and bags, with some bleeding from the ears from the force of the blasts.\par \par \uc2 About an hour after the airstrikes, the Israeli military issued new evacuation orders for residents of Dahiyeh, the southern suburbs of Beirut, warning they will be carrying out airstrikes on pre-specified buildings they said were \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  weapons installations.\par \par \uc2 enltrIsraeli military issues its nightly evacuation orders to residents of Dahiyeh, the southern suburbs of Beirut, a little over an hour after it carried out two airstrikes in central Beirut, without warning. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qmwrva3ZcT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qmwrva3ZcT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Will Christou (@will_christou) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/will_christou/status/1844442407137628591?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry\uc2  is reporting that at least 11 people were killed in the Israeli attacks on central Beirut tonight.\par \par \uc2 That followed reports just moments ago that a much smaller number had been killed. This following airstrikes that were targeting at least one senior \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  figure, according to Lebanese security sources, as reported by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Others were injured and a large fire was blazing as rescue workers used hand torches to search through the rubble for survivors, according to videos broadcast by \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s al-Manar television.\par \par \uc2 It was not clear who the \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  targets were. The neighbourhood was not previously hit by Israel and is well removed from Beirut\u8217\'20\'19s southern suburbs, \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters repeatedly bombed by Israel.\par \par \uc2 A thick column of smoke rose above central Beirut after what appeared to be Israel\u8217\'20\'19s latest major aerial attack in a widening offensive against Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s powerful Iran-backed \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  group. There was no immediate comment from the Israeli military.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no let-up in the tension in Beirut as the public waits for more information on the latest strikes in Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s capital from Israel. It\u8217\'20\'19s 9pm in Beirut, Tel Aviv and Gaza City. Stick with this blog for news developments as they emerge.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israeli media is reporting that the target of the airstrikes in central Beirut tonight was \uc2 Wafiq Safa\uc2 , one of the top political officials of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hezbollah}}}\uc2  and the head of its liaison and coordination unit.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fresh air strikes have been reported in central Beirut, outside the Lebanese capital\u8217\'20\'19s southern suburbs where Israeli strikes have normally targeted, according to multiple reports. An Israeli strike hit an area in central Beirut that had not been previously hit, a Lebanese security source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19 s crisis response unit said 28 people were killed and 113 wounded in the past 24 hours. The country\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry released the figure earlier today. This brings the total figure to 2,169 killed and 10,212 wounded over the past year of conflict between Israel and \uc2 Hezbollah in Lebanon\uc2 , according to the ministry, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 France has said it was waiting for explanations from Israel after \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  troops were targeted in Lebanon, adding it was an obligation to ensure their safety.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 TheUN peacekeeping mission in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2  (Unifil) said it is \u8220\'20\'1Calarmed\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D by the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s activity in the area where peacekeeping troops are based. Unifil said it was following up with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military after, it said, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at \uc2 UN\uc2  positions and two peacekeepers were injured and hospitalised.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Here is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6707e0108f084fc69f7f24a8#block-6707e0108f084fc69f7f24a8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the post}}}\uc2  with our previous summary of prior news.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  official target of latest Beirut blasts - reports\par \par \uc2 Israeli media is reporting that the target of the airstrikes in central Beirut tonight was \uc2 Wafiq Safa\uc2 , one of the top political officials of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and the head of its liaison and coordination unit.\par \par \uc2 Safa oversaw foreign relations for the group, embarking on a trip to the United Arab Emirates in March in what was then seen as a potential thawing of relations between the group and the Gulf. He was also involved with maintaining the security of the group and famously threatened the judge investigating the causes of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/beirut-explosion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beirut port blast}}}\uc2  case after they requested the interrogation of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 -affiliated officials.\par \par \uc2 Ambulances were heard rushing towards the scene of the airstrikes in central Beirut as reports of casualties began to emerge. Al-Makassed hospital, also in central Beirut, reportedly received a number of dead and wounded.\par \par \uc2 Pictures of the site of one of the airstrike showed a collapsed apartment building, similar to scenes of airstrikes in Dahiyeh, the southern suburbs of Lebanon. Residents did not receive a warning to evacuate the building, as Israel has been issuing prior to its nearly nightly bombings of Dahiyeh.\par \par \uc2 enltrTwo massive air strikes in Beirut itself, location reportedly in the Basta neighbourhood but still being narrowed down. Target unclear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qAHlSO1jT2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qAHlSO1jT2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Will Christou (@will_christou) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/will_christou/status/1844423382747709709?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19 s \u8220\'20\'1Crecommendation\u8221\'20\'1D is that the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  force in southern Lebanon, Unifil, move north, the country\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Danny Danon\uc2 , Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , said in a statement reported by Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Our recommendation is that Unifil relocate 5 km (3 miles) north to avoid danger as fighting intensifies and while the situation along the Blue Line remains volatile as a result of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s aggression.\par \par \uc2 He added that Israel \u8220\'20\'1Chas no desire to be in Lebanon, but it will do what is necessary\u8221\'20\'1D to force \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  away from its northern border, so that its 70,000 residents can return to their homes in northern Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two large airstrikes hit Beirut\par \par \uc2 At least two large airstrikes were carried out in the city of Beirut on Thursday night, striking the Basta neighbourhood in central Beirut, a working-class area that has hosted many displaced people since 23 September.\par \par \uc2 The blasts were heard across Beirut, shaking windowpanes at least a mile away. The target of the strikes were unclear.\par \par \uc2 The strikes were the third time that Beirut has been targeted since the \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 -Israel war started a year prior.\par \par \uc2 Israel has largely contained its strikes to Dahiyeh, the southern suburbs of the city.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 New Israeli strikes reported in central Beirut\par \par \uc2 Strikes have been reported in central Beirut, outside the Lebanese capital\u8217\'20\'19s southern suburbs where Israeli strikes have normally targeted, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 An Israeli strike hit an area in central Beirut that had not been previously hit, a Lebanese security source told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 ITV News\u8217\'20\'19s Emma Murphy reports at least two explosions were heard after a relatively quiet day in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 enltrStrikes are in central Beirut. V close to a school housing those displaced from the South. Two v big blasts which would suggest some targeted strike/assasination.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emma Murphy (@emmamurphyitv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emmamurphyitv/status/1844422661700714580?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The BBC\u8217\'20\'19s Nafiseh Kohnavard posted a clip of the immediate aftermath of the missile strike.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe impact right behind Achrafieh\par \par \uc2 The missile/ missiles targeted a building outside southern suburbs of Beirut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4Sl3aTCsrd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4Sl3aTCsrd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nafiseh Kohnavard (@nafisehkBBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nafisehkBBC/status/1844421904314290494?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The broadcaster\u8217\'20\'19s correspondent, Anna Foster, writes:\par \par \uc2 The sound of several loud explosions rumbled and bounced off downtown\u8217\'20\'19s tall buildings.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 28 killed and 113 wounded in Lebanon, says health ministry\par \par \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19 s crisis response unit said 28 people were killed and 113 wounded in the past 24 hours, the country\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 This brings the total figure to 2,169 killed and 10,212 wounded over the past year of conflict between Israel and \uc2 Hezbollah in Lebanon\uc2 , according to the ministry, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 The report also recorded 61 airstrikes and incidents of shelling in the past day, mostly concentrated in southern Lebanon, the southern suburbs of Beirut and the Bekaa Valley.\par \par \uc2 About 1,000 centres \u8211\'20\'13 including educational complexes, vocational institutes, universities and other institutions \u8211\'20\'13 are sheltering 186,400 people displaced by the Israeli offensive in Lebanon, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Among these shelters, 822 have reached full capacity. Overall, the total number of displaced individuals in Lebanon stands at 1.2 million.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon, Unifil, said that recent escalation along the Blue Line is causing widespread destruction of towns and villages in south Lebanon with rockets continuing towards Israel and \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (IDF) soldiers clashing with \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  on the ground while rockets continue to be launched towards Israel.\par \par \uc2 Confirming casualties, Unifil said in its statement:\par \par \uc2 This morning, two peacekeepers were injured after an IDF Merkava tank fired its weapon toward an observation tower at Unifil\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Naqoura, directly hitting it and causing them to fall. The injuries are fortunately, this time, not serious, but they remain in hospital.\par \par \uc2 It added:\par \par \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers also fired on \uc2 UN\uc2  position (UNP) 1-31 in Labbouneh, hitting the entrance to the bunker where peacekeepers were sheltering, and damaging vehicles and a communications system. An IDF drone was observed flying inside the \uc2 UN\uc2  position up to the bunker entrance.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at and disabled the position\u8217\'20\'19s perimeter-monitoring cameras. They also deliberately fired on UNP 1-32A in Ras Naqoura, where regular Tripartite meetings were held before the conflict began, damaging lighting and a relay station.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The BBC reports that the two injured \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers were Indonesian, according to a \uc2 UN\uc2  spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia contributes more soldiers than any other country to Unifil, supplying more than 1,200 troops, the broadcasters write.\par \par \uc2 The Indonesian and Israeli governments have not yet commented.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 France demands explanation from Israel after \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers targeted in Lebanon\par \par \uc2 France has said it was waiting for explanations from Israel after \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  troops were targeted in Lebanon on Thursday and that it was an obligation to ensure their safety, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrance expresses its deep concern following the Israeli shots that hit the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (Unifil) and condemns any attack on the security of Unifil,\u8221\'20\'1D the foreign ministry said in a statement, adding that none of its 700 troops in the mission had been wounded.\par \par \uc2 We await explanations from the Israeli authorities. The protection of peacekeepers is an obligation that applies to all parties to a conflict.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The jailed Nobel peace prize laureate Narges Mohammadi has marked the first anniversary of her award with a call for peace in the Middle East from Tehran \u8217\'20\'19s notorious Evin prison.\par \par \uc2 The Iranian human rights activist said in comments to Italy\u8217\'20\'19s Corriere della Sera:\par \par \uc2 Today, the dark shadow of war once again hangs over our beloved country. I hate war. All those responsible for war are not only condemned by the people of the lands and times they devastate, but they are also for ever disgraced and ostracised in the annals of human history.\par \par \uc2 Mohammadi, who has been imprisoned since November 2021 for convictions in relation to her campaigning against capital punishment and the obligatory hijab in Iran, said on Wednesday that her treatment had become even more severe since she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/oct/06/jailed-iranian-activist-narges-mohammadi-wins-2023-nobel-peace-prize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was awarded the prize on 6 October 2023}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This year\u8217\'20\'19s prize will be announced by the Norwegian Nobel Committee on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/nobel-laureate-narges-mohammadi-calls-for-peace-in-middle-east-from-iran-jail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nobel laureate Narges Mohammadi calls for peace in Middle East from Iran jail}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 1,000 Americans and their dependents have fled Lebanon on US chartered flights in the last week, arriving in Turkey for a temporary stay, according to the top US diplomat in Istanbul.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the fastest, safest way to get Americans out of harm\u8217\'20\'19s way,\u8221\'20\'1D consul general Julie Eadeh said, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 The security situation is dynamic, so we have been planning for months for all contingencies. Given the airport in Beirut remains operational and open, our focus is on facilitating departures by air.\par \par \uc2 The US has additionally secured more than 4,500 seats for citizens aboard commercial flights from Lebanon in recent weeks, Eadeh added.\par \par \uc2 The goal was not to fill every seat, she said.\par \par \uc2 We are giving people an option that, if they want to leave because they determine the situation is untenable \u8230\'20\'26 they have a way out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unifil 'alarmed' and 'deeply concerned' by Israel 'targeting' \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers Lebanon\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission in Lebanon (Unifil) said it is \u8220\'20\'1Calarmed\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D by the Israel i military\u8217\'20\'19s activity in the area where peacekeeping troops are based.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6707c9368f08d77e388bab18#block-6707c9368f08d77e388bab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier,}}}\uc2  Unifil said it was following up with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military after, it said, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at \uc2 UN\uc2  positions and two peacekeepers were injured and hospitalised.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the BBC on Thursday, Andrea Tenenti said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve been deeply concerned for days or for months but now it\u8217\'20\'19s very serious because we are there to ensure stability, safety, to bring back stability that now doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist. But targeting peacekeepers, it\u8217\'20\'19s a grave violation of international humanitarian law.\par \par \uc2 He said that the positions that Israeli forces hit were very well known as \uc2 UN\uc2  sites, adding that it was important to have a discussion with the Israeli authorities \u8220\'20\'1Cto understand what happened\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy chief, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , has condemned the shelling of \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers by Israeli forces in Lebanon, adding that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno justification\u8221\'20\'1D for such an \u8220\'20\'1Cinadmissible\u8221\'20\'1D act.\par \par \uc2 In a post to X on Thursday, he said the \uc2 EU\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Creiterates its full support\u8221\'20\'1D to the \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  mission, Unifil.\par \par \uc2 enltrAnother line has been dangerously crossed in Lebanon: IDF shelling of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UN}}}\uc2  peacekeepers whose positions are known.\par \par \uc2 We condemn this inadmissible act, for which there is no justification.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 EU\uc2  reiterates its full support to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UNIFIL_?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UNIFIL_}}}\uc2  , to its \uc2 UNSC\uc2 -mandated mission & its troops.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Josep Borrell Fontelles\uc2  (@JosepBorrellF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JosepBorrellF/status/1844385197560824311?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images sent over the newswires from the central Gaza Strip, after at least 28 people were killed in an Israeli airstrike on a school sheltering displaced families on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Among the dead are women and children and more than 50 others were injured in the Israeli attack on Rufaida al-Aslamia school in the city of Deir Al-Balah, medics said.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said it had carried out a \u8220\'20\'1Cprecise strike on terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D who had a command and control centre embedded in a school.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Irish troops based in Lebanon are safe and accounted for after Israeli troops opened fire at three positions held by \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers on Thursday, the Irish government has said.\par \par \uc2 enltrSituation Update on Irish Defence Forces serving with overseas missions in Lebanon for family members\par \par \uc2 The Defence Forces can confirm all IRISH pers are safe and accounted for. All necessary force protection measures are being observed.\par \par \uc2 The Defence Forces can also confirm that\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \u211\'00\'D3glaigh na h\u201\'00\'C9ireann (@defenceforces) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/defenceforces/status/1844346388575813638?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The taoiseach, Simon Harris, warned that firing on peacekeepers \u8220\'20\'1Ccan never be tolerated or acceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Miche\u225\'00\'E1l Martin\uc2 , Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister said a drone was operational and Indonesian soldiers were injured. Martin said:\par \par \uc2 This is unacceptable. Peacekeeping is the noblest thing anyone can do. Our soldiers are there, \uc2 UN peacekeeping\uc2  soldiers are there to keep the peace at the invitation of both sides to this conflict, and Israel has an obligation to make sure that no \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeeper gets into harm\u8217\'20\'19s way.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 The second round of polio vaccinations in Gaza will start next week, according to the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s children agency (\uc2 Unicef\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The second round of vaccinations will start on 14 October and will vaccinate nearly 590,000 children under the age of 10, \uc2 Unicef\uc2  executive director \uc2 Catherine Russell\uc2  has said. She said:\par \par \uc2 Area-specific humanitarian pauses have been agreed. It is critical that these pauses are respected by all parties. Without them, it is impossible to vaccinate the children.\par \par \uc2 The organisation said they will be including Vitamin A supplements to aid the immune system of children in the territory who are living in \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely dire\u8221\'20\'1D hygiene and sanitation conditions. Russell added:\par \par \uc2 With the additional vaccine equipment and cold boxes that arrived yesterday, \uc2 Unicef\uc2  is ready to deliver and vaccinate children to stop the transmission of polio. The success of the first round shows that when agreements are respected, we can get the job done.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Italy\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister, Guido Crosetto, said his country has protested to Israel after \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers in Lebanon said Israeli forces fired on two positions used by them.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6707c9368f08d77e388bab18#block-6707c9368f08d77e388bab18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier, }}}\uc2  the Unifil force said two of its peacekeepers were injured in one of the incidents, when an Israeli tank fired at an observation tower at the force\u8217\'20\'19s main headquarters in Naqoura, hitting the tower and causing them to fall.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from the Israeli military about the incidents.\par \par \uc2 Firing at Unifil bases was \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D and clearly flouts international law, Crosetto said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CFor these reasons, I protested to my Israeli counterpart and the Israeli ambassador to Italy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just past 5.30pm in Gaza, Beirut and Tel Aviv. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 28 people, including women and children, have been killed after an Israeli airstrike hit a school sheltering displaced people in central Gaza. The \uc2 Palestine Red Crescent Society\uc2  (PRCS) said it had responded to 27 fatalities and 54 injuries after the strike on the school turned shelter in Deir al-Balah. The Israeli military said it targeted militants who were operating in the compound.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 42,065 Palestinians have been killed and 97,886 injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza since 7 October 2023, the Gaza health ministry said in a statement on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military continued to push on with an offensive that began six days ago, when it sent its troops into Jabaliya, the largest of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s eight historic refugee camps and the nearby towns of Beit Hanoun and Beit Lahiya. Palestinian health officials say at least 130 people have been killed so far in the operation, which Israel says is aimed at preventing \uc2 Hamas\uc2  from regrouping. The military has told residents to evacuate an area in which the \uc2 UN\uc2  estimates more than 400,000 people are trapped.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of civilians in Gaza remain trapped by the latest Israeli offensive centred on Jabaliya refugee camp, according to \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies and human rights groups. \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , the head of the \uc2 UN Palestinian refugee agency\uc2 , \uc2 Unrwa\uc2 , said some \uc2 Unrwa\uc2  shelters and services were being forced to shut down for the first time since the war began and that with almost no basic supplies available, hunger was spreading again in northern Gaza, amid witness accounts of bodies lying uncollected in the streets because of the renewed fighting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three hospitals in northern Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 Indonesian, Al-Awda and Kamal Adwan hospitals \u8211\'20\'13 have been ordered by Israeli forces to evacuate, putting patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives at risk, medics say. The director of Kamal Adwan hospital n northern Gaza said eight patients, mostly children, were at risk inside the intensive care units should the Israeli army force them to evacuate. Israeli bombardment near Kamal Adwan hospital has already caused some damage to the facility, medics said. Officials said they know of many fatalities lying on the roads outside the hospital because of Israeli fire.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  spoke for the first time in weeks on Wednesday amid expectations of an imminent Israeli strike on Iran. The US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also joined the call. The White House said Biden emphasised \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need to minimize harm to civilians, in particular in the densely populated areas of Beirut\u8221\'20\'1D. The readout did not directly mention possible retaliation for the Iranian missile strike but said Biden had condemned Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally\u8221\'20\'1D and pledged \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US called on Israel to urgently address \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic conditions\u8221\'20\'1D among Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip and stop \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying suffering\u8221\'20\'1D by limiting aid deliveries. Speaking to the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  also warned Israel against trying to permanently expel Palestinians from Gaza or seize any territory for itself.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Simon Harris, said he is hopeful of a ceasefire in the Middle East after an hour long meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Washington on Wednesday night. Harris said the US president told him he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery lengthy\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with Netanyahu and he was left \u8220\'20\'1Cin no doubt that this was a conversation of substances and of depth in terms of actions that Israel need to take in terms of aid, humanitarian aid, in terms of bringing about a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera accused Israel of deliberately targeting journalists after one of its cameramen was shot and critically injured by an Israeli sniper on Wednesday while a photojournalist for another network was killed and a third also injured while covering the siege of Jabaliya camp in northern Gaza. The \uc2 Hamas\uc2  affiliated TV channel al-Aqsa said on Telegram that one of its photojournalists, Mohammad al-Tanani, had been killed in an Israeli attack in Jabalia refugee camp on Wednesday, while its journalist Tamer Labad, was injured. Two days earlier, another Al Jazeera cameraman, Ali Al-Attar, was also critically injured in an Israeli attack on a hospital in northern Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Unifil, the \uc2 UN\uc2 -peacekeeping force in Lebanon, said its headquarters and nearby positions in southern Lebanon have been repeatedly hit amid recent escalation along the blue line. Unifil said it is following up with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military after, it said, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at \uc2 UN\uc2  positions and two peacekeepers were injured and hospitalised. \u8220\'20\'1CAny deliberate attack on peacekeepers is a grave violation of international humanitarian law and of Security Council resolution 1701,\u8221\'20\'1D the peacekeeping force said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister, Yoav Gallant, warned its next strike on Iran will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdeadly, precise and surprising\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhoever attacks us will be hurt and will pay a price. Our attack will be deadly, precise and above all surprising, they will not understand what happened and how it happened, they will see the results,\u8221\'20\'1D Gallant said in a video message on Israeli media on Wednesday night, broadcast after he postponed a scheduled trip to Washington, and a few hours after the conversation between \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gulf states have been lobbying Washington to stop Israel from attacking Iran\u8217\'20\'19s oil sites because they are concerned their own oil facilities could come under fire from Tehran\u8217\'20\'19s proxies if the conflict escalates. As part of their attempts to avoid being caught in the crossfire, Gulf states including Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates and Qatar are also refusing to let Israel fly over their airspace for any attack on Iran and have conveyed this to Washington, three sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military said it had \u8220\'20\'1Celiminated\u8221\'20\'1D a \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  member in Syria who it claimed had relayed intelligence against Israel in the Israeli-occupied Golan Heights. Syrian state TV said early on Thursday that Israel had carried out airstrikes targeting an industrial site in the Syrian city of Homs and a military site in the countryside near the city of Hama, causing \u8220\'20\'1Csome material damage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UN\uc2  inquiry said it found that Israeli actions in Gaza amounted to both war crimes and the crime against humanity of extermination. A statement by ex-\uc2 UN\uc2  high commissioner for Human Rights Navi Pillay on Thursday accused Israel of \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless and deliberate attacks on medical personnel and facilities\u8221\'20\'1D in the war in Gaza, and said Israel carried out a concerted policy of destroying Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare system.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian organisations including \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2 , \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  and \uc2 War on Want\uc2  called on the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to stop all arms transfers to Israel. \u8220\'20\'1CThe escalation of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Lebanon underscore our concerns and the need for the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to immediately suspend all weapons licences to Israel, and ensure it is not complicit in atrocities,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK should end its half-hearted half measures towards Israel if \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is to be stopped from pushing the world off a cliff, the Palestinian ambassador to the UK, Husam Zomlot, said on Thursday at a briefing to mark the anniversary of the Gaza conflict. He called for a full arms embargo, recognition of Palestine as a state and economic sanctions that \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantle the apparatus of illegal settlements in the West Bank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  staff have stepped up their criticism over Europe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinaction\u8221\'20\'1D in response to the Israel-Gaza war, in a letter calling on the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s senior officials to start a dialogue with them aimed at changing course on the Middle East crisis. The war has sharply divided EU member states: Hungary and the Czech Republic are Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strongest supporters, while Spain, Ireland and non-EU Norway have recognised the Palestinian state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Unicef\uc2  have confirmed that the second round of polio vaccination for children in the Gaza Strip will start on 14 October. \uc2 Unicef\uc2  executive director \uc2 Catherine Russell\uc2  in a statement on Thursday said \u8220\'20\'1Carea-specific humanitarian pauses\u8221\'20\'1D had been agreed for the vaccination, adding that it was \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical that these pauses are respected by all parties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A young person has been detained in Sweden after a shooting at an Israeli defence company on Thursday. Police are investigating the incident, at Elbit Systems Sweden in Kalleb\u228\'00\'E4ck, Gothenburg on Thursday morning, as attempted murder and aggravated weapons offences. Nobody was injured.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unicef\uc2  have confirmed that the second round of polio vaccination for children in the Gaza Strip will start on 14 October.\par \par \uc2 Unicef\uc2  executive director \uc2 Catherine Russell\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 The second round of polio vaccination in the Gaza Strip is confirmed. It will start on 14 October to vaccinate around 590,000 children under the age of 10.\par \par \uc2 Area-specific humanitarian pauses have been agreed. It is critical that these pauses are respected by all parties. Without them, it is impossible to vaccinate the children\par \par \uc2 Unicef\uc2  will include vitamin A supplements to strengthen children\u8217\'20\'19s immune systems. Children in Gaza live in extremely dire hygiene and sanitation conditions.\par \par \uc2 With the additional vaccine equipment and cold boxes that arrived yesterday, \uc2 Unicef\uc2  is ready to deliver and vaccinate children to stop the transmission of polio. The success of the first round shows that when agreements are respected, we can get the job done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  inquiry accuses Israel of crime of 'extermination' in destruction of Gaza health system\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UN\uc2  inquiry said on Thursday it found that Israel carried out a concerted policy of destroying Gaza \u8217\'20\'19s healthcare system in the Gaza war, actions amounting to both war crimes and the crime against humanity of extermination, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 A statement by ex-\uc2 UN\uc2  high commissioner for Human Rights Navi Pillay released ahead of a full report accused Israel of \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless and deliberate attacks on medical personnel and facilities\u8221\'20\'1D in the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CChildren in particular have borne the brunt of these attacks, suffering both directly and indirectly from the collapse of the health system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pillay, whose report will be presented to the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly on 30 October.\par \par \uc2 Israel says that Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s militants operate from the cover of built-up populated areas including private homes, schools and hospitals and that it will strike them wherever they emerge, while also trying to avoid harming civilians. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  denies hiding militants, weapons and command posts among civilians.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the \uc2 UN\uc2  inquiry\u8217\'20\'19s statement also accused Israeli forces of deliberately killing and torturing medical personnel, targeting medical vehicles and restricting permits for patients to leave the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 As an example, it cited the death of a Palestinian girl, Hind Rajab, in February along with family members and two medics who came to rescue her from under Israeli fire.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO)\uc2  says more than 10,000 patients requiring urgent medical evacuation have been prevented from leaving Gaza since the Rafah border crossing with Egypt was shut in May. The Palestinian health ministry says nearly 1,000 medics have been killed in Gaza in the past year in what the \uc2 WHO\uc2  called \u8220\'20\'1Can irreplaceable loss and a massive blow to the health system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The statement said the treatment of both Palestinian detainees in Israel and hostages seized by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  fighters in the 7 October attack had been investigated and it accused both sides of involvement in torture and sexual violence.\par \par \uc2 The Commission of Inquiry (CoI) has a broad mandate to collect evidence and identify suspected perpetrators of international crimes committed in Israel and the occupied Palestinian territories. It bases its findings on a range of sources including interviews with victims and witnesses, submissions and satellite imagery.\par \par \uc2 The CoI has previously alleged that both Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  committed war crimes in the early stages of the Gaza war, and that Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions also constituted crimes against humanity because of the immense civilian losses. The term is reserved for the most serious international crimes knowingly committed as part of a widespread or systematic attack against civilians.\par \par \uc2 Israel has not cooperated with the inquiry, which it says has an anti-Israel bias. The CoI has accused Israel of obstructing its work and preventing investigators from accessing both Israel and the Palestinian territories, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, the evidence gathered by such \uc2 UN\uc2 -mandated bodies has formed the basis for war crimes prosecutions and could be drawn on by the international criminal court.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gulf states urging US to stop Israel from bombing Iran's oil sites - Reuters' sources\par \par \uc2 Gulf states are lobbying Washington to stop Israel from attacking Iran\u8217\'20\'19 s oil sites because they are concerned their own oil facilities could come under fire from Tehran \u8217\'20\'19s proxies if the conflict escalates, three Gulf sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 As part of their attempts to avoid being caught in the crossfire, Gulf states including Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates and Qatar are also refusing to let Israel fly over their airspace for any attack on Iran and have conveyed this to Washington, the three sources close to government circles told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Israel has promised Iran will pay for its missile attack last week while Tehran has said any retaliation would be met with vast destruction, raising fears of a wider war in the region that could suck in the US.\par \par \uc2 During meetings this week, Iran warned Saudi Arabia it could not guarantee the safety of the Gulf kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s oil facilities if Israel were given any assistance in carrying out an attack, a senior Iranian official and an Iranian diplomat told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Ali Shihabi, a Saudi analyst close to the Saudi royal court, said:\par \par \uc2 The Iranians have stated: \u8216\'20\'18If the Gulf states open up their airspace to Israel, that would be an act of war\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The diplomat said Tehran had sent a clear message to Riyadh that its allies in countries such as Iraq or Yemen might respond if there was any regional support for Israel against Iran.\par \par \uc2 A potential Israeli strike was the focus of talks on Wednesday between Saudi de facto ruler, Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman, and Iranian foreign minister \uc2 Abbas Araqchi\uc2 , who was on a Gulf tour to rally support, Gulf and Iranian sources told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The Iranian minister\u8217\'20\'19s visit, along with Saudi-US communications at defence ministry level, are part of a coordinated effort to address the crisis, a Gulf source close to government circles told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 A person in Washington familiar with the discussions confirmed with Reuters that Gulf officials had been in touch with US counterparts to express concern about the potential scope of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s expected retaliation.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the White House declined to comment when asked whether Gulf governments had asked Washington to ensure Israel\u8217\'20\'19s response was measured.\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  spoke on Wednesday about the Israeli retaliation in a call both sides described as positive.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Miranda Bryant is the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Nordic correspondent.\par \par \uc2 A young person has been detained in Sweden after a shooting at an Israeli defence company.\par \par \uc2 Police are investigating the incident, at Elbit Systems Sweden in Kalleb\u228\'00\'E4ck, Gothenburg on Thursday morning, as attempted murder and aggravated weapons offences. Nobody was injured.\par \par \uc2 Swedish broadcaster SVT {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.svt.se/nyheter/lokalt/vast/stor-polisinsats-vid-elbit-i-goteborg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that the young person who was held could be as young as 12. Police have not confirmed an exact age, only that they were under 15.\par \par \uc2 Police were alerted to the shooting at 9.30am on Thursday. They later found a bag belonging to the boy and the national bomb squad was called but it was found not to contain anything dangerous.\par \par \uc2 Police spokesperson, August Brandt, said:\par \par \uc2 We can confirm that a shooting has taken place here. Thankfully, no one was physically injured.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unfil reminds Israel of obligations after two \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers injured by \uc2 IDF\uc2  fire on \uc2 UN\uc2  positions in Lebanon\par \par \uc2 Unifil, the \uc2 UN\uc2 -peacekeeping force in Lebanon, was said it is following up with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military after, it said, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at \uc2 UN\uc2  positions and two peacekeepers were injured and hospitalised.\par \par \uc2 In a lengthy statement, the peacekeeping force, which was established in 1978 in the wake of the \u8220\'20\'1Ccoastal road massacre\u8221\'20\'1D and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/02/archive-1978-israeli-triple-thrust-rips-into-lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Operation Litani}}}\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 Recent escalation along the Blue Line is causing widespread destruction of towns and villages in south Lebanon, while rockets continue to be launched towards Israel, including civilian areas.\par \par \uc2 In the past days we have seen incursions from Israel into Lebanon in Naqoura and other areas. \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (IDF) soldiers have clashed with \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  elements on the ground in Lebanon. Unifil\u8217\'20\'19s Naqoura headquarters and nearby positions have been repeatedly hit.\par \par \uc2 This morning, two peacekeepers were injured after an IDF Merkava tank fired its weapon toward an observation tower at Unifil\u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Naqoura, directly hitting it and causing them to fall. The injuries are fortunately, this time, not serious, but they remain in hospital.\par \par \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers also fired on \uc2 UN\uc2  position (UNP) 1-31 in Labbouneh, hitting the entrance to the bunker where peacekeepers were sheltering, and damaging vehicles and a communications system. An IDF drone was observed flying inside the \uc2 UN\uc2  position up to the bunker entrance.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 IDF\uc2  soldiers deliberately fired at and disabled the position\u8217\'20\'19s perimeter-monitoring cameras. They also deliberately fired on UNP 1-32A in Ras Naqoura, where regular Tripartite meetings were held before the conflict began, damaging lighting and a relay station.\par \par \uc2 The statement continued:\par \par \uc2 We remind the \uc2 IDF\uc2  and all actors of their obligations to ensure the safety and security of \uc2 UN\uc2  personnel and property and to respect the inviolability of \uc2 UN\uc2  premises at all times. UNIFIL peacekeepers are present in south Lebanon to support a return to stability under security council mandate.\par \par \uc2 Any deliberate attack on peacekeepers is a grave violation of international humanitarian law and of Security Council resolution 1701. We are following up with the \uc2 IDF\uc2  on these matters.\par \par \uc2 Security council resolution 1701 was passed in 2006, and intended to resolve the 2006 Lebanon war, by calling for a full cessation of hostilities between \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and Israel, and that only the Lebanese army and the Unifil force have a presence between the blue line separating Israel and Lebanon and the Litani River, about 30km north of the blue line. Israel has criticised Lebanese authorities for failing to fully implement the resolution.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports there was no immediate comment from the Israeli military after the Unifil statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Palestinian and Dutch organisations on Thursday filed a legal complaint against the state of the Netherlands over its alleged failure to prevent Israel from committing possible genocide in Gaza and other violations of international law.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports the case argues that the Netherlands has a legal obligation to do everything in its power to stop alleged violations of international law and the 1948 Genocide Convention by Israel.\par \par \uc2 It is backed by Palestinian human rights organisations, Dutch social justice NGOs and Jewish organisations, who do not support the Israeli government.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Rankin is the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Brussels correspondent\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  staff have stepped up their criticism over Europe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinaction\u8221\'20\'1D in response to the Israel-Gaza war, in a letter calling on the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s senior officials to start a dialogue with them aimed at changing course on the Middle East crisis.\par \par \uc2 The group EU Staff for Peace & Justice said that as of September, 1,748 civil servants had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://eustaff4peace.eu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed a letter}}}\uc2  to the presidents of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , European Council and European parliament lamenting \u8220\'20\'1Chow little (if anything) the \uc2 EU\uc2  is doing to address the dire humanitarian crisis in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D. The group said it had yet to receive a response from any of the leaders, despite a statement from a Commission spokesperson in June claiming that a dialogue had been initiated with staff.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, dozens of staff gathered outside the Commission\u8217\'20\'19s Berlaymont headquarters during their lunch break to mark this week\u8217\'20\'19s one-year anniversary of the conflict, which began with the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks of 7 October.\par \par \uc2 enltrEU staff protest in pouring rain over union\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cinaction\u8221\'20\'1D over Israel/Gaza war. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6i4HvDHSPG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6i4HvDHSPG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jennifer Rankin (@JenniferMerode) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JenniferMerode/status/1844334683460600187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 After the protest, staff planned to send a follow-up letter to von der Leyen calling for talks with EU staff.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the Commission\u8217\'20\'19s June statement of having started a dialogue, the staff group wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough we are happy to hear of this willingness on the behalf of the Commission, no such dialogue with EU Staff for Peace and Justice has yet been initiated by the institution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group has requested a meeting to discuss the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in bringing about a ceasefire; ensuring the \uc2 EU\uc2  abides by fundamental values and that its staff and institutions do not become \u8220\'20\'1Cmorally complicit in breaches of international law committed in Gaza, the West Bank, Lebanon and Israel through EU-funded programmes and trade arrangements\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Israel-Gaza war has sharply divided EU member states: Hungary and the Czech Republic are Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strongest supporters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/22/significant-spain-norway-ireland-recognition-state-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 while Spain, Ireland and non-EU Norway have recognised the Palestinian state. }}}\par \par \uc2 The original letter was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/24/more-than-200-eu-staff-sign-letter-expressing-concerns-over-gaza-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  sent to von der Leyen and other top officials in May}}}\uc2 , signed by staff in their personal capacity as citizens. \u8220\'20\'1CTo stand idly by in the face of such an erosion of the international rule of law would mean failing the European project\u8221\'20\'1D envisaged by those who constructed it after world war two, the letter said. It has since been resent multiple times as signatories have increased, according to organisers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Patrick Wintour is diplomatic editor for the \uc2 Guardian\par \par \uc2 The Labour government in the UK should end its half-hearted half measures towards Israel if \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is to be stopped from pushing the world off a cliff, Husam Zomlot the Palestinian ambassador to the UK said on Thursday at a briefing to mark the anniversary of the Gaza conflict.\par \par \uc2 He said the lack of accountability of Israel for its actions is threatening to weaken the whole world, and countries such as the UK that are renowned for their support for international humanitarian law have to go further.\par \par \uc2 He called for a full arms embargo, recognition of Palestine as a state and economic sanctions that \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantle the apparatus of illegal settlements in the West Bank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said \u8220\'20\'1Cthis unconditional support for Israel by the US and western Europe is not bringing peace to Israel, security to Israel. It is literally pushing Israel and the region \u8211\'20\'13 and perhaps the world \u8211\'20\'13 off a cliff. There is no accountability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lesson to everyone else will be clear, international law and the global rules based on these prohibitions against war crimes and atrocities, and the famine of 2.3 million people are meaningless if we do not end it in Gaza. This very starkly is where we are headed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said half measures are not going to get Israel to agree to the \uc2 UN\uc2  resolution calling for a ceasefire and enforcement of the rulings of the \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2 . He added he could not understand why the UK had abstained at the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council on the enforcement of ICJ ruling directing Israel to leave the occupied territories in a year, pointing out that the UK had said it agreed with the ICJ opinion.\par \par \uc2 He said it was clear that the partial arms embargo imposed by the UK was having no effect. He pointed out that the \uc2 UK government\uc2  has said it is willing to recognise Palestine when it is most effective to do so, and he could not think of a more effective moment to do so than now.\par \par \uc2 He insisted the Palestinian aspiration was \u8220\'20\'1Cto live in peace and dignity just like everyone else, it\u8217\'20\'19s as simple and human as that. And what does Israel want? Do they know? What\u8217\'20\'19s the endgame?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael is engaged in a war not to defend itself or its people, but to defend its illegal occupation, and this includes a war on demolishing the entire global rules based order. Israel\u8217\'20\'19s strategic outlook is entirely dominated by the use of sheer military power to impose its will, rather than the compromises to reach any agreement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unifil says its HQ and nearby positions in southern Lebanon have been 'repeatedly hit'\par \par \uc2 United Nations peacekeepers\u8217\'20\'19 headquarters and nearby positions in southern Lebanon have been repeatedly hit amid recent escalation along the blue line, Unifil said in a statement on Thursday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Unifil added that two peacekeepers were injured by Israeli tank fire.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The director of Kamal Adwan hospital said eight patients, mostly children, were at risk inside the intensive care units should the Israeli army force them to evacuate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose children were injured with shrapnel all over their bodies, the upper parts and the brain. They are all in critical conditions and are hooked to oxygen systems,\u8221\'20\'1D Abu Safiya said in a video message to the media, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe hospital is also running out of fuel, and the occupation is refusing fuel to reach northern Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Abu Safiya appealed to world countries to press Israel to allow medical staffers in north Gaza \u8217\'20\'19s three hospitals to continue to operate saying:\par \par \uc2 Our message is a message of peace for the sake of those children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe urge the world to allow us to continue (working) and permit all things needed so that we can provide safe medical care in northern Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Israeli bombardment near Kamal Adwan hospital has already caused some damage to the facility, medics said. Officials said they know of many fatalities lying on the roads outside the hospital because of Israeli fire.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Death toll from Israel strike on school shelter rises\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that the death toll from an Israeli airstrike on a school sheltering displaced people in central Gaza has reached at least 28 people, including women and children. Earlier, Palestinian medical officials said the strike had killed at least 21 people on Thursday, with the toll likely to rise ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6707af8c8f08d77e388ba953#block-6707af8c8f08d77e388ba953"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see 11.44am BST}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Additionally, three hospitals in the north were told to evacuate putting patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives at risk, medics say. The strike, in which many more were injured, happened in the city of Deir Al-Balah.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said on Thursday it had carried out a \u8220\'20\'1Cprecise strike on terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D, who had a command and control centre embedded in a school.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a further example of the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorist organization\u8217\'20\'19s systemic abuse of civilian infrastructure in violation of international law,\u8221\'20\'1D the military statement said.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  denies such allegations. Medics said 54 other people were injured at the school.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that in the north of the territory, the Israeli military is pushing on with an offensive begun six days ago, when it sent its troops into Jabalia, the largest of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s eight historic refugee camps and the nearby towns of Beit Hanoun and Beit Lahiya.\par \par \uc2 Palestinian health officials say at least 130 people have been killed so far in the operation, which Israel says is aimed at preventing \uc2 Hamas\uc2  from regrouping. The military has told residents to evacuate an area in which the \uc2 UN\uc2  estimates more than 400,000 people are trapped.\par \par \uc2 The health officials said the Israeli military on Wednesday gave patients and medics 24 hours to leave the Indonesian, Al-Awda and Kamal Adwan hospitals or risk being stormed as happened earlier in the war at the Al Shifa hospital in Gaza City.\par \par \uc2 Israel, which has not yet commented on evacuation orders for medical facilities, has said \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has command facilities embedded in the hospitals, which it denies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli troops fire at 3 Unifil positions in southern Lebanon, \uc2 UN\uc2  source says\par \par \uc2 Israeli troops opened fire at three positions held by \uc2 UN\uc2  peacekeepers in southern Lebanon on Thursday, a \uc2 UN\uc2  source told Reuters, without immediately being able to specify the type of fire.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that the source said one of the locations that was fired at was Unifil \u8217\'20\'19s main base at Naqoura.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44am BST\par \par \uc2 An Israeli airstrike on a former school in Gaza that was sheltering displaced people on Thursday targeted militants who were operating in the compound, the Israeli military said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPrior to the strike, numerous steps were taken to mitigate the risk of harming civilians, including the use of precise munitions, aerial surveillance, and additional intelligence,\u8221\'20\'1D the military said.\par \par \uc2 Palestinian medical officials said the strike had killed at least 21 people on Thursday, with the toll likely to rise. On X, the \uc2 Palestine Red Crescent Society\uc2  (PRCS) said it had responded to 27 fatalities and 54 injuries after the strike on the school turned shelter in Deir al-Balah ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-6707aac28f08d77e388ba913#block-6707aac28f08d77e388ba913"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see 11.32am BST}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am BST\par \par \uc2 27 killed and more than 50 injured after Israeli attack on school turned shelter\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Palestine Red Crescent Society\uc2  (PRCS) says it has responded to 27 fatalities and 54 injuries after an Israeli strike on a school turned shelter in Deir al-Balah.\par \par \uc2 enltr?? Palestine Red Crescent teams responded to 27 fatalities and 54 injuries following the Israeli occupation army\u8217\'20\'19s targeting of Rafida School, located near the \uc2 Palestine Red Crescent Society\uc2  headquarters in Deir Al-Balah, in central {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Gaza?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Gaza}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QrsnxOfHHi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QrsnxOfHHi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 PRCS (@PalestineRCS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PalestineRCS/status/1844315926868656285?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Palestinian medical officials said the strike had killed at least 21 people on Thursday, with the toll likely to rise ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/10/middle-east-crisis-israel-gaza-iran-us-lebanon-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-67079f308f08d77e388ba874#block-67079f308f08d77e388ba874"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see 10.36am BST}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am BST\par \par \uc2 More than 42,065 Palestinians killed in Gaza since 7 October 2023, says health ministry\par \par \uc2 More than 42,065 Palestinians have been killed and 97,886 injured in Israel \u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza since 7 October 2023, the Gaza health ministry said in a statement on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The ministry does not distinguished not distinguish between militant and civilian deaths.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian organisations including \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2 , \uc2 Oxfam\uc2  and \uc2 War on Want\uc2  have called on the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to stop all arms transfers to Israel, as the bombardment of Lebanon and Gaza worsens more than a year into the conflict.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe escalation of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on Lebanon underscore our concerns and the need for the \uc2 UK government\uc2  to immediately suspend all weapons licences to Israel, and ensure it is not complicit in atrocities,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter says. It adds:\par \par \uc2 Despite the UK\u8217\'20\'19s partial suspension of arms licences to Israel, Israeli forces continue to commit apparently unlawful activities against Palestinians in both the Gaza Strip and the West Bank.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other signatories include Action Aid UK, the \uc2 Campaign Against Arms Trade\uc2  (\uc2 CAAT\uc2 ) and the International Centre of Justice for Palestinians, among others.\par \par \uc2 In September, the UK implemented a partial ban on export licenses to Israel after a review by the Foreign Office found a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear risk\u8221\'20\'1D that UK arms may have been used in violation of humanitarian law. The suspension included components for military aircraft, helicopters, drones and targeting equipment.\par \par \uc2 Campaigners however have criticised the government\u8217\'20\'19s decision to exclude all UK components for the F-35 fighter jet programme, which signatories have said make up 15% of every aircraft used by Israel.\par \par \uc2 The Labour government has previously said the components are exempted because they belong to a global programme which the UK does not have unilateral control over the components, which are sent to the US. They will not be exempt, the government said, on the rare occasion where the part is sent directly to Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  says it has destroyed Israeli tank advancing on Lebanon's southern border\par \par \uc2 Lebanese militant group Hezbollah\uc2  said it destroyed an Israeli tank advancing on Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s southern border on Thursday, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 The Iran -backed group fired rockets at \u8220\'20\'1Can Israeli tank as it advanced towards Ras al-Naqura, leading to its burning and destruction,\u8221\'20\'1D it said, claiming casualties. No other details were reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli strike on school turned shelter kills at least 21 Palestinians, medical officials say\par \par \uc2 An Israeli strike on a school sheltering displaced people in Gaza killed at least 21 people on Thursday, with the toll likely to rise, Palestinian medical officials said.\par \par \uc2 The Al-Aqsa Martyrs hospital in the central town of Deir al-Balah confirmed the toll, and an Associated Press (AP) reporter counted the bodies.\par \par \uc2 Witnesses say the strike on Thursday appeared to target a makeshift post staffed by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  -run police inside the school.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from the Israeli military.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Diplomatic communications have intensified in the past hours, before a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council meeting discussing the situation in the Middle East, Lebanon \u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Najib Mikati\uc2  said in a statement on X on Thursday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are contacts taking place between the United States and France with the aim of reviving a ceasefire declaration for a specific period in order to resume the search for political solutions,\u8221\'20\'1D he was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Irish PM says he is hopeful of Middle East ceasefire after meeting with Biden\par \par \uc2 Ireland \u8217\'20\'19s prime minister has said he is hopeful of a ceasefire in the Middle East after an hour long meeting with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Washington last night.\par \par \uc2 Simon Harris said the US president told him he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery lengthy\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and he was left \u8220\'20\'1Cin no doubt that this was a conversation of substances and of depth in terms of actions that Israel need to take in terms of aid, humanitarian aid, in terms of bringing about a ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrGood to meet with President of the United States tonight in the Oval Office. We marked 100 years of diplomatic relations between our two countries. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ytwHXYf1ev"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ytwHXYf1ev}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Harris TD (@SimonHarrisTD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonHarrisTD/status/1844147488703512583?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The taoiseach told reporters that he was clear that \u8220\'20\'1Cproportionality has been completely and utterly lost by the Netanyahu government\u8221\'20\'1D and the number of civilians, including children \u8220\'20\'1Cneedlessly dying\u8221\'20\'1D was \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said he also thanked the president, who he spoke to on Monday night, for his intervention over the positioning of Israeli artillery adjacent to an Irish peace keeping post on the blue line, the de facto border between Lebanon and Israel.\par \par \uc2 They also discussed the \u8220\'20\'1Cthuggery of Putin\u8221\'20\'1D and Northern Ireland.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Israel \u8217\'20\'19s military said it had \u8220\'20\'1Celiminated\u8221\'20\'1D a \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  member in Syria who it claimed had relayed intelligence against Israel in the Israeli-occupied Golan Heights, reports Reuters. Meanwhile, Syrian media reported on Thursday that Israeli airstrikes hit targets in Syria.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the Israeli military said on Thursday it had eliminated two \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  commanders in southern Lebanon and its fighter jets attacked ammunition depots in the Beirut area and ammunition depots and other military infrastructures in southern Lebanon on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Defense Force\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) said on Wednesday it had eliminated Adham Jahout, a member of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CGolan terrorist network\u8221\'20\'1D in the area of Quneitra in Syria.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IDF\uc2  said Jahout\u8217\'20\'19s role was to relay information from Syrian regime sources to \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and transmit intelligence gathered on the Syrian front to facilitate operations against Israel in the Golan Heights.\par \par \uc2 Syrian state TV said early on Thursday that Israel had carried out airstrikes targeting an industrial site in the Syrian city of Homs and a military site in the countryside near the city of Ham a, causing \u8220\'20\'1Csome material damage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The strikes targeted a car manufacturing plant in Homs and caused a fire, Syrian TV said, citing the director of the industrial site, Amer Khalil.\par \par \uc2 Explosions were also heard in the area of Darayya and were being investigated, state media reported.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said on Wednesday it had intercepted a drone that approached Israel over the Red Sea but did not cross into Israeli territory, minutes after the Islamic Resistance in Iraq said it had targeted Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Eilat with drones.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21am BST\par \par \uc2 At least 400,000 people trapped by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s latest Gaza offensive, says \uc2 Unrwa\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of civilians in Gaza remain trapped by the latest Israeli offensive centred on Jabaliya refugee camp, according to \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies and human rights groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt least 400,000 people are trapped in the area,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , the head of the \uc2 UN Palestinian refugee agency\uc2 , \uc2 Unrwa\uc2 , posted on X on Wednesday, amid witness accounts of bodies lying uncollected in the streets because of the renewed fighting.\par \par \uc2 enltrNorthern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Gaza?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Gaza}}}\uc2  : no end to hell.\par \par \uc2 At least 400,000 people are trapped in the area.\par \par \uc2 Recent evacuation orders from the Israeli Authorities are forcing people to flee again & again, especially from Jabalia Camp.\par \par \uc2 Many are refusing because they know too well that no place anywhere\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2  (@UNLazzarini) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UNLazzarini/status/1843892602757669067?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRecent evacuation orders from the Israeli authorities are forcing people to flee again and again, especially from Jabaliya camp,\u8221\'20\'1D added Lazzarini. \u8220\'20\'1CMany are refusing because they know too well that no place anywhere in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  is safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military says the large-scale raid, now in its fifth day, is intended to stop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2  fighters staging further attacks from Jabaliya and to prevent them regrouping, as at least 60 people were killed in Israeli military strikes on Gaza on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Lazzarini said some \uc2 Unrwa\uc2  shelters and services were being forced to shut down for the first time since the war began and that with almost no basic supplies available, hunger was spreading again in northern Gaza. \u8220\'20\'1CThis recent military operation also threatens the implementation of the second phase of the #polio vaccination campaign for children,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Israel did not immediately comment on Lazzarini\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. Israeli authorities have previously said they facilitate food deliveries to Gaza despite challenging conditions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59am BST\par \par \uc2 A Liberia -flagged tanker was struck by an unidentified projectile in the Red Sea about 73 nautical miles (135 kilometres) southwest of the Yemeni port of Hodeidah, British security firm Ambrey said on Thursday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations agency (UKMTO) said separately that it had received a report of an incident in the same area, adding authorities are investigating.\par \par \uc2 enltrUKMTO WARNING - INCIDENT 127 - ATTACK - UPDATE 002 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZgjRM6s03v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZgjRM6s03v}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MaritimeSecurity?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MaritimeSecurity}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MarSec?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MarSec}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QF1trwgIg7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QF1trwgIg7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations (UKMTO) (@UK_MTO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UK_MTO/status/1844238328830537951?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 10, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The chemical/products tanker, en route from Saudi Arabia \u8217\'20\'19s Jeddah to Muscat in Oman was struck on its starboard side. The projectile hit the bridge causing minor damage, Ambrey said.\par \par \uc2 Approximately four hours later, two additional projectiles reportedly detonated within 0.27 nautical miles of the vessel\u8217\'20\'19s port side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmbrey assessed the vessel to have a strong affiliation with the Houthi targeting profile,\u8221\'20\'1D Ambrey said, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Houthi fighters in Yemen have carried out nearly 100 attacks on ships crossing the Red Sea since November and say they are acting in solidarity with Palestinians in Israel \u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza. They have sunk two vessels, seized another and killed at least four seafarers, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The master of the Liberia-flagged vessel reported the tanker was hit by three projectiles, sustaining damage, but no fires or casualties were reported, UKMTO said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The crew are reported safe and the vessel is proceeding to its next port of call, the statement added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera accuses Israel of deliberately targeting journalists after reporter death and others injured\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera has accused Israel of deliberately targeting journalists after one of its cameramen was shot and critically injured by an Israeli sniper on Wednesday while a photojournalist for another network was killed and a third also injured while covering the siege of Jabalia camp in northern Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In a statement the Qatar -based broadcaster said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 The Israeli occupation forces targeted a number of journalists working in and around Jabalia camp in the Gaza Strip this afternoon, killing one of the cameramen, and seriously injuring Al Jazeera Arabic Channel\u8217\'20\'19s cameraman Fadi Al Wahidi with a bullet to his neck, causing critical injury while covering the attack on the camp \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 This incident marks yet another grave violation against journalists in Gaza, where Israeli forces have been increasingly hostile toward media workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2  affiliated TV channel al-Aqsa said on Telegram that one of its photojournalists, Mohammad al-Tanani, had been killed in an Israeli attack in Jabalia refugee camp on Wednesday, while its journalist Tamer Labad, was injured.\par \par \uc2 Two days earlier, another Al Jazeera cameraman, Ali Al-Attar, was also critically injured in an Israeli attack on a hospital in northern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hossam Shabat, one of the few remaining journalists in the area, said his colleagues Al Wahidi and Labad were in critical condition. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are in critical condition, and not much treatment is available for them here. Please pray for them and for us,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a post on X.\par \par \uc2 enltrFadi Alwahdi and Tamer Lobod are both journalists who were targeted in the north today. They are in critical condition, and not much treatment is available for them here. Please pray for them and for us. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rAzJahY3lk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rAzJahY3lk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ???? ???? (@HossamShabat) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HossamShabat/status/1844120137722626405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera reporter Anas al-Sharif wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnasAlSharif0/status/1844051066309976302"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another post}}}\uc2  that Al Wahidi, who had been wearing a press vest, \u8220\'20\'1Csustained severe injuries to his neck vertebrae and spinal cord. According to hospital specialists, he urgently requires surgery, and there is a risk of partial paralysis due to the extent of the damage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: The \uc2 Al Jazeera\uc2  crew came under fire from Israeli occupation forces, with our dear cameraman, Fadi Al-Wahidi, being shot in the neck by a sniper while covering the siege of Jabalia camp. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vtP37hlDq4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vtP37hlDq4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??? ?????? Anas Al-Sharif (@AnasAlSharif0) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnasAlSharif0/status/1844022011997352162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Al-Sharif also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ImadZakout/status/1844058518879629606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted footage}}}\uc2  that he said was the last thing filmed by Al Wahidi before he was shot, in which the journalist can be seen running while shots are fired.\par \par \uc2 It was not possible to verify the circumstances of the Israeli attacks as Israel does not allow foreign journalists into Gaza. However Israel has previously been accused of deliberately targeting journalists, which it denies.\par \par \uc2 Israel has not commented on the latest attacks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Israel says Iran strike will be 'deadly, precise, surprising'\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19 s defence minister has warned its next strike on Iran will be \u8220\'20\'1Cdeadly, precise and surprising\u8221\'20\'1D, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 Yoav Gallant issued the warning in a video message on Israeli media on Wednesday night, broadcast after he postponed a scheduled trip to Washington, and a few hours after the conversation between \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhoever attacks us will be hurt and will pay a price. Our attack will be deadly, precise and above all surprising, they will not understand what happened and how it happened, they will see the results,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 iwrtl????: ?????? ???? ?????? ???????? ???? ??????, ?????? ?????? ?????? - ?? ?? ????? ?? ??? ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Doron_Kadosh?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Doron_Kadosh}}}\par \par \uc2 (?????: ???? ????) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FOJwaCJAXP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FOJwaCJAXP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??? (@GLZRadio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GLZRadio/status/1844058019988111637?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 9, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17am BST\par \par \uc2 US calls on Israel to urgently address \u8216\'20\'18catastrophic conditions\u8217\'20\'19 in Gaza\par \par \uc2 Israel needs to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/09/at-least-400000-people-trapped-by-israels-latest-gaza-offensive-says-unrwa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urgently address \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic conditions\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  among Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip and stop \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying suffering\u8221\'20\'1D by limiting aid deliveries, the US has told the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 These catastrophic conditions were predicted months ago, and yet, have still not been addressed. That must change, and now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also warned Israel against trying to permanently expel Palestinians from Gaza or seize any territory for itself. \u8220\'20\'1CThere must be no demographic or territorial change in the Gaza Strip, including any actions that reduce the territory of Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas-Greenfield said.\par \par \uc2 Despite a year of relentless Israeli attacks on Gaza, and intermittent declarations by the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) and other officials claiming to have defeated \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , Israeli tanks and infantry attacked northern Gaza for a third time in force earlier this week, claiming the action was necessary to prevent \uc2 Hamas\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cregrouping\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of civilians in Gaza remain trapped by the latest Israeli offensive centred on Jabalia refugee camp, according to \uc2 UN\uc2  agencies and human rights groups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHundreds of thousands of people are again being pushed to move to the south, where living conditions are intolerable,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , the head of the \uc2 UN Palestinian refugee agency\uc2  (\uc2 Unrwa\uc2 ), told the security council.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 Yet again, Gazans are teetering on the edge of a man-made famine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  has long complained of obstacles to getting aid into Gaza and distributing it during the war. Reuters reported last week that food supplies to Gaza have fallen sharply in recent weeks because Israeli authorities have introduced a new customs rule on some humanitarian aid and are separately scaling down deliveries organised by businesses.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador \uc2 Danny Danon\uc2  defended his country\u8217\'20\'19s record:\par \par \uc2 Israel imposes no restrictions on humanitarian aid. In fact, 82% of all requests for humanitarian coordination have been approved and implemented.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden urges Netanyahu to \u8216\'20\'18minimise harm to civilians\u8217\'20\'19 in Lebanon\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  have spoken for the first time in weeks on Wednesday amid expectations of an imminent Israeli strike on Iran. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also joined the call.\par \par \uc2 In its readout of the call, the White House said the US president emphasised \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need to minimize harm to civilians, in particular in the densely populated areas of Beirut\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The readout did not directly mention possible retaliation for the Iranian missile strike but said Biden had condemned Tehran \u8217\'20\'19s attack \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally\u8221\'20\'1D and pledged \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 The president affirmed his ironclad commitment to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security. He condemned unequivocally Iran\u8217\'20\'19s ballistic missile attack against Israel on October 1st.\par \par \uc2 On Lebanon, the president emphasised the need for a diplomatic arrangement to safely return both Lebanese and Israeli civilians to their homes on both sides of the Blue Line. The president affirmed Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to protect its citizens from \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , which has fired thousands of missiles and rockets into Israel over the past year alone, while emphasising the need to minimise harm to civilians, in particular in the densely populated areas of Beirut.\par \par \uc2 On Gaza, the leaders discussed the urgent need to renew diplomacy to release the hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . The president also discussed the humanitarian situation in Gaza and the imperative to restore access to the north, including by reinvigorating the corridor from Jordan immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The timing and scope of the Israeli retaliation is still unclear, and a miscalculation could propel Iran and Israel into a full-scale war, which neither side says it wants. The US, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s staunch ally, is wary of being drawn into the fighting, and of oil price shocks.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is keen to weigh in on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s plans and avoid surprises like the Israeli killing of the \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  leader, \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 , although the Wall Street Journal reported that Israel had so far refused to share details.\par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s deadly bombardment across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2  has killed at least 1,200 civilians while forcibly displacing 1.2 million residents. Across the country, thousands of Syrian refugees, in addition to Lebanese residents, have fled into Syria in recent days in attempts to escape Israeli airstrikes.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has previously also asked Israel to minimize civilian casualties in Gaza where Israeli forces have killed more than 43,000 Palestinians while displacing nearly 2 million in the territory. The Biden administration has also spent a record $17.9bn in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/7058551/us-record-military-aid-israel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 military aid}}}\uc2  to Israel since last October.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 The US has told the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council that Israel needs to urgently address \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic conditions\u8221\'20\'1D among Palestinian civilians in the besieged Gaza Strip and stop \u8220\'20\'1Cintensifying suffering\u8221\'20\'1D by limiting aid deliveries, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Referring to reports of squalid conditions in south and central Gaza, US ambassador to the UN \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 These catastrophic conditions were predicted months ago, and yet, have still not been addressed. That must change, and now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also warned Israel against trying to permanently expel Palestinians from Gaza or seize any territory for itself. \u8220\'20\'1CThere must be no demographic or territorial change in the Gaza Strip, including any actions that reduce the territory of Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D Thomas-Greenfield said.\par \par \uc2 Separately, members of the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council also warned Israel against proceeding with a law aimed at curbing the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Palestinian refugees agency (\uc2 Unrwa\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Israel has long been at odds with \uc2 Unrwa\uc2  and alleged, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/22/israel-unrwa-staff-terrorist-links-yet-to-provide-evidence-colonna-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without providing any evidence}}}\uc2 , that 12 of its thousands of employees were involved in the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks.\par \par \uc2 More on that in a moment. First here is a summary of other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  office for the coordination of humanitarian affairs (OCHA) has published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/lebanon/lebanon-flash-update-33-escalation-hostilities-lebanon-7-october-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a flash update about the latest situation in Lebanon}}}\uc2  which says one quarter of Lebanese territory is now under Israeli military displacement orders. It said \u8220\'20\'1CLebanon\u8217\'20\'19s humanitarian crisis is deteriorating at an alarming rate\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1CIsraeli airstrikes have not only intensified but also expanded\u8221\'20\'1D and have \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly targeted critical civilian infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Five members of Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s civil defence were killed in an Israeli airstrike on their base in the town of Dardghaya, south {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2 , on Wednesday night. Pictures of the strike show burnt cars with civil defence written on the side of it, crumpled from the force of the blast as efforts to locate survivors and bodies remain ongoing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Canada will provide C$15m ($11m) in humanitarian assistance to Lebanese civilians who have been affected by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing strikes across the country. In a statement reported by Reuters on Wednesday, Canada\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister \uc2 M\u233\'00\'E9lanie Joly\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CCanada is deeply alarmed by the rapid escalation of the crisis in Lebanon. We are mobilising to ensure that Canada is there to bring much-needed assistance to the Lebanese people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The governor of Akkar, in the far north of Lebanon, has said there are obstacles to deliveringaid to the people who have sought refuge there after being internally displaced by Israeli strikes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hezbollahhas said its fighters have fired rockets and artillery shells \u8220\'20\'1Cas Israeli troops tried to advance in the Mays al-Jabal area from several directions\u8221\'20\'1D. The group added that \u8220\'20\'1Cclashes are ongoing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israeli strikes have killed five people and injured at least 12 in the Lebanese town ofWardiniyeh, about 40 kilometres south of Beirut, Al Jazeera reported, noting that the area is not one Israel has tried to empty of its residents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the BBC about Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s devastation caused by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks in the past year, \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , chief of the main \uc2 UN\uc2  aid relief organisation in Gaza, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are becoming wordless.\u8221\'20\'1D Lazzarini added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe soon have exhausted all our vocabulary to try to describe what has become a wasteland \u8230\'20\'26 an unliveable area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Palestinian news agency Wafa reports that the number of Palestinians killed by Israeli attacks inside the Gaza Strip on Wednesday has risen to 60. This includes an incident where it reported \u8220\'20\'1C15 civilians were killed today when the Israeli occupation forces bombed the tents of displaced people in Jabalia\u8221\'20\'1D. It has not been possible for journalists to independently verify the casualty figures being issued during the conflict.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) has ordered the closure once again of several hospitals in northern Gaza, including the Kamal Adwan, Indonesia and al-Awda hospitals. The Al Mezan Center for Human Rights described the situation as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeja vu\u8221\'20\'1D on social media, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe all know the horrors that follow such orders\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The International Rescue Committee (IRC) warned that after a year of conflict, as many as 51,000 children in Gaza could be unaccompanied or separated from their parents or caregivers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Al Jazeera has released a statement condemning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  for the killing of one of its camera operators and injuring another while they were working in Jabalia refugee camp in Gaza. \u8220\'20\'1CThe deliberate targeting of journalists is a flagrant violation of international laws protecting the press and humanitarian workers in war zones,\u8221\'20\'1D the network said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two Israelis were killed in Kiryat Shmona in the north-east of Israel after it was reported to have been hit by a rocket barrage from Hezbollah. Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military says it has destroyed the launcher used for the attack.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry spokesperson Maria Zakharova has been highly critical of Israel, saying Benjamin Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s government had a desire \u8220\'20\'1Cexpand the geography of armed escalation in the region\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241024ekao002pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
