\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Virginia candidate fired by Trump warns of Republican plans to politicize federal jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Woodbridge, Virginia \par \uc2 1,421 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2024\par 19:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Little-known policy embraced by Trump and included in Project 2025 would transform previously nonpartisan jobs\par \par \uc2 The Democrat Eugene Vindman stood before a group of roughly 30 fellow veterans and warned of an impending danger if Republicans like his opponent, Derrick Anderson, won key House races next month: a little-known policy called schedule F.\par \par \uc2 The policy, initially embraced by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the final months of his first term in office and now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/project-2025-trump-plan-fire-civil-service-employees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 included}}}\uc2  in the rightwing manifesto known as Project 2025, would transform previously nonpartisan jobs in the federal government into political appointments. The change could fundamentally alter and perhaps jeopardize the employment of tens or even hundreds of thousands of government workers, including 14% of the residents in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crsreports.congress.gov/product/pdf/R/R47716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh district}}}\uc2 , where Vindman is running for Congress.\par \par \uc2 Vindman knows something about the politicization of government posts. In 2020, Trump fired Vindman and his twin brother, Alexander Vindman, after they played a key role in the former president\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment. The brothers, who both held senior positions on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s national security council, raised alarms about the then president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged attempt to pressure Ukraine to launch an investigation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his son Hunter. They were both dismissed days after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment trial concluded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis idea of politicizing the civil service \u8211\'20\'13 I know that means a lot to the people in this room,\u8221\'20\'1D Vindman told the veterans at his campaign event. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know how you prevent something like Schedule F and Project 2025 from being implemented? You vote for Democrats up and down the ticket.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Anderson\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to distance himself from Project 2025, Vindman has sought to directly tie his opponent to the most controversial elements of the manifesto. If Republicans win the White House and control of Congress, they could implement Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans to politicize and relocate large numbers of federal employees.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crsreports.congress.gov/product/pdf/R/R47716"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 employs}}}\uc2  more than 2 million civilian workers, roughly 55,000 of whom live in the seventh district. Those jobs can provide steady employment that may pay better than other sectors, particularly for those with lower levels of education. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/999101.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  compiled by the \uc2 US Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , the average hourly wage for a federal employee was $44.20 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/oes/current/oes_nat.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared}}}\uc2  with $31.48 across all occupations.\par \par \uc2 Experts predict that moving government jobs out of Virginia would have devastating economic consequences. Terry Clower, a professor at \uc2 George Mason University\uc2  and director of Mason\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Regional Analysis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/08/30/trump-government-cuts-could-cost-house-republicans-majority-.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  that the policy would cost the state between $27bn-$28bn annually. Vindman predicted a \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor recession\u8221\'20\'1D if federal agencies left the region.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a military service member, but I empathize with the civil servants that are working hard every day on behalf of the American people, and they\u8217\'20\'19re just doing their jobs and being demonized,\u8221\'20\'1D Vindman said.\par \par \uc2 Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s success \u8211\'20\'13 or failure \u8211\'20\'13 to link Anderson with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposed overhaul of the federal workforce could determine the winner of this open seat in a battleground district that will be crucial in deciding the House majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether you\u8217\'20\'19re a Democrat or a Republican, you don\u8217\'20\'19t want your job to be subject to some sort of political loyalty oath,\u8221\'20\'1D Vindman said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re talking about people that are experts in either receiving threats from abroad or just understanding the weather and replacing them with political hacks. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen what that looks like from the White House myself, and it\u8217\'20\'19s profoundly damaging to national security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vindman has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbs19news.com/archives/know-your-ballot-7th-district-democratic-candidate-eugene-vindman/article_3ac4fc33-f44f-5afc-915f-241e0a5baf47.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he never envisioned himself as a politician, but his experience in the Trump administration spurred him to launch a congressional bid after the Democratic incumbent, \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , chose to run for governor rather than seek re-election in the district. Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to speak out against Trump won him some fans among Virginia Democrats and turbocharged his fundraising operation, helping him emerge victorious from a crowded primary in June.\par \par \uc2 David Buckley, a 66-year-old voter who attended the Vets for Vindman event in Woodbridge, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a man of character, somebody who\u8217\'20\'19s willing to step into the breach, so I\u8217\'20\'19m impressed by that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Anderson, a former army green beret turned lawyer, has mocked Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s congressional bid as a \u8220\'20\'1Crevenge tour\u8221\'20\'1D against Trump. Perhaps wary of capitalizing on his national profile, Vindman has not made his clash with Trump a central focus of his campaign, avoiding even mentioning the former president\u8217\'20\'19s name during his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vpm.org/elections/2024-10-03/vindman-anderson-congress-va07-fredericksburg-umw-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate}}}\uc2  against Anderson earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Anderson, like Trump, meanwhile, has pleaded ignorance of Project 2025, saying at the debate this month: \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know about it until my opponent continued to talk about it over and over again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked about the specific proposal to overhaul the federal workforce, Anderson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vpm.org/news/2024-10-10/federal-workers-policy-virginia-seventh-congressional-district-vindman-anderson-subramanyam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the NPR affiliate VPM this month, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to vote for legislation that\u8217\'20\'19s going to remove jobs from our district; bottom line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Anderson\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to distance himself from some of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s most controversial proposals appears to have helped keep the race close, as internal polls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jamesd0wns/status/1843027484889301418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 show}}}\uc2  him and Vindman running neck and neck. The Cook Political Report recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/house/house-overview/house-rating-changes-close-races-nj-07-and-va-07-shift-toward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moved}}}\uc2  the district from \u8220\'20\'1Clean Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss up\u8221\'20\'1D, a reflection of the seat\u8217\'20\'19s increased competitiveness without Spanberger on the ticket.\par \par \uc2 As he has downplayed concerns about Project 2025, Anderson has tried to redirect attention toward issues where Republicans traditionally hold an advantage, namely border security and the economy. Anderson\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, Diego de la Pe\u241\'00\'F1a, said in a statement, \u8220\'20\'1CVindman would continue the failed policies of the past that gave us brutally high prices and an open border. Derrick is focused on the future of this district \u8211\'20\'13 his home district. That means lowering costs, closing the border, and working together to balance the budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This strategy has proven successful here before. In 2021, the Republican governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  carried the district by seven points after Biden won the district by the same margin in the presidential election one year earlier, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/house/house-overview/house-rating-changes-close-races-nj-07-and-va-07-shift-toward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cook Political Report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Youngkin won in part by pitching himself as a less extreme version of Trump, noted Mark Rozell, founding dean of the Schar School of Policy and Government at \uc2 George Mason University\uc2 . Anderson appears to be pursuing a similar approach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo that\u8217\'20\'19s a calling card for Vindman and his campaign: to heighten awareness of Project 2025 and alert federal workers in the district of what potentially could happen should the Republicans win majorities in both houses of Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D Rozell said.\par \par \uc2 Vindman said he has heard from many constituents who have expressed deep concern about the potential effect on the federal workforce if Republicans win next month. Maurice Pettiford, a 63-year-old voter and 20-year veteran of the state department who hosted the Woodbridge event, predicted a policy like schedule F would limit the capabilities of federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the government is going to be effective, you need people with experience. You need people who are going to be loyal to whatever the mission is,\u8221\'20\'1D Pettiford said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn all my years of working, we didn\u8217\'20\'19t care whether [the president] was Democrat or Republican. It was about getting the job done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vindman expects the race to be close, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/generic-ballot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  suggest the House majority could be decided by just a handful of seats. In an encouraging sign for Vindman, Spanberger won her last election in 2022 by about five points, and Virginia Democrats have generally performed better when Trump was on the ballot, Rozell noted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CQuite possibly, the national narrative is what Vindman really is counting on in this campaign, which is: don\u8217\'20\'19t give the Republicans the majority,\u8221\'20\'1D Rozell said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump\u8217\'20\'19s elected especially, make sure the Democrats hold at least one house in Congress. Otherwise Project 2025 could end up being a real thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Biden won Virginia by 10 points in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.roanoke.edu/news/rc_poll_politics_may_2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  conducted before he withdrew from the presidential race suggested he could be in trouble there this year. Since taking over the top of the ticket, surveys have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cnu.edu/wasoncenter/surveys/archive/2024-10-07.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consistently}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aCZ9TJmY2yNRuJyc_cqoE-jL0rx7NDlE/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shown}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading Trump by several points in Virginia, which could help pull Vindman across the finish line as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWill there be a down-ticket benefit for Vindman in an extremely close, contested House race? Quite likely there will be,\u8221\'20\'1D Rozell said. \u8220\'20\'1CWill it be enough? We don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241023ekan0020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
