\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump is anti-worker. Here are 10 of his most shocking anti-worker statements\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,109 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2024\par 13:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The former president actually said that the wages of US workers are \u8216\'20\'18too high\u8217\'20\'19. And that\u8217\'20\'19s far from the worst\par \par \uc2 Many people failed to realize that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has a long, ugly history of making anti-worker and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/unions-election-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-union}}}\uc2  statements. He has at times insulted workers, saying their wages are too high, saying their work is so easy that a child can do it. The former US president has also sought to sabotage labor by saying union members shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t pay their dues and successful union leaders should be fired. Trump has also sought to trick workers by making wonderful-sounding promises that he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t possibly make good on.\par \par \uc2 Below are Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 10 most shocking anti-worker and anti-union statements:\par \par \uc2 Trump actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2015/11/12/politics/donald-trump-explains-wages-too-high-comment/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that the wages of US workers are \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo high\u8221\'20\'1D. He insulted the nation\u8217\'20\'19s workers by insisting their pay is too high because from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s billionaire, pro-business viewpoint, that makes it too hard for US companies to compete. Trump said that workers\u8217\'20\'19 pay was too high even though corporate profits and the stock market were booming at the time.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/business/autos/2015/08/12/trump-autos/31589899/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggested}}}\uc2  that automakers in the midwest move some operations to the south so that they could reduce their workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages \u8211\'20\'13 the last thing that workers want. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can go to different parts of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said that after the auto industry in the midwest \u8220\'20\'1Closes a couple of plants \u8211\'20\'13 all of sudden you\u8217\'20\'19ll make good deals [to lower workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages] in your own area\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-and-musk-discussed-firing-striking-workers-the-uaw-is-now-seeking-an-nlrb-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised}}}\uc2  the idea of firing workers who are on strike, even though that is illegal under federal law. In a conversation with his billionaire campaign supporter \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , Trump applauded the idea of corporations telling their striking workers: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re all gone.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the greatest cutter,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Musk. \u8220\'20\'1CI look at what you do. You walk in and say: \u8216\'20\'18You want to quit?\u8217\'20\'19 I won\u8217\'20\'19t mention the name of the company, but they go on strike and you say: \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s OK. You\u8217\'20\'19re all gone.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump tried to portray himself as a regular worker by donning an apron for a photo op {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/us-presidential-election-2024-updates-kamala-harris-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania, but the fact is, Trump has never been a worker and has always been an owner. As an owner, he has always had management\u8217\'20\'19s interest at heart, particularly when it comes to workers. If Trump really wanted to be a worker, rather than an owner, he certainly could have been. Trump, who always wanted to be a billionaire and be in glitzy headlines, insults workers\u8217\'20\'19 intelligence when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/20/politics/mcdonalds-donald-trump-pennsylvania/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  he always wanted to be a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s worker. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always wanted to work at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , but I never did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump insulted the nation\u8217\'20\'19s factory workers by saying their jobs are such a cinch that children can do them. By {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/news/trump-completely-trashes-autoworkers-disastrously-211911525.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  that, he showed he has very little understanding of blue-collar jobs and how hard, exhausting and sometimes dangerous they are. In a recent speech to the Economic Club of Chicago, Trump talked about auto assembly plant jobs as if they\u8217\'20\'19re as simple as a child assembling Lego. \u8220\'20\'1CThey [workers] don\u8217\'20\'19t build cars. They take\u8217\'20\'19em out of a box, and they assemble\u8217\'20\'19em. We could have our child do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/30/union-members-could-be-big-trump-he-keeps-complicating-that/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he hates overtime pay. In a speech last month in Pennsylvania, he revealed how stingy he is toward workers by saying he tried to minimize what he paid his workers by always making sure he avoided paying time-and-a-half overtime pay. \u8220\'20\'1CI hated to give overtime. I hated it. I shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say this, but I\u8217\'20\'19d get other people in. I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t pay. I hated it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To win support from workers, Trump, after driving past several closed factories and steel mills in Ohio, made a marvelous promise. He sounded like the pied piper when he told thousands of workers in Youngstown that all of Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s lost factory jobs would be coming back with him as president. Trump even told Ohio workers not to move, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkbn.com/news/trump-speaks-on-jobs-tells-valley-residents-dont-sell-your-house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promising}}}\uc2  them that the jobs would come back. But the truth is that hardly any of those factory jobs came back. Indeed, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  closed its giant assembly plant in nearby \uc2 Lordstown\uc2  not long after Trump gave his Youngstown speech. \u8220\'20\'1CThose jobs have left Ohio. They\u8217\'20\'19re all coming back. They\u8217\'20\'19re all coming back. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t move. Don\u8217\'20\'19t sell your house.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, the president of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , is one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s most successful and respected union leaders. Fain led a major strike last fall that won 25% raises from \uc2 GM\uc2 , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 /Chrysler and the restoration of cost-of-living adjustments, plus 68% raises for new workers. Despite Fain\u8217\'20\'19s huge successes, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qz.com/trump-wants-uaw-leader-shawn-fain-to-be-fired-1851599752%20l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at the Republican convention that Fain should be \u8220\'20\'1Cfired immediately\u8221\'20\'1D. Why in the world was a presidential candidate saying that such a respected, inspiring union leader should be fired? That\u8217\'20\'19s improper interference in union affairs, and what Trump was calling for would seriously hurt the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s huge momentum and successes. \u8220\'20\'1CThe leader of the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  should be fired immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2016/06/09/donald-trump-unpaid-bills-republican-president-laswuits/85297274/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lied}}}\uc2  to the country\u8217\'20\'19s workers and insulted their intelligence when he said he always paid contractors and workers on time and what they\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be paid. Before he became president, he was notorious for paying construction contractors and workers late and for refusing to pay them the amount he had promised to pay; sometimes he would pay tens of thousands of dollars less than he was contracted to pay. Hundreds of contractors and workers had sued Trump after he failed to pay them or after he insisted on paying them far less than what the contract called for. \u8220\'20\'1CWe pay everybody what they\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be paid, and we pay everybody on time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jacobin.com/2023/09/donald-trump-uaw-ev-biden-big-three-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  union members that they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t pay their union dues. By saying this, Trump was essentially seeking to sabotage the country\u8217\'20\'19s labor unions. If workers refuse to pay their union dues, that would greatly weaken unions and their ability to fight for higher wages, better benefits, improved working conditions. Profit-maximizing corporations would love it if workers stopped paying their union dues and that undermined unions\u8217\'20\'19 ability to battle for better things for workers. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m telling you, you shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t pay those dues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steven Greenhouse is a journalist and author, focusing on labour and the workplace\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241023ekan001eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
