\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Scrutiny of Republican \uc2 Tim Sheehy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business grows amid \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2024\par 22:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bridger Aerospace secured $160m in bond from Gallatin county to hire new workers, but spent $134m on debt\par \par \uc2 Scrutiny is growing about the Montana aerial firefighting company once led by \uc2 Tim Sheehy\uc2 , the former Navy Seal and Republican Senate candidate who could oust the Democrat incumbent \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  in next month\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/senate-candidate-tim-sheehys-firm-promised-jobs-montana-county-s-still-rcna176439"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to NBC News}}}\uc2 , Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s Bridger Aerospace, a company he founded in 2013, negotiated a deal with Gallatin county in eastern Montana to use its pristine credit rating to raise $160m in bonds. The county was meant to benefit from Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s plans to hire more workers and build two new aircraft hangers.\par \par \uc2 But the company used most of the money, or $134m, from the 2022 bond issue to pay back previous investment from Blackstone, a New York-based investment giant.\par \par \uc2 Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s finances have been complicated by the fact that there were fewer wildfires to fight this year and thus less revenue for Bridger. As of Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nifc.gov/fire-information/nfn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the National Interagency Fire Center}}}\uc2  reported 42,603 wildfires nationwide this year compared with the 10-year average of 48,689 for the same period.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/ix?doc=/Archives/edgar/data/1941536/000162828024036974/baer-20240630.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial filings}}}\uc2  for the quarterly period that ended 30 June 2024, Bridger said it had \u8220\'20\'1Ca substantial amount of debt\u8221\'20\'1D and that failure to service that debt \u8220\'20\'1Ccould prolong the substantial doubt about our ability to continue as a going concern\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A victory for Sheehy in November could hand Republicans control of the Senate, making his connections to Bridger a vital topic as voters head to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Sheehy, 38, stepped down as the company\u8217\'20\'19s CEO in July. He has run his campaign partly based on his business acumen.\par \par \uc2 The questions around Gallatin county\u8217\'20\'19s approval of Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s bond deal revolve around whether the board was correctly informed of the company\u8217\'20\'19s financial position \u8211\'20\'13 it has lost $150m since it was founded \u8211\'20\'13 and whether Gallatin\u8217\'20\'19s credit rating could be affected.\par \par \uc2 Marc Cohodes, a Wall Street investor who issued an early warning regarding \uc2 FTX\uc2  and its CEO, \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , as well as calling the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/meet-the-wall-street-short-seller-betting-against-canadian-real-estate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapse of Lehman Brothers}}}\uc2  in 2008, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://montanafreepress.org/2024/08/30/feds-asked-to-investigate-160m-bond-issued-to-tim-sheehys-business/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among the signatories}}}\uc2  on a letter to Gallatin county and the \uc2 US Small Business Administration\uc2  asking for an investigation into Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s use of capital.\par \par \uc2 The letter questioned why Bridger presented itself to the federal government as a \u8220\'20\'1Csocially and economically disadvantaged business\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGallatin County had their name on the bonds and when they default, and they will, lawyers and lawsuits will come after Gallatin County,\u8221\'20\'1D Cohodes told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bozemandailychronicle.com/news/debate-heats-up-over-tim-sheehy-bridger-aerospace-with-wall-street-short-seller-marc-cohodes/article_f15ca612-6ae8-11ef-a430-cbcabfcc4097.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bozeman Daily Chronicle}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Read the fine print\u8217\'20\'19 will not be a good defense on this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s campaign pushed back, saying the deal\u8217\'20\'19s critics were Democratic supporters of Tester.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clear Tester\u8217\'20\'19s supporters wrote this letter with one goal: to hurt Tim\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, tear down a Montana company, and help \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D a campaign spokesperson told the Chronicle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBridger Aerospace is a good company that protects public lands by fighting wildfires, and it is our hope that the authors of this letter cease their efforts to destroy a Montana business, put Montanans out of a job, and wipe out their retirement savings.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zach Brown, a Gallatin county commissioner, told NBC he was not worried that the bond money had gone to pay Blackstone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt isn\u8217\'20\'19t our role to monitor the construction and operational decisions of a private company or communicate to the community the status report of how they\u8217\'20\'19re doing,\u8221\'20\'1D Brown told NBC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur role is not to monitor whether they added jobs \u8211\'20\'13 it is to endorse the public interest of their project.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While Gallatin county is not on the hook for the bond repayments, the county could see its credit rating affected if Bridger went out of business. Since January last year, when Bridger went public, its stock is down 64%.\par \par \uc2 Bridger reported losses of $77m in 2023 and was at risk of failing to meet its financial obligations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Company has suffered recurring losses from operations, operating cash flow deficits, debt covenant violations, and insufficient liquidity to fund its operations that raise substantial doubt about its ability to continue as a going concern,\u8221\'20\'1D Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s auditor said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://montanafreepress.org/2024/04/09/u-s-senate-hopefuls-company-reported-losses-of-more-than-77-million-in-2023/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Montana Free Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company said in the report that it began cutting costs and had reduced its workforce to 148, down from 166 in 2022.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Bridger told NBC that the company has continued to pay interest on the bonds, which are backed by \u8220\'20\'1Crobust collateral which has appreciated significantly in value since the bond was issued\u8221\'20\'1D and is working to repair its cash flow problems.\par \par \uc2 Separately, \uc2 Sam Davis\uc2 , Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s CEO, told the outlet that the company had battled more than 160 Montana wildfires since the bond issue.\par \par \uc2 The county\u8217\'20\'19s support for the company, Davis added, had been \u8220\'20\'1Ctremendous\u8221\'20\'1D and allowed the firefighting company to \u8220\'20\'1Ccontract with multiple local businesses as we expand and operate our business, and provide a strong customer base to local hotels, restaurants, and transportation providers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Questions around Bridger come as Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s service record also has come under scrutiny. The Trump-backed candidate has claimed he was shot in the arm during a firefight in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 But a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/tim-sheehy-gunshot-wound-montana-park-ranger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana park ranger}}}\uc2  has claimed that the gunshot wound was self-inflicted in Glacier national park in 2015. Nor do Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s fellow soldiers recall him mentioning a gunshot wound or seeing a wound at the time during his service in central Asia.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/18/us/tim-sheehy-gunshot-wound-montana-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sheehy has insisted}}}\uc2  that he was shot in Afghanistan and that claims to the contrary are \u8220\'20\'1Ctantamount to falsely accusing him of stolen valor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sheehy has also come under attack for allegedly characterizing Crow Native Americans as \u8220\'20\'1Cdrunk Indians\u8221\'20\'1D. He told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/video/6362206222112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  last month they were old recordings, and suggested they were edited, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dailymontanan.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports the Daily Montanan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241022ekam00339\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
