\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  seeks to raise up to $25bn through stock and debt offering\b0\par\par\uc2 Jack Simpson \par \uc2 483 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2024\par 16:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Planemaker also enters into $10bn credit agreement in \u8216\'20\'18challenging environment\u8217\'20\'19 amid strikes and safety concerns\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is seeking to raise up to $25bn (\u163\'00\'A319bn) in an attempt to shore up its finances as the planemaker struggles with production delays amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/25/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a strike by 33,000 workers}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/08/boeing-plane-rudder-issue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing safety concerns}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A regulatory filing by the company on Tuesday said it intended to raise the money through a stock and debt offering, which would provide flexibility for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  to seek options to support its balance sheet over a three-year period.\par \par \uc2 It also entered into a separate $10bn credit agreement with a consortium of banks, which it said would provide short-term access to liquidity as it navigated through a \u8220\'20\'1Cchallenging environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Production at the planemaker has been hobbled by the strike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that began a month ago}}}\uc2 , which is estimated to have cost the company more than $1bn, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the company withdrew its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/09/boeing-withdraws-30-pay-rise-offer-as-negotiation-with-striking-workers-reaches-stalemate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offer of a 30% pay rise }}}\uc2  over four years for striking staff after talks with unions broke down, and later in the week it announced plans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/11/boeing-job-cuts-worker-strike-plane-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to shed 17,000 jobs}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 about 10% of its global workforce \u8211\'20\'13 to cut costs.\par \par \uc2 The strikes add to a tumultuous year for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , which began in January when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/feb/06/faa-regulation-boeing-blowout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a door panel blew out}}}\uc2  in mid-air from one of its 737 Max 9s shortly after it took off from Portland, Oregon. The \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration (FAA)\uc2  then enforced a cap on the production of the Max jets.\par \par \uc2 In July, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  agreed to plead guilty {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/08/boeing-737-max-crashes-guilty-plea-indonesia-ethiopia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to a US criminal fraud charge}}}\uc2  stemming from the crashes of two 737 Max jetliners in 2018 and 2019, which killed 346 people, and agreed to pay a fine of almost $250m (\u163\'00\'A3191m).\par \par \uc2 It was not clear when or how much the company expected to raise through the offering announced on Tuesday but analysts predicted it would be completed before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is also facing $11.5bn of debt maturing through February 2026, while it has committed to issuing $4.7bn of its shares {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/01/boeing-to-buy-supplier-spirit-aerosystems-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to acquire Spirit AeroSystems}}}\uc2 , as well as take on its debt. The deal to buy back the parts supplier, which it sold off nearly 20 years ago, was part of its plan to boost safety on production lines.\par \par \uc2 In a statement with the filing to the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis universal shelf registration provides flexibility for the company to seek a variety of capital options as needed to support the company\u8217\'20\'19s balance sheet over a three-year period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The separate $10bn credit facility was struck with banks including Citibank and \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  but the manufacturer confirmed it had yet to draw any money from it. It said: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are two prudent steps to support the company\u8217\'20\'19s access to liquidity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241015ekaf001v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
