\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US unions step up efforts to make case that Trump is no friend of workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,438 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2024\par 16:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unions have mobilized thousands of members to convince them that Harris is a far better ally than Trump\par \par \uc2 Even though the vast majority of US labor unions have endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , many union members support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and with the race so close, unions have stepped up efforts to convince those workers that Trump is no friend of unions or workers.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 states that Harris badly needs to win \u8211\'20\'13 union households are an important voting bloc, and unions have mobilized thousands of members to engage in worksite conversations, door-knocking and phone-banking to make the case that Harris is far better for workers than Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has found ways to break through with working people,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Shuler\uc2 , president of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the nation\u8217\'20\'19s main labor federation, told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has the rhetoric down, but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the results to back it up. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s important that we, as messengers, combat that with facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  is urging the nation\u8217\'20\'19s 14.4 million union members to look at its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://betterinaunion.org/candidate-comparison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccandidate comparison\u8221\'20\'1D website}}}\uc2 , which makes the case that Trump is anti-union. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/2016/9/16/open-letter-donald-trump-you-lost-my-vote-when-you-crossed-my-picket-line"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crossed a union picket line}}}\uc2 , praised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/donald-trump-cheers-elon-musk-over-firing-workers-youre-greatest-1938303"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the idea of firing workers}}}\uc2  who are on strike, and often {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/2016/7/12/when-donald-trump-had-choice-he-chose-nonunion-labor-his-construction-projects-ibew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used non-union workers}}}\uc2  at his construction sites.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, the website explains, Harris has shown solidarity with workers by, for instance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rgj.com/picture-gallery/news/2019/10/03/photos-senator-kamala-harris-campaigns-reno/3856937002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walking a United Auto Workers picket line}}}\uc2  and by, unlike Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-unanimously-endorses-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backing the Protecting the Right to Organize Act}}}\uc2 , which would make it easier to unionize workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people don\u8217\'20\'19t trust their information sources any more,\u8221\'20\'1D whether political parties or the news media, Shuler said. But workers trust their unions as an information source, she said, because workers have long trusted their unions on crucial issues like wages, benefits, pensions and job safety.\par \par \uc2 Shuler said member-to-member political communications, such as talking to co-workers, were \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most impactful\u8221\'20\'1D. The \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  recently announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckWZeXMT0Pc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a digital and streaming ad buy}}}\uc2 , going to 2.5 million workers, in which rank-and-file workers do the talking. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re noticed that union members\u8217\'20\'19 stories break through to workers in a way that\u8217\'20\'19s different,\u8221\'20\'1D Shuler said.\par \par \uc2 She noted that for the first time the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  was specifically doing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LizShuler/status/1841247974095274144"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women\u8217\'20\'19s mobilization}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 on equal pay, childcare and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/LizShuler/status/1841294653921865901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe haven\u8217\'20\'19t always been present on reproductive health,\u8221\'20\'1D she acknowledged.\par \par \uc2 Sara Nelson\uc2 , president of the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2 , said unions needed to have discussions with their members about \u8220\'20\'1Chow these elections affect our work lives\u8221\'20\'1D. With Trump and Harris as the candidates, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe conversation this year could not be easier\u8221\'20\'1D, Nelson said. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump wants to fire striking workers, and Biden and Harris have upheld our right to strike. If you want someone who fights for workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and fights against corporate greed and inequality, then vote for Harris and Walz.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nelson added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe see one candidate as the collective bargaining agent in chief and the other as the union buster in chief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Pittsburgh-based \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union has members out every morning at plant gates making the case for Harris. It also spread a pro-Harris message in 100 recent town hall meetings that steelworker locals held across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur focus is making sure we\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uswvoices.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 putting the issues in front}}}\uc2  of people and connecting them with the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 policies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kim Miller, a steelworkers official helping run the union\u8217\'20\'19s political operations. Miller noted that her union had for 50 years urged president after president to embrace industrial policies to help save manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the Biden-Harris administration,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the first time in decades, we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing an industrial policy\u8221\'20\'1D with the Chips Act bringing back computer chip production from overseas and the infrastructure bill. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not only rebuilding our nation, but they\u8217\'20\'19re using many products that steelworkers make.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several labor leaders said it was harder to get union members to volunteer this year to do political work. That has created some concern in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Steve Rosenthal, a former \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  political director, said, \u8220\'20\'1CI think there should be emergency statewide meetings in Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and Michigan with the people at the very top of the labor movement doing a serious \u8216\'20\'18Come to Jesus\u8217\'20\'19 and making it clear that from now until election day, we need as many people as we can get on the ground, lining up volunteers from locals, knocking on doors, making phone calls, going to worksites, speaking to members. To get volunteers, it takes a massive effort and constant badgering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump beat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in Michigan by just 11,837 votes in 2016, and Biden won Wisconsin by 20,682 in 2020. This means that persuading a small percentage of union voters in those states can make the difference. According to exit polls, 1.1 million or 21% of Michigan voters were from union households in 2020, as were 448,000 or 14% in Wisconsin and 1.2 million or 18% in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 union was the only one of the 10 largest unions not to endorse a presidential candidate. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/teamsters-chief-on-why-union-wont-endorse-trump-or-harris-our-system-is-broken"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, said}}}\uc2  one reason for the non-endorsement was he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to \u8220\'20\'1Clook out of step\u8221\'20\'1D because \u8220\'20\'1Chalf our membership [are] Democrats and half are Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That non-endorsement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/democrats-lash-out-misinformed-teamsters-union-makes-landmark-non-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upset many Democrats}}}\uc2 , partly because the Biden-Harris administration had worked hard to win enactment of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 main legislative priority, a bill that saved the pensions of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/06/21/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-announces-over-one-million-pensions-protected-thanks-to-the-american-rescue-plan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 400,000 Teamsters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe job of a leader is to lead,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosenthal said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you believe there are clearcut differences and there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot at stake for your union\u8217\'20\'19s members with the differences between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s your responsibility to make the case to your state and local leaders and your members. It\u8217\'20\'19s the union\u8217\'20\'19s job to communicate the difference between the candidates. It\u8217\'20\'19s the union\u8217\'20\'19s responsibility to get its members to support the candidate who will stand with workers and support unions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Soon after \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  headquarters announced that non-endorsement, Kevin Moore, president of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 regional council in Michigan, which represents 245,000 active and retired \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , rushed to get his council to endorse Harris \u8211\'20\'13 one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/21/teamsters-local-endorsement-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 20 Teamster locals and councils}}}\uc2  backing Harris. Moore questioned the accuracy of a \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  poll that showed strong support for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1COur people in Michigan overwhelming support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe remember that Harris cast the deciding vote to save \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 pensions, and we won\u8217\'20\'19t forget that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brian Pannebecker, a Ford worker in Michigan, helped found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/detroit/news/michigan-auto-workers-supporting-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Auto Workers for Trump}}}\uc2 , a group that holds frequent rallies outside auto plants. He voices disgust with the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of Harris \u8211\'20\'13 Shawn Fain, the union\u8217\'20\'19s president, has done {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FCkoaZUvvPI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video}}}\uc2  saying, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is all talk and no action when it comes to delivering for autoworkers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t give a rat\u8217\'20\'19s rear end what Shawn Fain says,\u8221\'20\'1D Pannebecker said, slamming Biden and Harris for pushing the transition to electric vehicles and noting that it takes fewer workers to produce EVs than internal combustion vehicles. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy would an autoworker support a government mandate forcing manufacturers to build electric vehicles when 50% of all EV batteries are built by the Chinese?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Pannebecker estimates that over half of autoworkers back Trump, but \uc2 UAW\uc2  officials insist that\u8217\'20\'19s exaggerated, saying autoworker support for the Republican candidate hasn\u8217\'20\'19t exceeded 35% in the past four presidential elections.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/11M1GasOH196ofjqjCTh1wgiDuOdbDkAo/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fain recently noted}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has for decades urged automakers to produce vehicles that are better for the environment. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t hide from this,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re fighting to keep internal combustion jobs as the nation builds more EV and EV battery plants so those are made here, not in China.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fain said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s policies were \u8220\'20\'1Cactually building manufacturing here\u8221\'20\'1D, while saying that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ctrickle-down policies\u8221\'20\'1D have led to \u8220\'20\'1Call these jobs leaving America\u8221\'20\'1D. He said that under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, it was \u8220\'20\'1Cmore of the same \u8211\'20\'13 the rich get richer, keep outsourcing our work, and the handful at the top and the shareholders take all the money and the workers who create the wealth get left behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of our members get that,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will win Michigan and that auto workers will be a big part of delivering that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241008eka80025u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
