\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US dock workers ended strike \u8211\'20\'13 but dispute is not over yet\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The interim agreement expires in January, and a further strike would again hurt America\u8217\'20\'19s fragile supply chain\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration breathed a sigh of relief on Thursday when the union representing port workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/03/dock-workers-ports-strike-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called off a strike}}}\uc2  that threatened mass disruption of goods just weeks before November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 But the dispute between the \uc2 International Longshoremen\u8217\'20\'19s Association\uc2  (ILA) and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s port operators is not yet over, and could hand whoever wins the White House their first political crisis come January.\par \par \uc2 The agreement to call off industrial action expires on 15 January, and if a new contract is not agreed by then, the ILA could take further action. The impact of which is likely to be felt worldwide.\par \par \uc2 As many Americans learned during the pandemic, the supply chain is somewhat fragile.\par \par \uc2 Imported goods made abroad are packed on to massive shipping containers that travel the seas to reach American shores. Once they arrive at a port, the containers are removed from the ships to be put in warehouses. The goods are then taken by truck or train to get to their destinations.\par \par \uc2 If one part of the chain is interrupted, there can be ripple effects.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why the dockworkers\u8217\'20\'19 strike that started on Tuesday was such a big deal. Goods shipped to a port on the east coast or Gulf coast of the US could not move along until the strike was called off.\par \par \uc2 The first of its kind since 1977, the dock strike probably cost the economy at least $5bn a day.\par \par \uc2 The ILA, representing 45,000 workers across 36 ports, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/03/port-workers-strike-pay-automation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for}}}\uc2  higher wages and forbidding automation and semi-automation at the ports, as a job protection measure.\par \par \uc2 The union and the United States Maritime Alliance (USMX), a consortium of carriers and terminal operations, have reached a tentative deal with a reported 62% increase in wages over six years. Other issues, including automation, remain unresolved.\par \par \uc2 As talks continue, here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for the US economy.\par \par \uc2 This strike ended after three days. What happened?\par \par \uc2 For most Americans, the impacts of the strike were minimal.\par \par \uc2 Companies knew the strike was a possibility for at least a few weeks, said Keely Croxton, professor of logistics at \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2 , and have been ramping up shipments and expediting getting containers off ships before the strike.\par \par \uc2 What if a new strike goes on for more than a couple of weeks?\par \par \uc2 The goods coming into the east and Gulf coast ports are largely shipments from Europe and South and Central America. The strike does not affect cruise ships or military cargo.\par \par \uc2 This means that some fresh fruit and vegetables transported in refrigerated containers could be affected first if the strike lasts more than two weeks. Many of the bananas consumed in the US, for example, come from South and Central America. Once the supply of bananas that has already gone through the ports starts to dwindle, the grocery store stock can be affected.\par \par \uc2 But economists say that only certain parts of the grocery store shelves might disappear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be selective to begin with. The broader macro impact wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t start to build unless this was going on for a very long time,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Michael Pearce\uc2 , deputy chief US economist at Oxford Economics, said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you start to get a strike lasting three to four weeks, that\u8217\'20\'19s when you start to see a more sustained period of disruption that we might need to start worrying about in terms of broader ripples through the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If a strike lasted for more than a few weeks, carriers could try to start shipping things in through the west coast ports. Price increases could come from carriers shifting the costs of that on to consumers, Pearce said.\par \par \uc2 Economists emphasize that the impacts of a strike would be different than what was seen during the pandemic, when there were widespread shortages, first induced by panic-buying and later continued when parts of the supply chain were disrupted by lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 Companies would be better prepared for this than they were for the pandemic, Croxton said. \u8220\'20\'1CCompanies learned from the pandemic and have developed a more robust sourcing and distribution strategy, and have found ways to be more flexible to respond to disruptions like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 How would it affect other workers?\par \par \uc2 Workers in other industries in the supply chain could see the most immediate impact, said Pearce. If the number of goods flowing through the supply chain slows, so will their work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose jobs in warehousing logistics, forwarding wholesalers \u8211\'20\'13 those that rely on the flood of goods coming through the ports, there will be a disruption of those businesses,\u8221\'20\'1D Pearce said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf this goes on for more than a week or so, you\u8217\'20\'19ll start to see reports of furloughs or temporary layoffs in those sectors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241005eka5000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
