\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Revealed: CEO at heart of US ports strike made crude attacks on Biden and Democrats\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 615 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par 19:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 David Adam of USMX made coarse remarks about president and appeared to endorse rightwing conspiracy theory\par \par \uc2 An executive representing ports where tens of thousands of workers went on strike this week made a series of critical and crude remarks about Joe Biden, tied \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to concerns about over-taxation, and appeared to endorse a rightwing conspiracy theory.\par \par \uc2 David Adam, chairman and chief executive of the United States Maritime Alliance (USMX), attacked prominent Democrats in a string of social media posts uncovered by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 It comes after about 45,000 dockworkers at ports along the US east and Gulf coasts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/01/us-port-workers-strike-ila-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked off the job}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the first such strike since 1977 \u8211\'20\'13 as part of a dispute between the USMX and the \uc2 International Longshoremen\u8217\'20\'19s Association\uc2  over pay and automation.\par \par \uc2 The sweeping strike, disrupting 36 ports from Maine to Texas, has already raised fears of supply shortages and price increases on the eve of November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 A month ago, when a LinkedIn user suggested that \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything Biden has touched in the past is turning to shit!\u8221\'20\'1D, Adam replied: \u8220\'20\'1CThe runny kind\u8230\'20\'26.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was part of a discussion about how Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student-debt relief plan was being held up in the courts. In another comment on the thread, Adam wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CIf ya can\u8217\'20\'19t get an American Democrat to pay what they borrrowed [sic], how you gonna get a California illegal immigrant to pay back their $150K loan the CA Dems are offering?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Three months ago, another user appeared to endorse a popular conspiracy theory surrounding the emergence of a totalitarian world government while commenting on a video of Biden discussing immigration. \u8220\'20\'1CDid I miss the vote America took in agreement of One World Order? Treasonous actions have consequences!\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Kerry and Gates voted two thumbs up on that a few years ago \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D Adam replied.\par \par \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  was the Democratic presidential candidate in 2004, and served as secretary of state under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate envoy. \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2  co-founded \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . Both men have been tied to debunked conspiracy theories surrounding secret global regimes.\par \par \uc2 USMX did not respond to multiple requests for comment on Adam\u8217\'20\'19s posts.\par \par \uc2 Just a few weeks ago, Adam commented on a meme that claimed the US has a 48% fuel tax, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/may/06/facebook-posts/claim-exaggerates-fuel-tax-rates-australia-and-can/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debunked in 2022 by Politifact}}}\uc2 , when the same post was shared in Canada with the same claim.\par \par \uc2 He seemed to suggest responsibility lay with the Biden administration and Harris, however, writing: \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone ask Kamala to explain why this is such and is she gonna fix it?!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, when another user suggested Biden had smiled while walking away from a question, Adam {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7202489050727923712?commentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A%28activity%3A7202489050727923712%2C7202497238323867649%29&replyUrn=urn%3Ali%3Acomment%3A%28activity%3A7202489050727923712%2C7202521871081234432%29&dashCommentUrn=urn%3Ali%3Afsd_comment%3A%287202497238323867649%2Curn%3Ali%3Aactivity%3A7202489050727923712%29&dashReplyUrn=urn%3Ali%3Afsd_comment%3A%287202521871081234432%2Curn%3Ali%3Aactivity%3A7202489050727923712%29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commented}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CActually I thought he looked like he just sharted himself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the strike began on Tuesday, Biden urged the port operators \u8211\'20\'13 represented by USMX \u8211\'20\'13 to give workers a \u8220\'20\'1Cmeaningful increase\u8221\'20\'1D in pay. Trump, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/trump-blames-port-workers-strike-massive-inflation-caused-harris-biden-regime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed}}}\uc2  the strike on high inflation under Biden and Harris.\par \par \uc2 The timing of the strike, just weeks before the election, also raised questions about the ILA\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with Trump. A photograph of the union\u8217\'20\'19s president, Harold Daggett, meeting Trump in November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/10/01/harold-daggett-trump-photo-longshoremens-union/75474233007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resurfaced}}}\uc2  on social media this week.\par \par \uc2 After an assassination attempt on Trump in July, the ILA released a statement describing the 2023 meeting as \u8220\'20\'1Cwonderful\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive\u8221\'20\'1D, and hailing Daggett\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clong relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with the former president.\par \par \uc2 The union has not made an endorsement ahead of next month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ilaunion.org/ila-president-harold-j-daggett-announces-endorsement-of-joe-biden-for-president-urges-ila-members-in-florida-ohio-and-illinois-to-vote-in-tuesdays-primaries/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed}}}\uc2  Biden in 2020, declaring him to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca true friend of the ILA and working men and women across America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241003eka3002s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
