\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden urges port operators to increase wages after 45,000 workers go on strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par 23:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 30\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Strike \u8211\'20\'13 the first by port workers on US east coast since 1977 \u8211\'20\'13 threatens to shut down ports from Maine to Texas\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has urged port operators to give workers a \u8220\'20\'1Cmeaningful increase\u8221\'20\'1D in pay after tens of thousands went on strike, prompting some of the busiest ports in the US to brace for crippling disruption.\par \par \uc2 About 45,000 port workers represented by the \uc2 International Longshoremen\u8217\'20\'19s Association\uc2  (ILA) began walking off the job after their contracts expired at midnight, with 36 ports along the east and Gulf coasts affected. They typically handle about half of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s ocean shipping.\par \par \uc2 Talks over a new contract between the ILA and the United States Maritime Alliance (USMX) have broken down, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union}}}\uc2  dismissed a last-ditch offer from operators hours before the strike was due to began.\par \par \uc2 Hours after the strike began, the White House issued a robust statement calling on USMX to negotiate a \u8220\'20\'1Cfair\u8221\'20\'1D contract that reflects \u8220\'20\'1Cthe substantial contribution\u8221\'20\'1D of ports workers to America\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is not the time for ocean carriers to refuse to negotiate a fair wage for these essential workers while raking in record profits,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy administration will be monitoring for any price-gouging activity that benefits foreign ocean carriers, including those on the USMX board.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The strike \u8211\'20\'13 the first by port workers on the US east coast since 1977 \u8211\'20\'13 threatens to shut down ports from Maine to Texas, mangling supply chains and straining the US economy.\par \par \uc2 As workers joined picket lines at ports including Philadelphia, Houston and Virginia in the early hours, economists have warned that failure to end the strike swiftly could lead to shortages and higher prices.\par \par \uc2 Ocean carriers have enjoyed \u8220\'20\'1Crecord profits\u8221\'20\'1D since the pandemic, Biden added, \u8220\'20\'1Cand in some cases profits grew in excess of 800% compared to their profits prior to the pandemic. Executive compensation has grown in line with those profits and profits have been returned to shareholders at record rates.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s only fair that workers, who put themselves at risk during the pandemic to keep ports open, see a meaningful increase in their wages as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Negotiators on both sides of the table have accused the other of refusing to bargain. The ILA has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/port-worker-strike-longshoremen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that USMX, which represents 40 ocean terminals and port operators, has \u8220\'20\'1Clow-balled\u8221\'20\'1D offers on wage raises for workers and accused it of violating the previous contract by introducing automation at several US ports.\par \par \uc2 It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/money/2024/09/30/port-shutdown-strike-what-to-expect/75450584007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  the strike will cost the economy as much as $5bn a day. The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ilaunion.org/ila-will-maintain-pledge-to-handle-military-cargo-during-strike-passenger-cruise-ships-to-be-unaffected-by-10-1-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  it will still handle military cargo, and that passenger cruise ships will be unaffected.\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s intervention on Tuesday, port operators said they were \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D of the pay and benefits offered to their employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have demonstrated a commitment to doing our part to end the completely avoidable ILA strike,\u8221\'20\'1D USMX said, arguing that its latest proposed wage increase \u8220\'20\'1Cexceeds every other recent union settlement\u8221\'20\'1D and addresses inflation. \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to hearing from the Union about how we can return to the table and actually bargain, which is the only way to reach a resolution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia, the local ILA president, Boise Butler, said the union would strike for as long as it needed to get a fair deal, and claimed that it had leverage over the companies. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not something that you start and you stop,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Associated Press. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not weak,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, pointing to the union\u8217\'20\'19s importance to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 Shipping companies made billions of dollars during the pandemic by charging high prices, and \u8220\'20\'1Cnow we want them to pay back\u8221\'20\'1D, Butler added. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re going to pay back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 USMX filed an unfair labor practice charge against the union with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  last Wednesday, alleging the union was refusing to negotiate. Before the strike on Monday, USMX said it and the union had exchanged new offers on wages. The union countered by claiming the charge was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpublicity stunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Current wages under the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ilaunion.org/wp-content/uploads/Master-Contract-2018.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contract}}}\uc2  that expired on Monday range from $20 an hour to the top wage of $39 an hour. The union is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/30/business/ports-strike-deadline/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking}}}\uc2  raises of 77% over the six-year contract, to a top rate of $69 an hour by 2030.\par \par \uc2 The Transportation Trades Department (TTD) of the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, issued a statement before the strike in support of the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us be clear: the employers, not the workers, have shirked their responsibility and punted labor negotiations to the 11th hour, when the damage to the public and the national supply chain would be most detrimental,\u8221\'20\'1D said Greg Regan and Shari Semelsberger, president and secretary-treasurer of TTD. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile USMX seeks to cast blame on the frontline workers who move our supply chain, they are at fault.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241001eka1000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
