\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Can\u8217\'20\'19t afford health insurance\u8217\'20\'19: California CVS workers take strike vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 787 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 18:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 7,000 workers to hold strike vote this week amid accusations of staff shortages and expensive healthcare\par \par \uc2 More than 7,000 workers at CVS stores across California are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw770.org/news-internal/cvsstrikeauthorizationvotes083024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holding}}}\uc2  a strike vote this week after accusing the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest pharmacy chain of shortchanging staff and failing to provide affordable healthcare.\par \par \uc2 CVS and its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union}}}\uc2  remain far apart in negotiations on a new contract. Their current union contract expired on 30 June 2024.\par \par \uc2 The union said the average CVS clerk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coronalivingmag.com/cvs-workers-announce-strike-authorization-votes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 makes}}}\uc2  less than $20 an hour, and the union wants improved healthcare costs for employees, and improvements to safety and staffing.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers\uc2  local union bargaining committee has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw770.org/cvs-ulp-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommended }}}\uc2  a yes vote on the strike authorization, with results expected late on 27 September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI work full-time yet can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to get health insurance, which is ridiculous, because CVS owns \uc2 Aetna\uc2 , and the only option I am given is a health insurance plan that\u8217\'20\'19s outside of what I can even afford due to the pay of my job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ian Peggs, a shift supervisor at a CVS store in San Luis Obispo, California.\par \par \uc2 He said he made the same wage he received when he started working at the store in 2020, and claimed his store was frequently understaffed and that it experienced frequent thefts, but workers were not given any security or resources even though CVS corporate pressured them over high theft and product shrink losses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey complain about things that are happening in store, yet want to do nothing to remedy the situation that they are perpetuating by not helping us,\u8221\'20\'1D added Peggs. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we are customer service, it\u8217\'20\'19s now to a point where on a daily basis, I am personally attacked for being a member of the LGBTQ community. I catch someone stealing and it\u8217\'20\'19s an automatic threat on my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw770.org/news-internal/cvsrallyforafaircontract082426"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  of CVS members at \uc2 UFCW\uc2  Local 770, 64%of workers reported not having health insurance through CVS, with 77% citing the high costs for not being able to use it. The union has criticized these high costs given that CVS is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.beckershospitalreview.com/disruptors/6-reasons-cvs-health-grew-to-become-2nd-largest-healthcare-company-in-the-world.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second-largest}}}\uc2  healthcare company in the world. CVS also reported {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw770.org/cvs-ulp-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $11bn}}}\uc2  in profits and its CEO, \uc2 Karen Lynch\uc2 , received more than $21.6m in total compensation in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Over the three-year contract, the union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/64652ea538621a1d5525de3b/t/66e47641286ac3483c1332ff/1726248513867/WHERE+NEGOTIATIONS+STAND+ENGLISH.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushed}}}\uc2  for raises of at least $3.60 an hour for store associates with less than five years of seniority to $6.35-an-hour wage increases for lead pharmacy technicians. CVS\u8217\'20\'19s latest proposal only offered $1.90-an-hour wage increases over three years for store associates and $2.35-an-hour increases for lead pharmacy techs.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UFCW\uc2  has filed several unfair labor practice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/31-CA-348401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  against CVS, alleging surveillance of workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/21-CA-349682"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intimidation}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/21-CA-348662"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusing }}}\uc2  to allow workers to speak with union representatives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re watching over workers, they\u8217\'20\'19re intimidating union-active members and they\u8217\'20\'19re really obstructing the communication with union representatives,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melissa Acosta, a \uc2 CVS pharmacy\uc2  technician for nine years in Lynwood. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have unsafe working conditions in the front of the store and pharmacy. The answer to that for the company is to lock everything up. Meanwhile we\u8217\'20\'19re understaffed and there\u8217\'20\'19s barely any workers to unlock these shelves that everything\u8217\'20\'19s been locked up, and it puts more pressure on them, and it frustrates the customers even more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Acosta said that despite CVS being a healthcare company, she had not experienced any benefit from that as she opts to use health insurance coverage through the marketplace rather than through CVS because she cannot afford it through her employer.\par \par \uc2 The union also claimed CVS had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/64652ea538621a1d5525de3b/t/66e47641286ac3483c1332ff/1726248513867/WHERE+NEGOTIATIONS+STAND+ENGLISH.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected }}}\uc2  their proposal to cut health insurance costs for many workers, and rejected proposals to improve staffing and provide workers with time to complete safety trainings. Workers are pushing for safety improvements, including security, trainings and improved staffing.\par \par \uc2 Amy Thibault, a spokesperson for CVS, did not comment on the unfair labor practice charges in an email, but noted that CVS had agreed to tentative agreements to lower top rate seniority pay levels from six to five years of service, regardless of job classification.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in active discussions with the \uc2 UFCW\uc2  and are confident we can reach an agreement that supports workplace safety, appropriate staffing, and competitive wages and benefits,\u8221\'20\'1D Thibault said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more to do, but we\u8217\'20\'19re committed to working together. We look forward to reconvening with \uc2 UFCW\uc2  on October 16 and 18 to continue negotiations and hope to finalize an agreement soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240924ek9o002uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
