\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 Meta\uc2  among world\u8217\'20\'19s top companies undermining democracy \u8211\'20\'13 report\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 869 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 16:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corporations such as \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2  and \uc2 Blackstone\uc2  also big funders of climate crisis, new trade union report finds\par \par \uc2 Some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest companies have been accused of undermining democracy across the world by financially backing far-right political movements, funding and exacerbating the climate crisis, and violating trade union rights and human rights in a report published on Monday by the International Trade Union Confederation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (ITUC).}}}\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , \uc2 Meta\uc2 , \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2 , \uc2 Blackstone\uc2 , \uc2 Vanguard\uc2  and \uc2 Glencore\uc2  are the corporations included in the report. The companies\u8217\'20\'19 lobbying arms are attempting to shape global policy at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.un.org/en/summit-of-the-future?gad_source=1&gclid=Cj0KCQjwrp-3BhDgARIsAEWJ6SyFQYPAZ7DEa1cC5XyWq4DFrUyVhdWYm9Q14hlYncrw5a3JyvP7ifoaAs9gEALw_wcB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Nations Summit of the Future}}}\uc2  in New York City on 22 and 23 September.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the report notes the company\u8217\'20\'19s size and role as the fifth largest employer in the world and the largest online retailer and cloud computing service, has had a profound impact on the industries and communities it operates within.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe company has become notorious for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/03/amazon-union-warehouse-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union busting}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.un.org/en/story/2023/10/1143067"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 low wages }}}\uc2  on multiple continents, monopoly in e-commerce, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/environment/data-centers-virginia-amazon-environment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 egregious carbon emissions}}}\uc2  through its \uc2 AWS\uc2  data centres, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://itep.org/amazon-avoids-more-than-5-billion-in-corporate-income-taxes-reports-6-percent-tax-rate-on-35-billion-of-us-income/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 corporate tax evasion}}}\uc2 , and lobbying at national and international level,\u8221\'20\'1D states the report.\par \par \uc2 The report cites \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s high injury rates in the US, the company challenging the constitutionality of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrreporter.com/focus-areas/labour-relations/quebec-gets-first-amazon-union-in-canada/386093"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts}}}\uc2  in Canada to overturn labor law, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uni-europa.org/news/victory-amazon-lobbyists-banned-from-european-parliament/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  lobbyists from the European parliament for refusing to attend hearings on worker violations, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.verdi.de/themen/geld-tarif/++co++4004349c-d6ad-11ec-a3dd-001a4a16012a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusal}}}\uc2  to negotiate with unions in Germany, among other cases. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/03/anti-abortion-lawmakers-donation-amazon-google-comcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 funded}}}\uc2  far-right political groups\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to undermine women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and antitrust legislation, and its retail website has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/hatewatch/2022/08/23/white-nationalist-group-exploits-amazon-fund-their-cause"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 used}}}\uc2  by hate groups to raise money and sell products.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , the report cites anti-union opposition by the company in the US, Germany, and Sweden; human rights violations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mightyearth.org/article/from-forests-to-electric-vehicles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 within its supply chains}}}\uc2  ; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s personal opposition to unions and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/nov/25/we-will-coup-whoever-we-want-the-unbearable-hubris-of-musk-and-the-billionaire-tech-bros"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 democracy,}}}\uc2  challenges to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  in the US, and his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1812256998588662068"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support }}}\uc2  for the political leaders Donald Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reason.com/2024/04/15/javier-milei-and-elon-musk-bond-over-markets/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Javier Milei}}}\uc2  in Argentina and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/narendramodi/status/1799332363375378815"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Narendra Modi}}}\uc2  in India.\par \par \uc2 The report cites \uc2 Meta\uc2 , the largest social media company in the world, for its vast role in permitting and enabling far-right propaganda and movements to use its platforms to grow members and garner support in the US and abroad. It also cited retaliation from the company for regulatory measures in Canada, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2019/mar/02/facebook-global-lobbying-campaign-against-data-privacy-laws-investment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expensive lobbying efforts}}}\uc2  against laws to regulate data privacy.\par \par \uc2 Glencore\uc2 , the largest mining company in the world by revenue, was included in the report for its role in financing campaigns globally against Indigenous communities and activists.\par \par \uc2 Blackstone\uc2 , the private equity firm led by \uc2 Stephen Schwarzman\uc2 , a billionaire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/05/24/us/politics/blackstone-stephen-schwarzman-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backer}}}\uc2  of Donald Trump, was cited in the report for its roles in funding far-right political movements, investments in fossil fuel projects and deforestation in the \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Blackstone\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s network has spent tens of millions of dollars supporting politicians and political forces who promise to prevent or eliminate regulations that might hold it to account,\u8221\'20\'1D the report noted. \uc2 Blackstone\uc2  has disputed the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  deforestation claim and sold its remaining shares in the company in question in 2021. The company argued it does not make direct political contributions and that contributions from its executives are personal.\par \par \uc2 The Vanguard Group\uc2  was included in the report due to its role in financing some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most anti-democratic corporations. \uc2 ExxonMobil\uc2  was cited for funding anti-climate science research and aggressive lobbying against environmental regulations.\par \par \uc2 Even in \u8220\'20\'1Crobust democracies\u8221\'20\'1D workers\u8217\'20\'19 demands \u8220\'20\'1Care overwhelmed by corporate lobbying operations, either in policymaking or the election in itself\u8221\'20\'1D, said Todd Brogan, director of campaigns and organizing at the \uc2 ITUC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about power, who has it, and who sets the agenda. We know as trade unionists that unless we\u8217\'20\'19re organized, the boss sets the agenda in the workplace, and we know as citizens in our countries that unless we\u8217\'20\'19re organized and demanding responsive governments that actually meet the needs of people, it\u8217\'20\'19s corporate power that\u8217\'20\'19s going to set the agenda.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re playing the long game, and it\u8217\'20\'19s a game about shifting power away from democracy at every level into one where they\u8217\'20\'19re not concerned about the effects on workers \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about maximizing their influence and their extractive power and their profit,\u8221\'20\'1D added Brogan. \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time for international and multi-sectoral strategies, because these are, in many cases, multinational corporations that are more powerful than states, and they have no democratic accountability whatsoever, except for workers organized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ITUC\uc2  includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/IMG/pdf/list_of_affiliates_june_2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor group affiliates}}}\uc2  from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/global-rights-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 169 nations}}}\uc2  and territories around the world representing 191 million workers, including the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest federation of labor unions in the US, and the Trades Union Congress in the UK.\par \par \uc2 With 4 billion people around the world set to participate in elections in 2024, the federation is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ituc-csi.org/ITUC-builds-alignment-for-robust-international-treaty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing}}}\uc2  for an international binding treaty being worked on by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/hr-bodies/hrc/wg-trans-corp/igwg-on-tnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Open-ended intergovernmental working group}}}\uc2  to hold transnational corporations accountable under international human rights laws.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 24 September 2024 to reflect \uc2 Blackstone\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s position on claims made in the \uc2 ITUC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s report.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240923ek9n001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
