\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US labor watchdog pressures Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s to bargain with New York union\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 654 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company may be ordered to recognize union amid allegations employees were threatened during election\par \par \uc2 Mobilizing workers at a Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s store on New York\u8217\'20\'19s Lower East Side marginally lost a union election last year. They may ultimately get their union after all.\par \par \uc2 The general counsel of the US\u8217\'20\'19s top labor watchdog is seeking an order demanding that Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s recognize and bargain with the union, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s United, amid allegations that employees were threatened and disparaged from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 Under a framework introduced by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) last year, employers can be ordered to bargain with a union if they commit unfair labor practices that would set aside the results of a union ballot.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/board-issues-decision-announcing-new-framework-for-union-representation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new framework}}}\uc2 , designed to ensure a \u8220\'20\'1Ctimely and fair\u8221\'20\'1D process of seeking union representation, was drawn up as the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  found the construction materials firm Cemex had engaged in more than 20 instances of objectionable or unlawful misconduct during a campaign.\par \par \uc2 If an employer commits an unfair labor practice during a union election which requires throwing out the result, under the Cemex framework \u8211\'20\'13 rather than re-run the election \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  can order the employer to recognize and bargain with the union.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s is one of the largest grocery chains in the US, with hundreds of stores and tens of thousands of employees nationwide. Facing a slew of allegations around its handling of unionizing efforts, the retailer has claimed the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  is unconstitutional, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/10/starbucks-trader-joes-spacex-challenge-labor-board#:~:text=SpaceX%2C%20Starbucks%2C%20Amazon%20and%20Trader,of%20powers%20by%20exercising%20executive%2C"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filing legal papers challenging the federal agency}}}\uc2  alongside firms including \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Workers who tried to unionize at its store on the Lower East Side of New York lost the election in a 76-76 tied vote in April 2023. But Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s United became the first union to file a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/trader-joes-union-files-to-force-company-to-recognize-union-under-new-nlrb-rule/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 request}}}\uc2  for a bargaining order under the new Cemex framework.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s general counsel issued a complaint consolidating charges filed by workers against Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, and is seeking a bargaining order.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs part of the remedy for the unfair labor practices alleged above, the General Counsel seeks an order requiring respondent to recognize and bargain with the union,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the complaint, issued on 17 September.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chas really thrown a lot into fighting our union\u8221\'20\'1D, Bridget Arend, an organizer who has worked for five years at the Essex store in New York. \u8220\'20\'1CThey wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do that if we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have quite a lot to gain from it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers pushed to unionize in response to issues they experienced through the Covid-19 pandemic, safety problems and having benefits scaled back over the years, according to Arend, who claimed broad support during early efforts to organize. \u8220\'20\'1CTo see how the corporation so harshly stamped that out was really heartbreaking,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s workers at the store \u8220\'20\'1Cknow kind of the extent of the illegal union busting that\u8217\'20\'19s happened\u8221\'20\'1D, Arend claimed. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced it firsthand. But to see it actually being dealt with is really exciting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s declined to comment on the consolidated complaint, or the request for a Cemex bargaining order. The company has until 1 October to respond. An administrative law judge hearing is scheduled to rule on the complaint in January.\par \par \uc2 Sarah Beth Ryther, vice-president of Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s United and a worker at a unionized store in Minneapolis, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a company that has proven time and again that they are unafraid of using really coercive tactics in order to stop workers from exercising their rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve built over the past two years a really strong network of organizers at organized and unorganized stores and that advocacy is slow, but we\u8217\'20\'19re trying through bargaining trying to put as much pressure on the company as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240924ek9o001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
