\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US cannabis company Eaze pays supervisors less than those they oversee, workers say\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,164 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shift supervisors unable to unionize are left in limbo, despite workers claiming low pay and lack of authority\par \par \uc2 The largest cannabis delivery service in the US faces a growing backlash in southern California from shift supervisors who said they are paid less than the workers they supervise, struggle to make ends meet on low and stagnant wages, and are at odds with the company over their right to form a union.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 600 delivery drivers at Eaze in California voted to unionize in 2023 with the \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.greenmarketreport.com/eaze-reaches-deal-with-drivers-union-to-avoid-strike-ahead-of-4-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secured}}}\uc2  a first contract earlier this year after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/apr/15/cannabis-delivery-strike-california-eaze"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatening to strike}}}\uc2  in April.\par \par \uc2 More of the firm\u8217\'20\'19s workers have unionized this year \u8211\'20\'13 an additional 100 drivers and staff at other California depots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufcw.org/actions/victories/cannabis-delivery-workers-in-california-continue-to-join-local-770/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined}}}\uc2 UFCW\uc2  Local 770, while drivers in Sacramento {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/eaze-cannabis-workers-join-teamsters-302101752.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unionized}}}\uc2  in March with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but shift supervisors have been left in limbo.\par \par \uc2 Supervisors at Eaze are awaiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/31-CA-319647"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisions}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 . While the company has argued they are unable to form a union because they are in management roles, workers claimed they should be allowed to unionize due to low pay and a lack of authority.\par \par \uc2 Eaze has been plagued by financial troubles. Its assets were sold at public auction to an unidentified buyer last month. For now, the company claims it is unable to make changes to workers\u8217\'20\'19 pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not making enough money to survive,\u8221\'20\'1D said one shift supervisor at Eaze in the Los Angeles area, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m on food stamps, but those benefits have started to decrease. I can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to repair my car if it needs it. I can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to eat out. And I\u8217\'20\'19m not the only person that\u8217\'20\'19s going through these kinds of financial problems.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers said their most recent pushes for raises to the company have gone ignored, with staff receiving no annual wage increases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe number we were asking for was $27 an hour,\u8221\'20\'1D the shift supervisor recalled, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut we were planning on negotiating down to $25 an hour plus a yearly wage structure. Because, as it is right now, we are functionally running the depots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey see us as the lowest on the totem pole, and they just they don\u8217\'20\'19t feel the need to compensate us. They treat us as if we are extremely replaceable, and they keep adding responsibilities to our plate every day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Staff alleged they have been cross trained to perform duties outside their job scope, without being compensated for doing so, and that they struggle to live on $18 an hour, just above the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dcba.lacounty.gov/newsroom/minimumwage20242025/#:~:text=Here%20are%20seven%20important%20facts,nonprofit%20in%20unincorporated%20LA%20County."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $17.24 an hour minimum wage}}}\uc2  in Los Angeles county.\par \par \uc2 The labor strife at Eaze comes as the cannabis industry has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/us-marijuana-industry-all-time-high-jobs-sales-1891143"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 steadily growing }}}\uc2  in the US, as more states have legalized recreational use. The sector\u8217\'20\'19s workforce rose by 5.4% last year. Annual sales increased in 2023 by 10.4% to $28.8bn. Labor unions have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/31/us-cannabis-industry-union-recognition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing}}}\uc2  workers in the industry to try to ensure this growth and expansion doesn\u8217\'20\'19t come at the expense of workers.\par \par \uc2 Other shift supervisors at Eaze, who also spoke on the condition of anonymity,described their struggles with their current level of pay.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe drivers make more than us now, which, if we\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be their management, makes no sense to us,\u8221\'20\'1D said another supervisor in the Los Angeles area, who explained that drivers make over $20 an hour, plus mileage compensation and tips. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s happened so many times, where a couple days before payday, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I\u8217\'20\'19m going to have enough gas to even make it to work, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve actually borrowed money from drivers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of them are comfortable enough with lending me money like that, but also it\u8217\'20\'19s kind of embarrassing that I\u8217\'20\'19m supposed to be your supervisor, but I need to borrow money from you because I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I can actually make it to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They also alleged the depot where they work has been plagued with pest infestations including mice, roaches, and ants, and claim that they are frequently understaffed and have to take on extra workloads if a coworker calls out or leaves early. This makes it difficult to be able to take breaks, the supervisor said, adding that their depot manager rarely shows up on site because they manage two depots simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen a manager does decide to show up, it feels very much like an absentee parent trying to spend time with their kid,\u8221\'20\'1D they added. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone currently employed is looking for a different job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A third shift supervisor in the Los Angeles area said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like I\u8217\'20\'19m gasping for air some weeks getting simple things like groceries that I have to hold off while I get by on peanut butter and jelly sandwiches.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supervisor said they had been delaying medical care because they could not afford the out of pocket costs, even with health insurance. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re currently fighting for a wage raise, and there\u8217\'20\'19s been no confirmation from the company whatsoever that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get that raise,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CThen you look at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s, for example, standard employees are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/28/california-fast-food-workers-minimum-wages-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making}}}\uc2  $20 an hour, and that\u8217\'20\'19s not even supervisors or managers. That\u8217\'20\'19s standard employees. Nobody should have to come in at a supervisory or management role for minimum wage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An inventory specialist supervisor at Eaze in the Los Angeles area alleged a lack of organization inside the company. \u8220\'20\'1CTo get an answer from somebody in upper management to figure out and process things properly, it\u8217\'20\'19s like a game of telephone,\u8221\'20\'1D they said. \u8220\'20\'1CWho wants to pick up the phone? And who\u8217\'20\'19s going to tell us what what to do? And then it may be the right or wrong answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A unionized driver at Eaze in the Los Angeles area explained the pay discrepancy has caused issues with morale and the work environment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough we won our contract, I\u8217\'20\'19m most disappointed about the fact that they were successful in keeping the supervisors out of the union, because they\u8217\'20\'19re on their own. They have no one to advocate for them, and they\u8217\'20\'19re clearly being taken advantage of,\u8221\'20\'1D the driver said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pretty clear they were given a title to keep them from unionizing. They don\u8217\'20\'19t get paid like management. They\u8217\'20\'19re underpaid and they don\u8217\'20\'19t have authority to really do much.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eaze declined to comment on the record. The company\u8217\'20\'19s assets were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pplgroupllc.com/auction/eaze-technologies-inc-complete-going-concern-business/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sold}}}\uc2  at auction on 6 August amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.greenmarketreport.com/former-green-dragon-owner-sues-eaze-on-auction-day/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ongoing strife}}}\uc2  between investors, including the billionaire founder of Netscape, \uc2 James Clark\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company also said it is currently working with the new ownership to maintain operations and employees. It claimed to be complying with the collective bargaining agreement with \uc2 UFCW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240919ek9j001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
