\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  accused of being \u8216\'20\'18unprepared\u8217\'20\'19 for federal mediation as strike continues\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 665 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par 11:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union members \u8216\'20\'18frustrated\u8217\'20\'19 that company was allegedly unwilling to discuss wages and pensions in negotiations\par \par \uc2 Union officials have accused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/boeing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing}}}\uc2  of being \u8220\'20\'1Cunprepared\u8221\'20\'1D after talks resumed to end the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest strike.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers will be joined on picket lines by the president of the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM)\uc2 , Brian Bryant on Thursday a day after the company announced plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/18/boeing-furloughs-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furlough \u8220\'20\'1Clarge numbers\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  of employees.\par \par \uc2 Around 33,000 workers at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  in Washington and Oregon began striking on 13 September. Union officials have said talks between the two sides have gotten off to a poor start.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Boeing\uc2  must deliver a contract that reflects the hard work and sacrifices that workers have made over the past decade,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bryant. \u8220\'20\'1CThe IAM and our 600,000 members have the backs of every single striking \uc2 Boeing\uc2  worker in this nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/16/boeing-furlough-employees-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a freeze recruitment efforts and is planning to enact furloughs affecting thousands of workers as the strike halts production, and costs to the company reach an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/boeing-union-negotiators-meet-striking-workers-dig-2024-09-17/#:~:text=SEATTLE%2C%20Sept%2017%20(Reuters),estimated%20%24100%20million%20a%20day."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  $100m per day.\par \par \uc2 Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  96% in favor of the strike after rejecting a tentative agreement that included 25% wage increases over the four-year contract, but workers have argued that came with takeaways.\par \par \uc2 IAM Local 751 went into negotiations with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and a federal mediator on Tuesday, but talks reportedly did not initially go well with union officials accusing the company of coming into the negotiation unprepared.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not mince words \u8211\'20\'13 after a full day of mediation, we are frustrated. The company was not prepared and was unwilling to address the issues you\u8217\'20\'19ve made clear are essential for ending this strike: Wages and Pension,\u8221\'20\'1D the union\u8217\'20\'19s negotiating committee said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iam751.org/?zone=/unionactive/private_view_page.cfm&page=IAM2FBoeing20Contract202024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe company doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to be taking mediation seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D the negotiating committee said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting for what is right and just \u8211\'20\'13 for what we have earned over the past 16 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bruce McFarland, an instrumentation technician who has worked at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  for 36 years, explained he waited to get hired for a year after leaving the military because of how coveted jobs at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  were. That is no longer the case, he said, and the company now has difficulty hiring and retaining workers.\par \par \uc2 He explained that in previous contract renewals, workers lost their pension, faced climbing healthcare costs and did not receive wage increases that kept up with inflation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe lost our pension, our buying power stagnated like crazy and our medical was going up,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been losing, and everybody feels it. Covid hit us hard. We\u8217\'20\'19ve just been paying more and more, and what we expect in the contract is no takeaways. So what happens? We get a 25% pay raise over four years that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t match or keep up with the cost of inflation over the last eight years and before, because we came off another bad extension before that, when we were giving the company concessions for the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He compared the proposals to the exorbitant executive pay at \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , the \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden parachutes\u8221\'20\'1D of exiting CEOs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/boeing-ceo-dave-calhoun-exits-saved-by-golden-parachute.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dave Calhoun}}}\uc2  in 2024 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2019/12/24/tech/boeing-ceo-dennis-muilenburg-severance/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dennis Muilenburg }}}\uc2  in 2019, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bhr.stern.nyu.edu/quick-take/boeings-decline-traced-to-decades-of-catering-to-shareholders-above-all-others/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 billions of dollars}}}\uc2  the company has spent on stock buybacks in the last decade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt makes us feel unvalued by the company,\u8221\'20\'1D added McFarland. \u8220\'20\'1CThey took away the bonus, they take away more medical and they make you pay more, and they\u8217\'20\'19ll find a way to make you pay more \u8211\'20\'13 the company is good at that. The pay just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t cut it. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t keep up with inflation and it hurts our members. If the company wants to be world class, it needs to start treating its workers as world class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe days are over of us just rolling over. We did that eight years ago, and we\u8217\'20\'19re not doing that again,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded McFarland. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not backing down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240919ek9j001mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
