\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  threatens strike at \u8216\'20\'18out of control\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  over factory commitments\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2024\par 11:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The union has accused the company of refusing to provide information about 2023 contract promises\par \par \uc2 One of America\u8217\'20\'19s biggest carmakers, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , could face fresh strikes after the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  announced plans for members to vote on authorizing a walkout.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, Shawn Fain, accused executives at the automotive giant of being \u8220\'20\'1Cout of control\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday evening. \u8220\'20\'1CThe company wants you to be scared,\u8221\'20\'1D he told his union\u8217\'20\'19s members, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut we are 100% within our rights and within our power to take strike action if necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 , one of the most powerful trade unions in the US, conducted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of strikes}}}\uc2  against top auto manufacturers last year. After 44 days of action at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-reaches-a-tentative-agreement-with-stellantis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a tentative agreement with the company.\par \par \uc2 Its deal with \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , the \uc2 Jeep\uc2  maker, included significant wage increases, as well as a commitment to bringing back and creating additional jobs at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Belvidere plant in Illinois, which the company had shuttered earlier in the year, resulting in more than 1,300 layoffs. The contract also stipulated that \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  would add a battery plant in the complex and produce the Ram Dakota at the plant, creating thousands of additional jobs.\par \par \uc2 This week, however, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  filed unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , including charges filed by 28 \uc2 UAW\uc2  locals representing thousands of \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  workers, accusing the company of refusing to provide information to the union about the product commitments it made in the 2023 contract.\par \par \uc2 In a live stream, Fain announced that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  will be convening its \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  council in Detroit and holding strike authorization votes at one or more \uc2 UAW\uc2  locals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to save the company from themselves, and to save our communities from the war on the working class,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said, pausing during his speech to drink from a coffee mug with \u8220\'20\'1CBoss\u8217\'20\'19s tears\u8221\'20\'1D labeled on it. \u8220\'20\'1CThe problem isn\u8217\'20\'19t that \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  workers are making too much. The problem is that no amount of profit for \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  executives like [CEO] \uc2 Carlos Tavares\uc2  will ever be enough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  recently announced a decision to lay off workers at its Warren truck assembly plant in Michigan, potentially cutting as many as 2,500 jobs. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has also alleged that \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  reneged on the deal to reopen and expand production at Belvidere, and accused the company of attempting to offshore production of the Dodge Durango, in violation of their agreement.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CShawn Fain continues to allege that the company has violated the contract, but to date has provided no data or information to back up his claims. Instead, he continues to willfully damage the reputation of the company with his public attacks which is helpful to no one including his members. We would all be better served if these issues were addressed across the table with productive, respectful and forward-looking dialogue. A strike does not benefit anyone \u8211\'20\'13 our customers, our dealers, the community and, most importantly, our employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Business/wireStory/uaw-fight-stellantis-escalates-union-files-unfair-labor-113740297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  violating the contract and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/stellantis-confirms-belvidere-investment-plans-are-delayed-2024-08-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed}}}\uc2  it has delayed reopening the Belvidere plant due to market conditions, but still plans on fulfilling the deal, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.autonews.com/manufacturing/stellantis-throws-belvidere-back-upheaval"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 beginning}}}\uc2  in 2027.\par \par \uc2 Fain criticized that explanation, citing backlash toward \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  from the company\u8217\'20\'19s own shareholders and car dealers. \u8220\'20\'1CEither we allow an out-of-control CEO and his billionaire backers who have enjoyed years of record profits to close plant after plant and are continuing to destroy our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cor we stand up, fight back and we rally the American working class to take on corporate greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240918ek9i00003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
