\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares fall as factory workers begin strike; UK interest rates to fall to 3% next year, predicts Goldman \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Graeme Wearden \par \uc2 4,134 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2024\par 05:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready to get back to the table to reach a new agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Boeing\uc2  pledges, as walkout over pay deal begins\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33am BST\par \par \uc2 A late update, just for the record.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares ended up falling 3.7% on the day, to finish at $156.77.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing post\par \par \uc2 Time to wrap up\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/boeing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing}}}\uc2  workers have walked off the job early this morning after voting overwhelmingly to strike for higher pay, halting production of the planemaker\u8217\'20\'19s strongest-selling jet as it wrestles with chronic output delays and mounting debt.\par \par \uc2 The company said on Friday it was ready to talk and \u8220\'20\'1Cget back to the table to reach a new agreement\u8221\'20\'1D as striking workers picketed.\par \par \uc2 Newly installed \uc2 Boeing\uc2  CEO \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/12/boeing-boss-urges-workers-not-to-put-recovery-in-jeopardy-with-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded with workers}}}\uc2  not to go on strike \u8211\'20\'13 the first since 2008 \u8211\'20\'13 ahead of the vote, saying the action would put the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecovery in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 About 33,000 workers in \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US Pacific north-west region late on Thursday voted down a tentative agreement reached between their union and the company that included a 25% pay increase over four years. They voted in favor of a strike beginning on Friday at midnight Pacific time (8am UK time), which will halt production of the 737 Max.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers voted 94.6% to reject the agreement, and 96% in favor of striking.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing workers walk off the job after vote to strike and rejecting pay deal}}}\par \par \uc2 News of the strike knocked \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares down by 2% in early trading; they\u8217\'20\'19ve since recovered slightly, and are down 0.9% at $161.41.\par \par \uc2 In other news\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The gold price has hit a new alltime high of $2,583.29 per ounce, as the US dollar weakens ahead of an expected cut to US interest rates next week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/sep/13/boeing-factory-workers-vote-to-strike-threatening-aircraft-deliveries-gold-hits-record-high-business-live?page=with:block-66e4228e8f082dce7ae32c64#block-66e4228e8f082dce7ae32c64"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Goldman Sachs have predicted}}}\uc2  that UK interest rates will have been slashed to 3% in a year\u8217\'20\'19s time, down from 5% today.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2024/sep/13/plans-unveiled-for-cheaper-high-speed-alternative-to-scrapped-hs2-northern-leg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plans unveiled for cheaper high-speed alternative to scrapped HS2 northern leg}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/uk-government-to-buy-electricity-system-operator-from-national-grid-for-630m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK government to buy electricity system operator from National Grid for \u163\'00\'A3630m}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/imf-plan-to-go-to-russia-to-assess-economy-prompts-dismay-across-europe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IMF plan to visit Russia to assess economy prompts dismay across Europe}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/vodafone-three-merger-tens-of-millions-could-face-higher-bills-says-uk-watchdog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vodafone-Three merger: tens of millions could face higher bills, says UK watchdog}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/china-pwc-47m-fine-six-month-ban-evergrande-audit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China gives PwC record \u163\'00\'A347m fine and six-month ban over Evergrande}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/lloyds-plans-to-shut-another-55-bank-branches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lloyds plans to shut another 55 bank branches}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are new photos from the picket line outside \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assembly plant in Renton this morning:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Airlines who have placed orders for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 737 MAX jet will be watching the strike, and trying to anticipate if their deliveries will be delayed.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has more than 4,700 of the jets on order, with \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 United Airlines\uc2 , and Lion Air the top three customers awaiting deliveries, according to aviation data provider Cirium. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/factbox-boeing-strike-puts-spotlight-150017298.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back on Wall Street, \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are recovering some of their earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re still in the red, though; down 0.9% at $161.30.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 CFM\uc2 , who are the sole-source engine supplier for the 737 MAX, said there was no immediate impact to its operations from the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The strike at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  could send ripples through the US aerospace industry, knocking demand for the components used to build its planes.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said \uc2 Boeing\uc2  could adjust the pace at which it takes material.\par \par \uc2 Analyst Seth M. Seifman said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt a minimum, a prolonged strike could affect supplier growth expectations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://usw2.nyl.as/t1/273/blg74xug83n3l8wjtfl4fxvtb/1/76985f80557a134bd7385ecaa1c034680ff28a4207068bd0ba1577a0cc780e71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jungho Suh}}}\uc2  , a teaching assistant professor of management at the George Washington University School of Business, says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers\u8217\'20\'19 overwhelming vote to strike underscores a broader discontent within labor forces, despite offers of increased pay and benefits. It reflects a deeper struggle for dignity, equity, and sustainable work conditions in a high-stakes industry.\par \par \uc2 As negotiations unfold, \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stakeholders find themselves at a pivotal moment, grappling with the reality of how advanced technology is reshaping the workplace and prompting urgent questions about the future of work and equitable labor conditions in the age of artificial intelligence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Just in: US consumer confidence has picked up a little this month.\par \par \uc2 The latest consumer sentiment index, from the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 , has risen to 69.0 from 67.9 in August.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a little higher than expected:\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/US?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #US}}}\uc2  Michigan Consumer Sentiment for Sep preliminary is at 69.0, beating expectations (68) and up from August (67.9). Reflects improving consumer confidence as inflation cools and economic outlook steadies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Economy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Economy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/USA?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #USA}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Inflation?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Inflation}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Market?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Market}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Equity Insights (@Fundamenta21972) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Fundamenta21972/status/1834593911916154958?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 After a choppy open, \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are down 2% at $159.55.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares fall after staff vote for strike\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Boeing\uc2  have dropped at the start of trading in New York, as investor react to the strike action underway at its factories.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are down 1.5% in early trading, to $160.53, following last night\u8217\'20\'19s news that staff had voted to reject a pay deal, and to go on strike.\par \par \uc2 They are the top faller on the Dow Jones industrial average this morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrBOEING SHARES FALL 1.5% AFTER U.S. FACTORY WORKERS STRIKE, HALTING 737 MAX PRODUCTION {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 *Walter Bloomberg (@DeItaone) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DeItaone/status/1834586149982978126?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 That takes their losses so far this year to over 38%.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean Pierre\uc2  has said the Biden administration was in touch with both sides in the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  pay dispute.\par \par \uc2 She says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to encourage both parties to negotiate in that way, in good faith and reaching a strong contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg Intelligence analyst \uc2 George Ferguson\uc2  predicts \uc2 Boeing\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Csoon\u8221\'20\'1D make a better offer to its employees, to end the strike and get them back to work.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BA}}}\uc2  "needs the workers right now more than the workers need \uc2 Boeing\uc2 ," Bloomberg Intelligence analyst \uc2 George Ferguson\uc2  says. "I don't think it's going to be a long strike because I think \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is going to have to go back and make their offer better, soon." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iBEiyuYzsQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iBEiyuYzsQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yahoo Finance (@YahooFinance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YahooFinance/status/1834580836974301628?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of workers manned picket lines at the Renton factory outside of Seattle that makes \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top-selling aircraft, the 737 Max, as the strike began, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-09-13/boeing-factory-union-workers-reject-contract-setting-stage-for-strike?sref=Xl91GI8N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2 , adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been an amazing experience to be a part of this and all the camaraderie,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Solis, 19, who just celebrated his one-year anniversary at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and was getting his first taste of a strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve heard all sorts of things from different people, but the way that the company is acting just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem very fair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Financial Times points out that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/sep/13/boeing-factory-workers-vote-to-strike-threatening-aircraft-deliveries-gold-hits-record-high-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66e3d48b8f08c69019f64762#block-66e3d48b8f08c69019f64762"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Boeing strike}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/boeing-strike-machinists-contract-9f61a7d48675d1c3517233d40d4ec2b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began just after midnight, Pacific time}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could hurt the company\u8217\'20\'19s financial postion.\par \par \uc2 The FT {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/f0a6d5a8-63b0-41f2-9c96-9991b3060f82"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explains}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The strike will limit \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to deliver planes, slowing its cash flow after it reported an $8.3bn outflow during the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s credit rating stands one notch above junk, and avoiding a downgrade depends on its ability to generate cash from deliveries.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 UK interest rates to fall to 3% in a year, predicts \uc2 Goldman Sachs\par \par \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  have predicted that UK interest rates will have been slashed to 3% in a year\u8217\'20\'19s time, down from 5% today.\par \par \uc2 In a new research note today, Goldman analyst James Moberly forecasts that the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  will reconsider its cautious approach later this year.\par \par \uc2 Moberly writes:\par \par \uc2 With Bank Rate currently well above our terminal rate forecast, we see compelling reasons for the MPC to accelerate the pace of easing as wage pressures moderate and underlying services inflation falls back.\par \par \uc2 We therefore expect the Bank to cut sequentially from November until Bank Rate reaches 3% in September 2025.\par \par \uc2 Goldman also expect the Bank will vote to leave interest rates on hold at 5% at next week\u8217\'20\'19s meeting. They anticipate a 7-2 split on the monetary policy committee, with just deputy governor Sir \uc2 Dave Ramsden\uc2  and external member Swati Dhingra voting for a cut to 4.75%.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pwc.com/gx/en/news-room/press-releases/2024/pwc-network-statement-regarding-pwc-zhong-tian-administrative-penalties.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PwC}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pwc.com/gx/en/news-room/press-releases/2024/pwc-network-statement-regarding-pwc-zhong-tian-administrative-penalties.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has said}}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdisappointed by PwC Zhong Tian\u8217\'20\'19s audit work of Hengda Real Estate, \uc2 Evergrande\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mainland division, following this morning\u8217\'20\'19s fine and ban in China ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/sep/13/boeing-factory-workers-vote-to-strike-threatening-aircraft-deliveries-gold-hits-record-high-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66e3f8aa8f08c69019f6488a#block-66e3f8aa8f08c69019f6488a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see earlier post}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 This work \u8220\'20\'1Cfell unacceptably below the standards we expect of member firms of the \uc2 PwC\uc2  network,\u8221\'20\'1D the company says.\par \par \uc2 It added that it sacked six partners; a further five staff who were directly involved in the Hengda audit work either left or were fired.\par \par \uc2 Mohamed Kande\uc2 , global chair of \uc2 PwC\uc2 , said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe work performed by PwC Zhong Tian\u8217\'20\'19s Hengda audit team fell well below our high expectations and was completely unacceptable. It is not representative of what we stand for as a network and there is no room for this at \uc2 PwC.\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/china-pwc-47m-fine-six-month-ban-evergrande-audit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China gives PwC \u163\'00\'A347m fine and six-month ban over Evergrande}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia raises interest rates from 18% to 19%\par \par \uc2 Ovee in Moscow, \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s central bank\uc2  has raised interest rates to 19%.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia voted to increase its bench mark rate by one percentage point, due to concerns over high inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 The Bank says:\par \par \uc2 By the end of 2024, annual inflation is likely to exceed the July forecast range of 6.5\u8211\'20\'137.0%. Growth in domestic demand is still significantly outstripping the capabilities to expand the supply of goods and services.\par \par \uc2 It hopes that tightening monetary policy will reduce inflation expectations and help bring inflation down to its 4% target in 2024.\par \par \uc2 It also hints that further tightening may be needed, saying:\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia holds open the prospect of increasing the key rate at its upcoming meeting. According to the Bank of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s forecast, given the monetary policy stance, annual inflation will decline to 4.0\u8211\'20\'134.5% in 2025 and stay close to 4% further on.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Jefferies analyst Chloe Lemarie has warned that production levels of \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 737 MAX jet could be hit if the strike runs for a long time.\par \par \uc2 In a research note, Lemarie says:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe key question now is on the duration of the strike given the gap between the proposed wage increase and union members request.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The deal rejected by \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employees yesterday was worth 25% over four years, and included a $3,000 signing on bonus \u8211\'20\'13 and a pledge to build the company\u8217\'20\'19s next commercial jet in Seattle.\par \par \uc2 The company union had initially demand for pay raises of 40% over three years.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42am BST\par \par \uc2 UK public's inflation expectations fall to 3-year low\par \par \uc2 Almost half the UK public believe interest rates are too high, a new survey shows.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of England\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest quarterly survey of public attitudes to inflation, released this morning, shows that 42% of respondents thought that interest rates should \u8216\'20\'18go down\u8217\'20\'19. That matches the reading back in May.\par \par \uc2 Just 9% of respondents think rates should \u8216\'20\'18go up\u8217\'20\'19, down from 10% in May, while 28% thought interest rates should \u8216\'20\'18stay where they are\u8217\'20\'19 (up from 24%).\par \par \uc2 The Bank\u8217\'20\'19s next interest rate meeting is next week; the financial markets indicate there\u8217\'20\'19s a 77% chance that rate are left on hold.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s survey also found that people expect inflation to average 2.7% over the next year, down from the 2.8% expected in May [inflation was 2.2% in July]. That\u8217\'20\'19s the lowest since August 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers have begun picketing outside the company\u8217\'20\'19s factory in Washington, as the strike begins.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/boeing-strike-machinists-contract-9f61a7d48675d1c3517233d40d4ec2b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Outside the Renton factory, people stood with signs reading, \u8220\'20\'1CHistoric contract my ass\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CHave you seen the damn housing prices?\u8221\'20\'1D Car horns honked and a boom box played songs such as Twisted Sister\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re Not Gonna Take It\u8221\'20\'1D and Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CLook What You Made Me Do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Liam Byrne re-elected as Business & Trade Committee chair\par \par \uc2 Back in the UK, Liam Byrne MP has been re-elected as chair of parliament\u8217\'20\'19s Business and Trade Committee.\par \par \uc2 Byrne also let the committee, which scrutinises the policy, spending and administration of the \uc2 Department for Business and Trade\uc2  and its public bodies, in the last parliament.\par \par \uc2 He says it\u8217\'20\'19s a huge honour to be re-elected, adding:\par \par \uc2 MPs welcomed the hard-hitting style we pioneered in the last parliament, but, above all, the whole House wants to rebuild an opportunity economy in Britain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople know that the Business and Trade Committee is the key space in parliament where we can hold ministers to account and, crucially, find that overlapping consensus about the big steps our great nation needs to take to deliver the fastest growth in the G7, rebuild trade alliances with our allies and ensure that wealth is fairly shared. I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to get started.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Byrne was pushed quite close in the voting by his fellow Labour MP, Matt Western, who also ran for the job.\par \par \uc2 Three hundred and two MPs voted for Byrne, while Western, the Labour MP for Warwick and Leamington, received 251 votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42am BST\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  fined and banned for six months in China over \uc2 Evergrande\uc2  audit\par \par \uc2 Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s finance ministry\uc2  has imposed a six-month business suspension on \uc2 PwC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s auditing unit in mainland China over the auditing of \uc2 Evergrande\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  has also been hit with financial penalties totalling around \u163\'00\'A347m.\par \par \uc2 Reuters has the details:\par \par \uc2 The ministry also imposed a fine of 116 million yuan (\u163\'00\'A312m) on PwC Zhong Tian LLP, the registered accounting entity and the main onshore arm of \uc2 PwC\uc2  in China, according to a statement on the MOF website.\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s securities regulator said in a separate statement that it confiscated the unit\u8217\'20\'19s revenue involved in the \uc2 Evergrande\uc2  case totalling 27.7 million yuan (\u163\'00\'A33m) and fined the unit 297 million yuan (\u163\'00\'A332m).\par \par \uc2 Such a ban had been expected:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/22/pwc-expecting-six-month-china-ban-over-evergrande-audit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PwC expecting six-month China ban over Evergrande audit}}}\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  has been in hot water in China since Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s securities regulator said that \uc2 Evergrande\uc2  had inflated its revenues by almost $80bn (\u163\'00\'A361.6bn) in 2019 and 2020, before its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/jan/29/evergrande-collapse-liquidation-china-debt-developer-property-giant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapse in January}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares fall 4% in premarket\par \par \uc2 Shares in \uc2 Boeing\uc2  are on track to fall when Wall Street opens later today.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/premarket.asp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Premarket trading}}}\uc2  has just begun, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/investing/stock/ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing\u8217\'20\'19s shares have fallen by over 4%}}}\uc2  as investors react to the strike which has hit its operations today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Three's CEOs disagree with CMA's findings\par \par \uc2 The bosses of \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Three have just declared that they disagree with the \uc2 Competition and Markets Authority\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s provisional findings against their merger ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/sep/13/boeing-factory-workers-vote-to-strike-threatening-aircraft-deliveries-gold-hits-record-high-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-66e3d9e38f082dce7ae32921#block-66e3d9e38f082dce7ae32921"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see earlier post}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Margherita Della Valle\uc2  has told reporters that the merger would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ccatalyst for change\u8221\'20\'1D, that would lead to more competition and unlock \u163\'00\'A311bn of investment.\par \par \uc2 Della Valle also points out that CMA\u8217\'20\'19s decision isn\u8217\'20\'19t final; \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  is looking forward to working with the regulator to get final approval, she says.\par \par \uc2 Della Valle argues that combining \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Three would \u8220\'20\'1Ctake the handbrake off\u8221\'20\'1D the UK\u8217\'20\'19s connectivity, and build \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world-class infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D the country deserves.\par \par \uc2 She disagrees with the CMA\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the deal could lead to higher prices, insisting that there are no plans to change pricing strategies.\par \par \uc2 Della Valle pledges :\par \par \uc2 We not see the possibiltiy of pricing increasing going forward.\par \par \uc2 Robert Finnegan\uc2 , the CEO of Three UK, tells the media that the deal would bring \u8220\'20\'1Cbest in class 5G\u8221\'20\'1D to the UK.\par \par \uc2 Both CEOs also reject the CMA\u8217\'20\'19s argument that the deal could hurt wholesale telecoms customers (who buy network capacity from operators). They argue that a combined \uc2 Vodafone\uc2 -Three would be a stronger competitor with other wholesale providers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike began just after midnight on the west cost of the US , Dow Jones Newswiresreports, saying:\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s biggest labor union went on strike, halting production of its best-selling jets and dealing the latest blow to the struggling aerospace giant.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of machinists that build \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 737, 777 and 767 jets walked off the job shortly after midnight Pacific time Friday, after rejecting a labor deal struck between the union\u8217\'20\'19s leaders and \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executives. The contract offered 25% wage increases over four years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26am BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not immediately clear how long the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike will last for, or how soon talks might resume.\par \par \uc2 Jon Holden, who headed the negotiations for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s largest union, told reporters in the US:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get back to the table as quickly as we can.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is something that we take one day at a time, one week at a time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Photos \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's strike vote\par \par \uc2 Here are some photos of \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers voting on their pay deal yesterday:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 : We are ready to get back to the table and agree a deal\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has declared that it is ready to return to negotiations with its worker to agree a pay deal.\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued after staff voted to strike, the company says:\par \par \uc2 The message was clear that the tentative agreement we reached with IAM leadership was not acceptable to the members.\par \par \uc2 We remain committed to resetting our relationship with our employees and the union and we are ready to get back to the table to reach a new agreement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31am BST\par \par \uc2 CMA concerned about \uc2 Vodafone\uc2 -Three deal\par \par \uc2 Newsflash: Britain\u8217\'20\'19s competition regulator has raised concerns over the proposed merger of two mobile phone companies.\par \par \uc2 The Competition and Markets Authority (CMA)\uc2  has warned this morning that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jun/14/vodafone-and-three-agree-merger-to-form-uk-largest-mobile-operator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vodafone\u8217\'20\'19s $19bn merger with Three UK}}}\uc2  could hurt customers.\par \par \uc2 The deal could lead to \u8220\'20\'1Ctens of millions of mobile customers having to pay more\u8221\'20\'1D for their services, the CMA says, as it sets out its provisional view on the merger.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, it also flags that the merger could improve the quality of mobile networks.\par \par \uc2 The competition watchdog says:\par \par \uc2 The CMA has particular concerns that higher bills or reduced services would negatively affect those customers least able to afford mobile services as well as those who might have to pay more for improvements in network quality they do not value.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the CMA has provisionally concluded that the merger would lead to a substantial lessening of competition in the UK \u8211\'20\'13 in both retail and wholesale mobile markets.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s potentially a blow to \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Three\u8217\'20\'19s hopes. But, this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a final decision \u8211\'20\'13 the CMA is going to consult, and see what commitments could be made to adress its concerns.\par \par \uc2 But, it retains the option to prohibit the merger if it\u8217\'20\'19s not satisfied.\par \par \uc2 Stuart McIntosh\uc2 , chair of the inquiry group leading the investigation, says\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve taken a thorough, considered approach to investigating this merger, weighing up the investment the companies say they will make in enhancing network quality and boosting 5G connectivity against the significant costs to customers and rival virtual networks.\par \par \uc2 We will now consider how \uc2 Vodafone\uc2  and Three might address our concerns about the likely impact of the merger on retail and wholesale customers while securing the potential longer-term benefits of the merger, including by guaranteeing future network investments.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Unite union\uc2  has urged the CMA to block the deal, fearing it would lead to job losses and higher prices.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/22/vodafone-merger-three-customers-unable-find-cheaper-deals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vodafone merger \u8216\'20\'18could leave 1m Three customers unable to find cheaper deals\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  factory workers vote to strike, threatening aircraft deliveries\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is facing possible delays to the production of some planes after machinists at the troubled aircraft manufacturer voted to go on strike.\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of workers at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  have voted to reject a new contract, which would have raised their pay by 25% over four years, and to go on strike instead \u8211\'20\'13 the first walkout in 16 years.\par \par \uc2 The move puts pressure on the aircraft manufacturer to offer more generous terms, and is a fresh blow to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  as it tries to raise quality following problems with its manufacturing processes.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  said 94.6% of voting workers rejected a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/boeing-labor-contract-machinists-strike-4fd6c9055b126ad78a6c8facc12e87d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contract}}}\uc2  and 96% approved the strike \u8212\'20\'14 easily surpassing a two-thirds requirement. IAM District 751 represents over 30,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers in Washington state\par \par \uc2 The strike was set to begin today in the US.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  CEO \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/12/boeing-boss-urges-workers-not-to-put-recovery-in-jeopardy-with-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded with workers}}}\uc2  not to go on strike, warning it would put the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecovery in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/13/boeing-union-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing workers vote to strike after rejecting pay deal}}}\par \par \uc2 S&P Global Ratings\uc2  has flagged that an extended worker strike could delay the planemaker\u8217\'20\'19s recovery and hurt its overall credit rating.\par \par \uc2 Ben Tsocanos, aerospace director at \uc2 S&P Global Ratings\uc2 , believes the strike could undermine \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ability to reach its target of increasing MAX jet production to 38 planes a month by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Tsocanos added:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA shorter strike (along the lines of the situation at Spirit Aero last summer where union leadership accepted the company\u8217\'20\'19s offer and membership rejected it) would probably be manageable for the company and the rating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Introduction: Gold price rises to new record high\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our rolling coverage of business, the financial markets and the world economy.\par \par \uc2 Optimism that the US central bank will finally start cutting interest rates next week has helped to push the gold price to a new alltime high.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold has hit a record high of $2,570.03 per ounce this morning, adding to strong gains on Thursday. Bullion has gained about 3% so far this week, and 25% so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The gold price was pushed up by a weakening US dollar, which is close to its lowest level of 2024.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped as investors ponder how aggressively the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  will cut borrowing costs. A cut \u8211\'20\'13 the first in the current cycle \u8211\'20\'13 next week is widely expected, but traders are split between anticipating a small, quarter-point cut or a larger half-point reduction to the Federal funds rate.\par \par \uc2 enltrOdds of a 50+ bps rate cut just shot up to 25%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rAy7vJL85Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rAy7vJL85Q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Polymarket (@Polymarket) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Polymarket/status/1834349312303620276?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kyle Rodda, senior financial market analyst at capital.com, explains:\par \par \uc2 The weaker Dollar provided room for gold to finally break-out to new record highs. Although yields have lifted as the markets price-out a 50 point move from the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2 , the drop in the Greenback was enough to spark a break-out for the yellow metal from its recent range.\par \par \uc2 The outlook and price-action remains bullish for gold, even if sentiment might be erring on the excessively bullish side.\par \par \uc2 The agenda\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 8.30am: Eurozone finance ministers hold a Eurogroup meeting in Budapest\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 9.30am BST: \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 /\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  Inflation Attitudes Survey\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 10am BST: Eurozone industrial production data for July\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 3pm BST: \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US consumer confidence report\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240913ek9d000s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
