\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Sun and Daily Mail publishers cut jobs in US digital operations\b0\par\par\uc2 Alexandra Topping and Nadeem Badshah \par \uc2 284 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par 18:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Daily Mail owner says it has made \u8216\'20\'18a small number\u8217\'20\'19 of job cuts in US, and US Sun is also cutting back\par \par \uc2 The publishers of the Sun and the Daily Mail are cutting jobs in their American digital operations amid financial pressure on the industry.\par \par \uc2 News UK\uc2 , the publisher of the Sun, and \uc2 DMGT\uc2 , the owner of the Mail, this week announced internal restructuring of their online divisions, Sky News reported.\par \par \uc2 DMGT\uc2  launched Dailymail.com in the US in 2010. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  understands that the number of job losses in the Mail\u8217\'20\'19s US newsroom, which employs 200 people in New York, is in the mid teens.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Associated Newspapers\uc2 , a subsidiary of \uc2 DMGT\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made a small number of job cuts in some areas of our US editorial department. This was a difficult, but necessary decision, which will enable us to continue to invest in areas where we can grow our audience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Sun launched an American edition online in January 2020 and it is thought to employ about 100 people.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 News UK\uc2  spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe US Sun has been an incredibly successful business, driving billions of page views; however, the digital landscape has experienced seismic change in the last 12 months and we need to reset the strategy and resize the team to secure the long-term, sustainable future for the Sun\u8217\'20\'19s business in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A source close to \uc2 News UK\uc2  denied suggestions that 80% of jobs would be cut, saying it was a significantly smaller percentage and that the restructuring would give more prominence to video journalism.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240913ek9d002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
