\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers go on strike as White House calls for \u8216\'20\'18good faith\u8217\'20\'19 negotiations\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 819 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2024\par 16:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 44\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US Pacific north-west region workers voted 96% in favor of the strike and walked off the job early on Friday\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/boeing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boeing}}}\uc2  workers walked off the job early on Friday after voting overwhelmingly to strike for higher pay, halting production of the planemaker\u8217\'20\'19s strongest-selling jet as it wrestles with chronic output delays and mounting debt.\par \par \uc2 The company said on Friday it was ready to talk and \u8220\'20\'1Cget back to the table to reach a new agreement\u8221\'20\'1D as striking workers picketed.\par \par \uc2 The newly installed \uc2 Boeing\uc2  CEO \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/12/boeing-boss-urges-workers-not-to-put-recovery-in-jeopardy-with-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded with workers}}}\uc2  not to go on strike \u8211\'20\'13 the first since 2008 \u8211\'20\'13 ahead of the vote, saying the action would put the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecovery in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 About 33,000 workers in \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US Pacific north-west region late on Thursday voted down a tentative agreement reached between their union and the company that included a 25% pay increase over four years. They voted in favor of a strike beginning on Friday at midnight Pacific time (7am GMT), which will halt production of the 737 Max.\par \par \uc2 Early on Friday afternoon, the White House said it was in contact with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  representing the strikers and that it hoped they can reach a contract deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe encourage them to negotiate in good faith \u8211\'20\'13 toward an agreement that gives employees the benefits they deserve and makes the company stronger,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House spokesperson Robyn Patterson said.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers voted 94.6% to reject the agreement, and 96% in favor of striking.\par \par \uc2 Breaking: unionized \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers have approved a strike. IAM 751 says 33,000+ workers in Washington will stop work at midnight. People here say the pay & benefits in the company's latest offer isn't enough to live on. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9VI0jPdmoJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9VI0jPdmoJ}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Casey Martin (@caseyworks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/caseyworks/status/1834450008315150574?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about respect, this is about addressing the past, and this is about fighting for our future,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jon Holden, who headed the negotiations for the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM)\uc2 , \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s largest union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe strike at midnight,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, as members in the union hall cheered and chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CStrike! Strike! Strike!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement released after the vote, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to get back to the table\u8221\'20\'1D to negotiate a deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe message was clear that the tentative agreement we reached with IAM leadership was not acceptable to the members. We remain committed to resetting our relationship with our employees and the union and we are ready to get back to the table to reach a new agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a tentative agreement had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/sep/09/boeing-union-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached}}}\uc2  between the IAM and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  on 8 September after marathon bargaining sessions over the weekend, ahead of the contract expiration on Thursday. The agreement included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iam751.org/?zone=/unionactive/private_view_page.cfm&page=IAM2FBoeing20Contract202024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25% }}}\uc2  pay increases over the four-year contract, short of the 40% increase pushed by the union.\par \par \uc2 Union leadership {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iam751.org/?zone=/unionactive/private_view_page.cfm&page=IAM2FBoeing20Contract202024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recommended }}}\uc2  ratification but the local union president, Jon Holden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seattletimes.com/business/boeing-machinists-union-chief-expects-members-will-reject-deal-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  the Seattle Times he expected members to reject the agreement given the overwhelming negative response to it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Boeing\uc2  is saying they are in a tough spot recovering yet their executive salaries haven\u8217\'20\'19t changed. COO [chief operating officer] \uc2 Stephanie Pope{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www1.salary.com/Stephanie-F-Pope-Salary-Bonus-Stock-Options-for-BOEING-CO.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 makes}}}\uc2  over $300,000 every two weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  mechanic who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. They voted down the contract in favor of going on strike. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is much deeper than pay and benefits. It is \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s culture. We are a family here in my shop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.king5.com/article/tech/science/aerospace/boeing/machinists-protest-unions-tentative-deal-with-boeing/281-6a94dd88-b48f-4c2d-8ba5-e3f898194d14"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally}}}\uc2  protesting against the tentative agreement outside \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s production facility in Everett, Washington, earlier this week. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bhr.stern.nyu.edu/quick-take/boeings-decline-traced-to-decades-of-catering-to-shareholders-above-all-others/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $68bn}}}\uc2  on stock buy-backs and dividends since 2010.\par \par \uc2 The company has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/08/boeing-2018-2019-crashes-victims-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mired in scandal}}}\uc2  but has still paid huge salaries to top executives. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/25/boeing-ceo-dave-calhoun-resign-cabin-panel-blowout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Outgoing}}}\uc2  CEO \uc2 Dave Calhoun\uc2  received a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-04-05/boeing-ceo-s-2023-pay-soared-45-before-blowout-unleashed-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 45%}}}\uc2  increase in 2023, to nearly $33m in 2023. Their ousted former CEO, \uc2 Dennis Muilenburg\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/boeing-737-max-ceo-severance/corrected-update-2-boeings-ousted-ceo-departs-with-62-mln-even-without-severance-pay-idUKL4N29F3II/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left}}}\uc2  with a golden parachute of $62m.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the vote, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  pleaded with workers to approve the tentative agreement and not go on strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the reaction to our tentative agreement with the IAM has been passionate. I understand and respect that passion, but I ask you not to sacrifice the opportunity to secure our future together, because of the frustrations of the past,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Ortberg in a message to \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employees in Washington and Oregon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , it is no secret that our business is in a difficult period, in part due to our own mistakes in the past. Working together, I know that we can get back on track, but a strike would put our shared recovery in jeopardy, further eroding trust with our customers and hurting our ability to determine our future together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240913ek9d000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
