\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  boss tells workers strike would \u8216\'20\'18put recovery in jeopardy\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe \par \uc2 550 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2024\par 10:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  in last-minute plea to assembly staff before vote on 25% pay offer during \u8216\'20\'18difficult period\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new chief executive, \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2 , has pleaded with workers to not go on strike, before a crucial union vote, saying the action would put the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecovery in jeopardy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 About 33,000 aircraft assembly workers, most of them in the Seattle area, are to vote on Thursday on a pay offer that includes rises {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/sep/09/boeing-union-deal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worth 25% over four years}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the members of the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers (IAM)\uc2  reject the contract offer and two-thirds of them vote to strike, a stoppage would start in the early hours of Friday, just after midnight in Seattle.\par \par \uc2 Shutting down production would not cause flight cancellations but would be another blow to \uc2 Boeing\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reputation and finances. The aircraft maker has lurched from crisis to crisis since two 737 Max airliners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jul/08/boeing-2018-2019-crashes-victims-family#:~:text=It%20was%20the%20second%20fatal,189%20people%20on%20board%20died.&text=%E2%80%9CFor%20others%2C%20I%20guess%20they,or%20something%2C%E2%80%9D%20Kiernan%20said."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crashed in 2018 and 2019}}}\uc2 , killing 346 people. Then in January, a cabin panel blew out of a Max mid-flight, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/apr/09/boeing-whistleblower-faa-investigation-report%20."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the planemaker was investigated}}}\uc2  after several whistleblowers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/apr/17/boeing-whistleblower-safety-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came forward with allegations}}}\uc2  about their experiences working for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and the safety of its planes.\par \par \uc2 Ortberg told machinists on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CNo one wins\u8221\'20\'1D in a strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , it is no secret that our business is in a difficult period, in part due to our own mistakes in the past,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWorking together, I know that we can get back on track, but a strike would put our shared recovery in jeopardy, further eroding trust with our customers and hurting our ability to determine our future together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although the bargaining committee that negotiated the contract recommended members approve it, Jon Holden, the IAM District 751 president, who represents more than 32,000 aerospace workers at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and other suppliers, said earlier this week that the strike vote would go ahead. Many workers have complained about the deal on social media.\par \par \uc2 Voting will take place at union halls in Washington state, Portland, Oregon, and other locations, with results expected to be released on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 Holden told members on Monday that the union obtained everything possible in bargaining and recommended approval of the deal \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause we can\u8217\'20\'19t guarantee we can achieve more in a strike\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The deal fell short of the union\u8217\'20\'19s initial demand for pay raises of 40% over three years. Many workers are also unhappy about their pensions.\par \par \uc2 A strike would halt production of the 737 Max, the company\u8217\'20\'19s bestselling airliner, along with the 777 jet and the 767 cargo plane at factories in Everett and Renton, Washington, near Seattle. It is not expected to affect \uc2 Boeing\uc2  787 Dreamliners, which are built by non-union workers in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 The Jefferies analyst Chloe Lemarie said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis represents a key risk for 737 Max production levels.\u8221\'20\'1D Over time, the disruption could lead to market share losses to rival \uc2 Airbus\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s A320neo, she said.\par \par \uc2 Cai von Rumohr\uc2 , a senior aerospace analyst at TD Cowen, said a strike could last into mid-November, which could cost \uc2 Boeing\uc2  up to $3.5bn (\u163\'00\'A32.7bn) in cashflow because the company gets about 60% of the sale price when it delivers a plane to the buyer.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240912ek9c001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
