\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morning Mail: PIs used in family violence cases, Republican dismay after debate, Clover Moore rejects \u8216\'20\'18ageism\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Farrer \par \uc2 1,124 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par 21:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Want to get this in your inbox every weekday? Sign up for the Morning Mail here, and finish your day with our Afternoon Update newsletter\par \par \uc2 Morning everyone. In our top story today we ask why John Edwards, who killed his two children in 2018, was able to hire private investigators, despite his long history of domestic violence.\par \par \uc2 Plus: a new survey shows nearly half of young people gambled in the past year, what to make of Elle Macpherson and the wellness industry, and we have reports and analysis on the fallout from the US presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 Australia\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Clover in? |\par \par \uc2 Clover Moore says ageism and sexism are at play as she seeks a record sixth term as the lord mayor of Sydney after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/sep/12/clover-moore-sydney-lord-mayor-nsw-council-elections-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost desperate\u8221\'20\'1D campaign}}}\uc2  she has experienced in decades of public life.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doxing bill |\par \par \uc2 The Albanese government is introducing a new bill to outlaw online doxing \u8211\'20\'13 the malicious use or exposure of personal data \u8211\'20\'13 with the offence {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/sep/11/government-doxing-bill-prison-time-new-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 punishable by up to seven years}}}\uc2 . But Labor has backed down on its proposal to outlaw hate speech and vilification against minority groups.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gambling |\par \par \uc2 About a third of young adults who gambled in the last year started punting before the age of 18, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/sep/11/nearly-half-of-young-people-gambled-in-past-year-survey-shows-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new survey shows}}}\uc2 , and those who started young experienced greater harms from gambling as an adult. It also shows almost half of 16- to 35-year-olds had a bet in the past year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Melbourne clashes |\par \par \uc2 While violent clashes between anti-war activists and police raged outside, the scene inside Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s weapons expo was much more serene, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/sep/11/at-melbournes-weapons-expo-arms-dealers-snack-on-popcorn-a-grenades-throw-from-tanks-and-autonomous-robots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Nino Bucci}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Education |\par \par \uc2 All high school students in New South Wales will be studying Aboriginal people\u8217\'20\'19s experiences of colonisation by 2027, including the Frontier Wars and the concept of terra nullius, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/sep/12/nsw-new-school-curricula-colonisation-aboriginal-resistance-prue-car"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under the state\u8217\'20\'19s reformed syllabuses}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 World\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican dismay |\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-republican-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 damage control mode }}}\uc2  amid dismay among supporters over his presidential debate performance. Both candidates attended the 9/11 attack commemoration in New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/harris-trump-9-11-commemoration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where they shook hands again}}}\uc2  after meeting for the first time the previous evening. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tiny social media empire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/sep/11/trump-media-stock-falls-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slumped to fresh lows }}}\uc2  on the stock market. Follow all the developments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/sep/11/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-presidential-debate-reaction-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at our live blog}}}\uc2 . And could cats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/feline-frenzy-could-cats-swing-the-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 really swing the outcome of the election?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mexican standoff |\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s Senate has approved {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/11/mexico-senate-approve-changes-judiciary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an overhaul of the judiciary }}}\uc2  paving the way for all judges to stand for election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2024/sep/11/protesters-storm-mexicos-senate-after-lawmakers-approve-plan-to-overhaul-judiciary-video-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bringing angry protests }}}\uc2  from opponents who fear it will threaten the democracy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18outraged\u8217\'20\'19 |\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has described the \uc2 Israel Defense Force\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fatal shooting of the Turkish American protester Aysenur Ezgi Eygi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/11/biden-aysenur-ezgi-eygi-killed-idf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war |\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US government\uc2  has given its strongest hint yet that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/11/blinken-hints-us-will-lift-restrictions-on-ukraine-using-long-range-arms-in-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will lift its restrictions on Ukraine }}}\uc2  using long-range weapons supplied by the west on key military targets inside Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Medical emergency |\par \par \uc2 Doctors\u8217\'20\'19 and nurses\u8217\'20\'19 unions in Italy have called for authorities to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/11/call-for-army-to-protect-italian-hospital-staff-after-spate-of-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 consider bringing the army into hospitals}}}\uc2  in response to an increase in attacks by patients and their relatives.\par \par \uc2 Full Story\par \par \uc2 Elle Macpherson, misinformation and making sense of the wellness industry\par \par \uc2 Our medical editor, Melissa Davey, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2024/sep/11/elle-macpherson-misinformation-and-making-sense-of-the-wellness-industry-full-story-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaks to Nour Haydar }}}\uc2  about the controversy over Elle Macpherson\u8217\'20\'19s cancer treatment and how to make sense of the claims and products pushed by the wellness industry.\par \par \uc2 In-depth\par \par \uc2 John Edwards (pictured inset), who murdered his two children in 2018, had a long history of family violence. He also had a habit of using private investigators \u8211\'20\'13 an under-scrutinised industry with few obligations to screen clients for AVOs or family violence risks. A number of firms are even selling spyware specifically marketed to catch \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating spouses\u8221\'20\'1D, and a report from the \uc2 NSW Crime Commission\uc2  found some may be \u8220\'20\'1Cwilfully blind to their client\u8217\'20\'19s criminal involvement and intentions\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/article/2024/sep/12/why-was-child-killer-john-edwards-who-had-a-violent-history-able-to-hire-a-pi-to-spy-on-his-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ariel Bogle takes a look at the risks}}}\uc2 , and why there are calls for regulation of the industry to change.\par \par \uc2 Not the news\par \par \uc2 We spend roughly a third of our lives sleeping and yet a lot of us still don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to do it right, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/wellness/article/2024/sep/11/top-10-sleep-mistakes-experts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Madeleine Aggeler}}}\uc2 . She offers 10 tips on how to get a better night\u8217\'20\'19s shuteye, including not eating or working in bed, winding down properly with a book or such before hitting the hay, and trying not to worry too much about not being able to sleep.\par \par \uc2 The world of sport\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Cricket |\par \par \uc2 Travis Head top scored with 59 as Australia set England 180 to win the first T20 in Southampton this morning. In reply the hosts got into trouble early. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2024/sep/11/england-v-australia-first-mens-t20-cricket-international-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Check out the score at our live blog}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Football |\par \par \uc2 Graham Arnold says the draw against Indonesia was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a disaster\u8221\'20\'1D but failing to beat either them or Bahrain leaves the Socceroos boss \u8211\'20\'13 and the wider Australian game \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/blog/article/2024/sep/12/australia-socceroos-world-cup-qualifier-qualifying-vs-indonesia-bahrain-graham-arnold-malaise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with a lot of thinking to do}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Paris Olympics |\par \par \uc2 The Australian hockey player Tom Craig {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/sep/11/australian-hockey-player-tom-craig-banned-12-months-for-buying-cocaine-at-olympics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been banned for 12 months}}}\uc2 , with six months suspended, after he was arrested in Paris for buying cocaine during the Games.\par \par \uc2 Media roundup\par \par \uc2 The Herald Sun reports on what it calls the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heraldsun.com.au/truecrimeaustralia/police-courts-victoria/amid-the-flames-and-plumes-of-smoke-police-horses-were-forced-to-tread-carefully-through-the-burning-debris-towards-protesters/news-story/1d4607815cb431addd7afc6b8730222d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmoment Melbourne CBD became like a war zone\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  when anti-war protesters clashed with police. Labor faces a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newcastleherald.com.au/story/8753730/newcastles-2024-council-election-labor-faces-challengers/?cs=305"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong challenge from independents}}}\uc2  as it tries to hang on to power in Newcastle, the Herald reports. Work has started on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.couriermail.com.au/lifestyle/brisbane-airport-5bn-upgrade-to-transform-international-terminal/news-story/68415f0cd16f9c51890805632d507a6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive\u8221\'20\'1D changes to transform Brisbane airport}}}\uc2 , the Courier Mail says, offering a \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst look\u8221\'20\'1D at what it might look like.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening today\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Canberra |\par \par \uc2 Trade minister Don Farrell to address the China Business Council.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Western Australia |\par \par \uc2 Trial in Broome for man accused of assaulting three Indigenous children with cable ties.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arts |\par \par \uc2 The winners of the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s literary awards will be announced at the \uc2 National Library of Australia\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive this Morning Mail update to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/23/morning-mail-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up-inbox-subscribe?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 , or finish your day with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/oct/13/afternoon-update-newsletter-best-daily-news-email-guardian-australia-free-sign-up?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our Afternoon Update newsletter}}}\uc2 . And check out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the full list of our local and international newsletters}}}\uc2 , including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/25/election-newsletter-sign-up-stakes?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Stakes}}}\uc2 , your guide to the twists and turns of the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Prefer notifications? If you\u8217\'20\'19re reading this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/ng-interactive/2018/may/15/the-guardian-app?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in our app}}}\uc2 , just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/guardian-australia-s-morning-mail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 click here and tap \u8220\'20\'1CNotifications\u8221\'20\'1D on the next screen}}}\uc2  for an instant alert when we publish every morning.\par \par \uc2 Brain teaser\par \par \uc2 And finally, here are the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crosswords to keep you entertained throughout the day. Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16958"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2