\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  accused of retaliating against staff union effort\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 877 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2024\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UAW Staff United says they have been \u8216\'20\'18shut down\u8217\'20\'19 for requesting same worker protections the union champions\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , one of biggest trade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unions}}}\uc2  in the US, has been accused of firing an organizer in retaliation for their role in an internal union, and delaying bargaining over a contract.\par \par \uc2 Staff workers formed the UAW Staff United union last March. It covers \uc2 UAW\uc2  employees at 34 locals across New York City, Connecticut, Massachusetts, Rhode Island, New Hampshire, Vermont, Maine and Puerto Rico.\par \par \uc2 A series of high-profile campaigns, including a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike at big three automakers}}}\uc2  Ford, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and \uc2 General Motors\uc2  in 2023, and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/19/volkswagen-unionize-uaw-tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic election victory}}}\uc2  at a \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant in Chattanooga, Tennessee, earlier this year, have driven the \uc2 UAW\uc2  into the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, president of \uc2 UAW\uc2 , was elected in 2023 as a reform candidate in the wake of a corruption scandal involving some high-level union officials.\par \par \uc2 But inside the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , staff who formed an internal union in the wake of Fain\u8217\'20\'19s election claim they have been \u8220\'20\'1Cshot down\u8221\'20\'1D when requesting the same protections it campaigns for on behalf of members.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, UAW Staff United accused the \uc2 UAW\uc2  of being \u8220\'20\'1Cinflexible\u8221\'20\'1D on \u8220\'20\'1Ccore\u8221\'20\'1D issues. \u8220\'20\'1CTheir bargaining tactics have delayed negotiations for over a year,\u8221\'20\'1D it said. UAW Staff United has filed unfair labor practice charges against the \uc2 UAW\uc2  for retaliation, bad-faith bargaining and withholding of information.\par \par \uc2 UAW Staff United added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe unjust termination of Alex Chan highlights a deeper problem: \uc2 UAW\uc2  leadership is employing the same bad-faith tactics used by the big three automakers and bosses around the region, offering their own staff working conditions they would never accept for their members.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alex Chan, a temporary organizer with UAW Region 9A, was recently told by email that their contract would not be renewed. They believe they are the first organizer to not be renewed before the end of their three-year term. UAW Staff United is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/UAWStaffUnited/status/1830961748695781615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  for Chan\u8217\'20\'19s reinstatement and will be picketing outside the UAW Region 9A political leadership conference in New York City on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe actually know that non-renewal is a tool that has been used to retaliate against us before, and it is consistent with what we know practices around temps are,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chan. \u8220\'20\'1COf course, it hurts me as an individual, I have to have health insurance. This is my livelihood. This is my full-time job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut what is going to be even more apparent in the near future is the effect it has on the campaigns that I\u8217\'20\'19m working on, which are at different stages, but one of which has an election in three weeks, and I\u8217\'20\'19m the only staffer that is working on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chan said bargaining between the \uc2 UAW\uc2  and UAW Staff United has been going on since August last year, after the union won recognition, and that they began their role in June last year supporting \uc2 UAW\uc2  members at \uc2 New York University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Temporary organizers are hired under a three-year contract cap and renewed every three months, a structure Chan said is a holdover from the auto industry, but puts organizers in a position where they lack job security.\par \par \uc2 According to Chan and the union, bargaining with \uc2 UAW\uc2  for more than a year has been slow, with bargaining sessions far apart, and only minor tentative agreements reached on some issues, with outstanding issues including economics, job security, and grievance processes. Some 170 rank and file \uc2 UAW\uc2  members signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/u/1/d/e/2PACX-1vQdE8QW6a_h3aX0ynj4WfxrSdJIQ5BCxEkYOAeXcP2dIkWbkrClT0go1sOWt1NdX8OSVmNl6Zd12RmR/pub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  supporting the staff unions\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to secure a first contract, and expressing disappointment in how staff have been treated in negotiations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor example, with pay, I believe we are stuck somewhere at 3% raises over each year for four years, which is quite laughable if you compare it to any of the contracts that we fight for,\u8221\'20\'1D added Chan. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s kind of the bottom line, where we wanted to be clear that, whatever values \uc2 UAW\uc2  espouses for the members that it fights for \u8230\'20\'26 We should also be treated the same.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers at several unions have faced retaliation and opposition from organizing and contract efforts by their labor union leadership. After employees at the \uc2 National Education Association\uc2 , the largest teachers union in the US, went on a three-day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.neasomatters.org/nations-largest-union-retaliates-against-staff-union-with-lockout-for-ulp-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  in July, the union locked out the workers before reaching an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.neasomatters.org/nea-and-its-staff-union-neaso-reach-a-tentative-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement }}}\uc2  in August. In May, staffers at SEIU Local 1199 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thechiefleader.com/stories/staffers-accuse-seiu-local-1199-of-union-busting,52434?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the union of firing a staffer in retaliation ahead of a union election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just want the same protections and security that we fight for our members for. And we have said this multiple times in bringing up contract language that our members have, but have been shot down time and time again at the table,\u8221\'20\'1D Chan said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is disappointing and shocking to see some of the same tactics being used against ourselves by a union that\u8217\'20\'19s supposed to be fighting for and protecting labor and workers everywhere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  declined to comment, citing a policy of not commenting on personnel matters. A source at \uc2 UAW\uc2  claimed the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is bargaining in good faith and that the union routines negotiates agreements with multiple unions that represent staffers.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240910ek9a001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
