\par\par \uc2 Environment\par \b \uc2 UPS\uc2  faces backlash from extreme heat incidents: \u8216\'20\'18I got flowers and that was it\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,533 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 September 2024\par 08:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Driver Chris Begley\u8217\'20\'19s death in August underscores a list of alleged heat-related incidents across Texas\par \par \uc2 Neysa Lambeth was in Florida caring for her ailing father on 23 August 2023 when she received a call from her husband, Chris Begley, who had worked as a \uc2 UPS\uc2  driver for 28 years in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Begley, 57, had collapsed from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/extreme-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heat}}}\uc2  while delivering packages. Lambeth said a manager picked him up and took him home to recover. He had fallen ill a couple of times from the heat over the previous two years, Lambeth said, and she had picked him up from the \uc2 UPS\uc2  service center on those occasions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis time I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t home, and so instead of taking him to the hospital or dialling 911, they took him home to an empty house and left him,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lambeth.\par \par \uc2 When she spoke with her husband on the phone when he arrived home, she noted he was very confused. Over the next few days, she said her husband tried to recover as he had in the past after falling ill from the heat by resting and drinking Gatorade, but he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t able to keep it down. He collapsed in his home a couple of days later and couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get up.\par \par \uc2 Lambeth called her son to pick him up and take him to the hospital. When she arrived at the hospital in Texas, Lambeth said her husband\u8217\'20\'19s doctors weren\u8217\'20\'19t hopeful about his prognosis, Begley\u8217\'20\'19s organs were shutting down. He died on 28 August. Her father, who she had been in Florida to care for when her husband\u8217\'20\'19s heat incident occurred, died a few days after her husband.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was telling him to fight. And he tried, but he just couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lambeth. \u8220\'20\'1CUPS, they never contacted me. I contacted them to let them know he passed. I got flowers and that was it, I never heard from them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lambeth said that in previous media statements, \uc2 UPS\uc2  denied her husband\u8217\'20\'19s death was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/27/us-heat-related-deaths-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heat-related}}}\uc2 , claiming it was a heart issue, but she took offense at that characterization. \uc2 The Occupational Safety and Health Administration\uc2  issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/texas/news/widow-of-ups-driver-who-collapsed-on-the-job-calls-for-better-worker-protections-in-extreme-heat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fine }}}\uc2  against \uc2 UPS\uc2  for $66,000 after an investigation found the company failed to provide Begley with access to medical care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was horrified and disgusted to read that they would put something like that in the media without at least talking to me first,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lambeth. \u8220\'20\'1CFor them to imply his collapse in a triple-digit-degree day while doing his route had nothing to do with his essential heart failure and subsequent death, it really defies common sense and it infuriates me that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t see to the safety and wellbeing of their employee when he collapsed. Even if he did have a heart condition, of course I had no knowledge of, if they took him to the hospital that day, would they have been able to find it and correct it in time to save his life, I will never know because they didn\u8217\'20\'19t do the right thing for him in my opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesperson said in response to Begley\u8217\'20\'19s death: \u8220\'20\'1CChris was a valued member of the \uc2 UPS\uc2  family who dedicated 28 years of service to our company, and we continue to extend our heartfelt condolences to the Begley family. We fully cooperated with authorities on the investigation following his death in August 2023. The claim that Chris died of heat stress is inconsistent with the autopsy report. The autopsy did not cite heat as Chris\u8217\'20\'19s cause of death. His last day of work was several days before he became hospitalized and died.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lambeth began speaking out after recent incidents at \uc2 UPS\uc2  in Texas that are also alleged to have been heat-related. Heat is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tpr.org/news/2024-08-16/texas-likely-undercounting-heat-related-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seldom }}}\uc2  considered in autopsy reports, leading to likely undercounts of heat-related deaths across the US.\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 UPS\uc2  represented by the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  demanded and won improvements for workers exposed to extreme heat in their union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/jul/23/ups-drivers-extreme-heat-contract-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contract}}}\uc2  with \uc2 UPS\uc2  settled in July 2023, winning language that aimed to include air conditioning in vehicles purchased after 1 January 2024 and to include cooling devices in 28,000 UPS package delivery vehicles by the end of the contract in 2028.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 UPS\uc2  workers are still facing heat-related incidents and pushing on \uc2 UPS\uc2  to implement the changes, with the Teamsters International {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/article/2024/aug/23/ups-delivery-workers-air-conditioning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleging}}}\uc2  the company has made little progress in living up to the contract on heat protections.\par \par \uc2 On 6 August, 37-year-old Luis Grimaldo, a \uc2 UPS\uc2  driver for four years in Bell county, Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcentv.com/article/news/local/bell-county/ups-delivery-driver-dies-central-texas/500-ec4345b2-64a1-4746-8c99-3a87b5eecc74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died}}}\uc2 , with co-workers alleging his death was heat-related, which \uc2 UPS\uc2  has denied.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesperson said Grimaldo\u8217\'20\'19s death is still under investigation, but added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are saddened by the loss of our delivery driver Luis Grimaldo and extend our heartfelt condolences to his family and friends. We continue to work with authorities as they investigate the cause of death. Luis was only two hours into his work week, and at this time, we have no indication his death is related to heat stress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A day later on 16 August, a \uc2 UPS\uc2  driver in McKinney, Texas, the same site where Chris Begley worked, passed out from the heat while driving a \uc2 UPS\uc2  package vehicle and crashed. Teamsters Local 767 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2024/08/20/ups-driver-passed-out-texas-crash-heat-exhaustion-teamsters/74869224007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged}}}\uc2  the driver called in to \uc2 UPS\uc2  to report experiencing heat illness symptoms but asked the driver to drive himself back to the \uc2 UPS\uc2  site. The union has claimed no air conditioning is available in any of the more than 2,000 vehicles at the site yet and the union held a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tEmm3ojqYPU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest}}}\uc2  last week to demand them.\par \par \uc2 Teamsters Local 657, which represents 22 \uc2 UPS\uc2  sites in Texas, also held rallies to demand air conditioning in vehicles in the wake of the incidents.\par \par \uc2 Teamsters Local 886 in Oklahoma also held a rally on 30 August outside \uc2 UPS\uc2  sites to demand the company take immediate action to protect workers from heat, in solidarity with locals in Texas. \u8220\'20\'1CUPS Teamsters across the country, including our union siblings in Texas Teamsters Local 767, are facing unbearable and dangerous heat conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Zakk Flash Luttrell, a representative of Teamsters Local 886, in a press release. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are united in our demand that \uc2 UPS\uc2  take immediate action to honor the contract and protect our members\u8217\'20\'19 lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 TEXAS TEAMSTERS DEMAND UPS DELIVER AIR-CONDITIONED TRUCKS NOW\par \par \uc2 Members of Teamsters Local 657 rallied today in Texas to demand the company move faster on the union contract it signed with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  last year and start delivering tens of thousands of air-conditioned package\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5ctErKaJhO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5ctErKaJhO}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  (@Teamsters) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Teamsters/status/1828923138085634375?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are aware of an incident involving our driver in McKinney, TX. We care deeply about his safety and wellbeing. We can confirm the driver received minor medical treatment and went home. We continue to work with authorities to investigate and defer to them for questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat it appears to me, all I could think was \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s happening again.\u8217\'20\'19 I literally just sat on the couch all day and cried because I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t believe all this was occurring again. After having a death last summer, how could they not make changes?\u8221\'20\'1D said Lambeth.\par \par \uc2 She emphasized that she wants \uc2 UPS\uc2  to improve heat protections and safety for workers to prevent these cases from continuing to happen and to expedite rolling out air conditioning to vehicles, especially in southern states where workers experience more intense heat days.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 UPS\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe health and safety of our team members is important to us, and we are committed to providing a safe working environment for our employees. We have comprehensive training and protocols to support our employees and continuously work to improve these measures. We invest more than $409m annually on safety training in the US and have added more cooling equipment to our vehicles and facilities. We provide employees with specialized cooling gear, access to ice and water, and encourage our people to take extra time to cool down anytime they need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson added the company had provided 96,000 water jugs to drivers, installed an additional 1,500 ice machines and 1,700 water fountains in our facilities, and nearly 14,000 additional fans. They said \uc2 UPS\uc2  currently had \u8220\'20\'1Chundreds\u8221\'20\'1D of vehicles on the road in the US with air conditioning. \uc2 UPS\uc2  has about 100,000 package delivery {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fleetequipmentmag.com/fleet-profile-ups-shares-results-of-strong-investment-in-alternative-fuel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vehicles}}}\uc2  on the road in the US.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson also said \uc2 UPS\uc2  has installed over 200,000 fans in package vehicles, installed 76,000 heat shields and equipped over 74,000 vehicles with air scoop induction technology.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I want Chris\u8217\'20\'19s legacy to be is safety,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lambeth. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are not doing the right thing for their employees. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem like they have a policy or procedure in place to handle these situations and that\u8217\'20\'19s not fair to their employees. In my opinion, they are putting their employees\u8217\'20\'19 lives in jeopardy by not having any safety protocols in place for this situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240907ek970015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
