\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Union dispute shuts down Canadian freight rail amid fears for US trade\b0\par\par\uc2 Leyland Cecco in Toronto \par \uc2 802 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2024\par 11:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Nearly 10,000 workers locked out at Canada\u8217\'20\'19s two major rail freight firms in dispute over working conditions\par \par \uc2 Both of Canada\u8217\'20\'19s major rail freight companies have shut down their rail networks in the country and locked out nearly 10,000 workers after unsuccessful negotiations with a major union.\par \par \uc2 The decision, confirmed by the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 , sets the stage for an unprecedented rail stoppage that could badly damage the Canadian economy and have a significant effect on cross-border trade with the US.\par \par \uc2 Canada is the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest country by area and relies heavily on rail transport. The stoppage is expected to cripple shipments of grain, potash and coal while also slowing the transport of petroleum products, chemicals and vehicles.\par \par \uc2 Industry groups had urged \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Liberal government to prevent a stoppage, noting Canada\u8217\'20\'19s railways transport about C$380bn (\u163\'00\'A3214bn) worth of goods annually.\par \par \uc2 Canadian National Rail (CN) and Canadian Pacific Kansas City (CPKC) began lockouts on Thursday morning after tense negotiations following complaints from workers over worsening job conditions failed to produce a deal.\par \par \uc2 CN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CNRailway/status/1826473154543247599"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2  it had moved ahead with the lockout, saying the union \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not respond to another offer by CN in a final attempt to avoid a labour disruption\u8221\'20\'1D. It said: \u8220\'20\'1CWithout an agreement or binding arbitration, CN had no choice but to finalise a safe and orderly shutdown and proceed with a lockout.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union said: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite months of good faith negotiations on the part of the Teamsters Canada Rail Conference, parties remain far apart, and both CN and CPKC have began their lockout of 00:01 today \u8230\'20\'26 Despite the lockout, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  remain at the bargaining table with both companies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In its announcement, CPKC said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe TCRC [union] leadership continues to make unrealistic demands that would fundamentally impair the railway\u8217\'20\'19s ability to serve our customers with a reliable and cost-competitive transportation service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A pause to freight traffic will have cascading effects on Canada and the US. According to the \uc2 Railway Association of Canada\uc2 , affected rail carries more than C$1bn worth of goods each day. Nearly half the aviation fuel used at Toronto\u8217\'20\'19s Pearson airport, Canada\u8217\'20\'19s busiest air terminal, arrives by rail. More than 32,000 commuters in Montreal, Vancouver and Toronto rely on the rail network. A strike would also hit the mining, agriculture and retail industries.\par \par \uc2 The federal labour minister, Steven MacKinnon, said on Wednesday night that he had completed meetings with the companies and the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 . He called for urgency at the negotiating table and for a deal to be done.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the Calgary-based CPKC and Montreal-based CN had started winding down operations. In Canada, both companies, valued at roughly C$100bn each, own virtually all of the rail track in the country and control most of the freight shipment. The country has never experienced a labour stoppage involving both companies simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 As the possibility of a strike loomed, industry groups issued a joint statement calling on the government to intervene, saying it \u8220\'20\'1Chas a responsibility to protect the Canadian public and maintain national security, and it is time to act decisively to fulfil that obligation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 MacKinnon last week declined a request from CN and CPKC to move negotiations to binding arbitration. \u8220\'20\'1CThese collective bargaining negotiations belong to \uc2 CN Rail\uc2 , CPKC and [\uc2 Teamsters\uc2 ] workers alone \u8211\'20\'13 but their effects will be borne by all Canadians,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trudeau said the country\u8217\'20\'19s two main rail companies and the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2  had to settle their differences at the negotiating table, but stopped short of suggesting his government might get involved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy message is very straightforward. It is in the best interest of both sides to continue doing the hard work at the table to find a negotiated resolution,\u8221\'20\'1D the prime minister said. \u8220\'20\'1CMillions of Canadians, of workers, of farmers, of businesses right across the country are counting on both sides to do the work and get to a resolution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The deputy prime minister, \uc2 Chrystia Freeland\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that the best deals are reached at the bargaining table, and I am calling with extreme seriousness on the employers and on the union to roll up their sleeves to get a deal done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union representing workers at CPKC said the company wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cgut the collective agreement of all safety-critical fatigue provisions\u8221\'20\'1D while those with CN said the rail operator wanted work days to be extended in western provinces, potentially creating \u8220\'20\'1Ca fatigue-related safety risk\u8221\'20\'1D. The unions have cited fatigue management, rest periods and scheduling as key sticking points.\par \par \uc2 Both companies said offers on the table were competitive and did not compromise safety.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240905ek95002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
