\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Biden pitch for steel votes in Pittsburgh in first joint appearance on campaign trail\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi \par \uc2 985 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2024\par 14:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  join forces in Labor Day outing, their first joint event since Harris accepted Democratic nomination for presidency\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  on Monday made their first post-convention joint appearance on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential campaign}}}\uc2  trail, celebrating Labor Day with a tribute to union workers in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are so proud to be the most pro-union administration in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI love Labor Day. I love celebrating Labor Day, and Pittsburgh is the cradle of the American labor movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Between comments about the administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for organized labor and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/uaw-union-charge-trump-elon-musk-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on labor organizing}}}\uc2 , Harris, the vice-president, spoke against the pending purchase of \uc2 US Steel\uc2  by \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , arguing that the iconic Pennsylvania steel company should remain in the hands of American owners.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 US Steel\uc2  is an historic American company and it is vital for our nation to maintain strong American steel companies. And I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t agree more with President Biden: \uc2 US Steel\uc2  should remain American-owned and American-operated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union, representing about 10,000 \uc2 US Steel\uc2  employees, opposes the $14.9bn deal, taking issue with \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s alleged violations of the union\u8217\'20\'19s rights concerning change of control under their four-year basic labor agreement signed in 2022. The union and the companies are in arbitration talks.\par \par \uc2 Harris again voiced support for the Protecting the Right to Organize (PRO) Act, a broad basket of labor reforms that would spur union organizing.\par \par \uc2 Kenny Cooper, president of the IBEW union, introduced Biden and Harris, noting that the passage of the Butch Lewis Act by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s tie-breaking vote saved the benefits of 2 million union members. \u8220\'20\'1CThey were only tied up for one reason,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe couldn\u8217\'20\'19t find a Republican senator.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris also cast the tie-breaking vote for the Inflation Reduction Act, which the USW International president, \uc2 David McCall\uc2 , said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usw.org/blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments}}}\uc2  had been \u8220\'20\'1Crevolutionizing the cement, chemical, glass and steel sectors along with other traditional core industries\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Republican presidential nominee, also opposes the \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  deal and has said he will block it if president. Biden announced his opposition to the \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  deal in March.\par \par \uc2 Less crisply perhaps than Harris, Biden described the accomplishments of his administration in Pennsylvania, from investments in clean energy to infrastructure money. He noted that his administration required project labor agreements that respected labor rights and required American products, while reminding listeners that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed union busting officials to the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWall Street didn\u8217\'20\'19t build America,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe middle class built America and unions built the middle class.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The appearance of Biden and Harris together provides an image of how the two may campaign in the waning days of the election. Biden described Harris as having \u8220\'20\'1Cthe backbone of a ramrod and the moral compass of a saint\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris spent the morning in Detroit, hailing the virtues of union organizing \u8211\'20\'13 the five-day work week, sick leave, vacation time and other benefits \u8211\'20\'13 with labor leaders at Northwestern High School.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe celebrate unions because unions helped build America, and unions helped build America\u8217\'20\'19s middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen union wages go up, everybody\u8217\'20\'19s wages go up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden is the first sitting president to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk a union picket line}}}\uc2 , supporting the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  in their dispute with major car manufacturers in September 2023. \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 UAW\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 you saved the automobile industry back in 2008 and before,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden shouted through a bullhorn on the picket line in Michigan. \u8220\'20\'1CYou made a lot of sacrifices, gave up a lot. The companies were in trouble. Now they are doing incredibly well and guess what? You should be doing incredibly well too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shawn Fain, president of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , has been both a strident voice reinvigorating the American labor movement and a strident opponent of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is all talk, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  walks the walk,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said at the Democratic national convention in August, while wearing a shirt that said \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is a scab\u8221\'20\'1D. Harris supporters chanted that phrase in Detroit this morning.\par \par \uc2 Though Trump called in his acceptance speech before the Republican national convention for Fain to be \u8220\'20\'1Cfired immediately\u8221\'20\'1D, the Republican nominee has made overtures to labor voters during his run to return to office. The renegotiation of the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2  and his proposed tariffs of 10-20% on foreign trade have been central to his outreach, arguing that this will bring manufacturing back from offshore plants.\par \par \uc2 But Project 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 a conservative playbook for a second Trump administration penned by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 aims to end merit-based employment for thousands of unionized federal workers; calls for changes to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotected concerted activity\u8221\'20\'1D, which would allow employers to retaliate more easily against union organizing; and eliminate the \u8220\'20\'1Cpersuader rule\u8221\'20\'1D requiring company disclosures when hiring union-busting consultants.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also flip-flopped in public comments about the electric car industry, initially calling for an end to electric car mandates but recently walking that rhetoric back after the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/19/elon-musk-trump-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  his candidacy. During an interview on Musk\u8217\'20\'19s X/\uc2 Twitter\uc2  social media space, Trump gushed at Musk\u8217\'20\'19s approach to labor relations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey go on strike,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CI won\u8217\'20\'19t mention the name of the company, but they go on strike and you say, \u8216\'20\'18That\u8217\'20\'19s OK. You\u8217\'20\'19re all gone. You\u8217\'20\'19re all gone. So every one of you is gone,\u8217\'20\'19 and you are the greatest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That prompted the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien \u8211\'20\'13 who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/teamsters-union-president-sean-obrien-rnc-trump-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  at the Republican convention {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/17/teamsters-sean-obrien-rnc-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to the surprise}}}\uc2  of many labor leaders \u8211\'20\'13 to walk his own overtures towards Trump back. \u8220\'20\'1CFiring workers for organizing, striking and exercising their rights as Americans is economic terrorism,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240903ek9200003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
