\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 London workers slower to return to office than New York or Paris, study says\b0\par\par\uc2 Julia Kollewe \par \uc2 687 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 September 2024\par 13:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Office attendance in UK capital similar to levels in Toronto and Sydney, thinktank findsBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Workers in London have been slower to return to the office than those in other global cities such as Paris and New York, a report has found.\par \par \uc2 London was near the bottom of the pack, with office attendance similar to levels in Toronto and Sydney, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.centreforcities.org/publication/return-to-the-office/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research by the Centre for Cities thinktank}}}\uc2 , which surveyed employees and employers in six big cities.\par \par \uc2 Workers in central London spend 2.7 days a week in the office on average, up from 2.2 days a week last year, the poll found. That was less than workers in Paris, who come in 3.5 days a week, while those in Singapore attend 3.2 days a week and workers in New York\u8217\'20\'19s central business district spend 3.1 days in the office.\par \par \uc2 London\u8217\'20\'19s results were similar to Toronto, where the average office attendance is 2.7 days a week, and Sydney, where the figure was 2.8 days a week.\par \par \uc2 On Fridays, London\u8217\'20\'19s offices are the emptiest of all the cities. It is also the only city where younger workers come in to the office more often than their senior colleagues, the report found. People in their 20s are in the office three days a week, on average, while those over 35 go in for two-and-a-half days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn London, a quarter of workers come into the office just one or two days \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the most of any city,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rob Johnson, an analyst at the thinktank and the author of the report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo you\u8217\'20\'19ve got quite a lot of workers who are quite tenuously linked to their offices. London\u8217\'20\'19s offices on a Friday are the emptiest of all the cities and we see the sharpest drop from the midweek average. And London\u8217\'20\'19s midweek average is relatively low.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Travel costs are more of a barrier to office working in London than in any other city, the report said. It recommended that \uc2 Transport for London\uc2  should resume and extend its off-peak Fridays policy to reduce travel costs.\par \par \uc2 In March, the capital\u8217\'20\'19s transport authority launched a three-month trial of off-peak fares all day on Fridays on its network, including the underground, the \uc2 Docklands Light Railway\uc2 , the overground, the Elizabeth line and some National Rail services across London and the south-east.\par \par \uc2 Workers\u8217\'20\'19 attitudes suggest very few simply do not like being in the office, and companies with budgets for \u8220\'20\'1Cperks\u8221\'20\'1D or office revamps to entice workers back might find their money better spent on subsidising commutes instead, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Centre for Cities suggested that business leaders should lead by example. \u8220\'20\'1CMore senior staff coming into the office could improve decision-making, productivity and the development of younger colleagues,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 The thinktank called on the government and the mayor of London to continue to work with companies in the centre of the capital and business groups to set higher expectations of days in the office, through a campaign similar to the \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s Do London\u8221\'20\'1D that was launched to revive tourism after pandemic lockdowns eased.\par \par \uc2 Fewer than one in 10 London workers would look for a new job if attendance mandates rose, the survey found.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLondon\u8217\'20\'19s most popular number of mandated days has shifted from two to three days over the past year, and almost all employers in the London city centre have some sort of mandate,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut in the international context, London has the lowest mandates of all cities looked at.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Separate research in June commissioned by \uc2 International Workplace Group\uc2  found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/jun/16/hybrid-working-makes-employees-happier-healthier-and-more-productive-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hybrid working made employees happier, healthier and more productive}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nick Bloom, a professor at \uc2 Stanford University\uc2 , who has looked at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://siepr.stanford.edu/publications/policy-brief/hybrid-future-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hybrid working}}}\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe pandemic has started a revolution in how we work, and our research shows working from home can make firms more productive and employees happier. But like all revolutions, this is difficult to navigate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240903ek930015t\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row 